window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4701,"title":"Chapter 4701: News","paragraphs":["The Azure Emperor demonstrated the water manipulation technique once to Yue’er, then instructed her to study the accompanying book on her own. With that, he left her by the cascading waterfall to practice and went to check on the progress of his other two disciples.","Time flowed serenely in the mountains, especially when one was immersed in the focused discipline of cultivation. The three children dedicated themselves to their training, gradually acclimating to their new life amidst the tranquil peaks.","A year later, the early morning air was shattered by a deafening roar.","\"Boom!\"","In the vast realm governed by Xuanyuan Mo Ze, a formidable bolt of lightning tribulation erupted, its thunderous sound echoing through the nine heavens. The celestial phenomenon spread across the sky, causing tremors that rippled through the very fabric of the four cardinal directions.","\"What’s going on? What in the heavens happened?\" In another distant realm, several powerful monarchs were engaged in a serious discussion when the sudden, earth-shattering sound of lightning reverberated through their domain. They couldn’t help but rise from their seats, their faces etched with surprise and concern, and step outside to investigate.","\"Let us see,\" one of the Monarchs declared, his voice filled with authority. He closed his eyes, focusing his considerable divine sense to probe the source of the disturbance. After a moment of intense concentration, he opened his eyes, his expression slightly altered. \"It is the Ghost Doctor causing such a commotion. He must have successfully completed some kind of extraordinary heavenly medicinal pill. That is the telltale sound of pill tribulation.\"","No sooner had he spoken than another deafening clap of lightning echoed across the heavens, reaching their ears with undiminished intensity.","\"Is it the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu?\" The group of monarchs exchanged startled glances, their attention fixed on the echoing sounds emanating from the sky outside. One of them mused aloud, \"Hasn’t the Ghost Doctor been uncharacteristically quiet for quite some time now? I heard rumors that she had entered a period of seclusion. Why would she be refining medicinal pills again?\"","Another monarch offered a somber observation. \"The Green Dragon Lord Xuanyuan Mo Ze failed his ascension tribulation that fateful day, and it was said that his very soul was struck by lightning and scattered between the realms. Now, only a faint trace of his spiritual consciousness remains within the realm he governs, and a full year has passed without any sign of improvement. I fear it is truly dire news.\"","\"Rather than dwelling on whether his situation is truly hopeless,\" one of the monarchs interjected, a keen glint in his eyes, \"I am far more intrigued by what kind of medicinal pill the ghost doctor has concocted this time that could attract such a potent lightning tribulation. Her strength has already reached the Supreme level. If she successfully breaks through to the next stage and directly ascends to become an immortal, she will truly attain a lifespan as long as heaven and earth. Upon ascending, she will undoubtedly become a formidable figure in the Upper Immortal Realm, potentially ruling over the various realms and becoming the supreme sovereign of the world.\"","At this point, the monarch’s eyes flickered with an enigmatic light as he added, \"Do you all still recall those cryptic few words about the Phoenix Star?\"","The other monarchs were taken aback, exchanging puzzled glances. One of them finally responded, \"We remember them, but we still do not fully comprehend the meaning of ’breaking through the heavens and skies Furthermore, if she does ascend to immortality and achieve a lifespan as long as heaven and earth, won’t there still be powerful beings above her in the Upper Immortal Realm? If she truly goes up there, where will she ultimately belong? With those powerful entities already established in the Upper Immortal Realm, how could she possibly surpass them and become the supreme being of the world?\"","\"Hehe, you simply do not know!\" Another monarch chuckled softly, a hint of knowing anticipation flashing in his eyes. \"I have heard whispers that the Green Dragon Lord Xuanyuan Mo Ze failed his ascension tribulation this time not due to his own shortcomings, but because someone from the Upper Immortal Realm deliberately interfered, amplifying the power of the lightning tribulation with the intention of killing him. There are those above who do not wish for their ascension.\" As he spoke these words, the lord subtly pointed towards the heavens.","Upon hearing this startling revelation, the other monarchs fell into a moment of stunned silence. In truth, despite their lofty status as rulers of vast territories, their understanding of the intricate affairs of the Upper Immortal Realm remained largely superficial.","Generally speaking, the Upper Immortal Realm was comprised of members of ancient families that had been scattered across the cosmos for millennia. Those who truly attained immense power were exceedingly rare. Rulers such as themselves, capable of governing entire regions and wielding authority akin to emperors in the mortal world, were relatively common in comparison."]},{"number":4702,"title":"Chapter 4702: Guesses","paragraphs":["For many, the dream of ascending to the Upper Immortal Realm is a powerful one, driven by the desire for extended life, perhaps even to live as long as the heavens and earth themselves.","However, this aspiration is often tempered by a harsh reality: once they reach this elevated plane, individuals without the backing of a powerful family face significant challenges. They are often relegated to joining a major sect as a mere disciple or attaching themselves to a powerful figure, becoming a subordinate with limited autonomy.","This precarious existence means that, without strong support, their lives in the Upper Immortal Realm are easily extinguished. It is this grim prospect that often deters even the most ambitious, forcing them to suppress their longing for ascension.","In stark contrast, those born in the Upper Immortal Realm begin their lives with an inherent advantage. They start from a higher point, often inheriting status and influence rather than earning it. While they may not possess formidable individual strength, their family’s power is often enough to allow them to navigate their world with arrogance and impunity. For rulers from other realms, even those who wield immense power in their own domains, the situation is different. When confronted by a thousand-year-old clan in the Upper Immortal Realm, they often find themselves in a position where endurance, rather than direct confrontation, is their only viable option, regardless of their personal might.","\"Alas, I truly hope that the Ghost Doctor can become the supreme ruler of the world,\" one monarch sighed, looking up at the sky with his arms folded behind his back. \"That would indeed be a good thing for all of us.\" He continued, his voice tinged with concern, \"Given that there are powerful entities in the Upper Immortal Realm who wish to prevent Feng Jiu’s ascension, her journey will likely be fraught with extreme danger. Should anything go awry, she might suffer a fate similar to Xuanyuan Mo Ze.\"","Just as their conversation reached this point, the resounding crash of the third bolt of lightning tribulation echoed, swiftly followed by an eerie silence. The air, charged with anticipation moments before, now hung still.","\"Considering the Ghost Doctor’s vengeful nature,\" another monarch interjected, a glimmer of anticipation in his eyes, \"those above had better pray that she fails to ascend. Because if she makes it up there, she will undoubtedly unleash chaos in the Immortal Realm. It’s difficult to predict whether those powerful figures will be able to cling to their positions once she arrives!\" His words carried a mixture of warning and almost gleeful expectation, highlighting the potential disruption Feng Jiu could bring.","Meanwhile, in a completely different world, Feng Jiu emerged from an alchemy room. She had clearly spent a considerable amount of time within, as her clothes were covered in medicinal residue, giving her a somewhat dishevelled appearance. Yet, despite her untidy state, her eyes remained remarkably clear, their light captivating and sharp.","\"Congratulations, Master, on the completion of the divine medicinal pill !\" Leng Hua, Du Fan, and the others, who had been patiently waiting outside the courtyard, rushed forward to offer their felicitations. Their faces were alight with unbridled joy. Their master had been preparing for this momentous task since emerging from seclusion three months prior. The preparation of the intricate medicinal herbs alone had consumed two months, and the refinement of this particular batch of pills had taken a full month of dedicated effort.","\"Is there any news about what I asked you to investigate?\" Feng Jiu inquired, her gaze falling upon Du Fan and the others, her voice betraying a hint of urgency.","\"Yes, Master, we already have some crucial clues,\" Du Fan responded promptly. \"We were waiting for you to come out to report. However, a few days ago, Luo Yu and Gu Mo went to confirm the information. They will send word back as soon as they have definitive news.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu’s expression subtly shifted, a flicker of something unread able passing through her clear eyes. She nodded and instructed, \"Come to the study and tell me everything in detail.\"","\"Yes,\" Du Fan affirmed, ready to follow her command.","\"Master, I have already ordered someone to prepare a bath for you,\" Leng Shuang interjected, her voice gentle and considerate. \"Please return to your room and bathe first!\"","\"Mm,\" Feng Jiu replied, a soft acknowledgment, and then turned, making her way towards the main courtyard.","After a refreshing bath and changing into a clean set of clothes, Feng Jiu consumed a light meal before heading directly to the study.","\"Master,\" Du Fan greeted her, bowing respectfully as she entered, then followed her into the quiet room.","\"How did you find out?\" Feng Jiu asked, settling herself at the desk, her focus immediately shifting to the investigation.","\"It’s in the East Sea Spirit Realm,\" Du Fan began, providing the details. \"Every three months, the sea water there experiences a significant stirring, and during this time, high-ranking spirit beasts can be observed kneeling and howling around the sea area. This unusual commotion has attracted a great deal of attention. When the news reached us, Luo Yu and Gu Mo went to check it out first. The reason is that any place where all beasts collectively kneel must surely be the location of ancient divine beasts. Moreover, the East Sea Spirit Realm is specifically where the Green Dragon is said to go to sea. Based on all these converging clues, we surmised that Hell’s Lord might indeed be there.\""]},{"number":4703,"title":"Chapter 4703: Going Down to Sea","paragraphs":["Du Fan concisely relayed the information he had meticulously gathered, then stood quietly, his gaze fixed on Feng Jiu, awaiting her decision. As Feng Jiu listened, her heart suddenly leaped as she looked at him with surprise.","\"The Eastern Sea Spirit Realm... Why didn’t I think of that?\" she murmured, almost to herself. The realization seemed to jolt her back to full awareness. She immediately rose, a new resolve firming her features. \"I have to go there myself,\" she declared.","Hearing this, Du Fan hesitated for a brief moment. \"Master, perhaps we should wait for Luo Yu and the others to send back confirmed news before we depart?\" he suggested, a touch of caution in his tone. \"After all, this is merely our conjecture, and we haven’t actually verified whether Hell’s Lord is truly there.\"","Feng Jiu, however, shook her head, dismissing his reservations. \"Whether he is or not, I must go there myself,\" she stated unequivocally. \"You go and make the necessary arrangements! We’ll set off momentarily. Let Leng Hua and Leng Shuang accompany us. The others can attend to their respective duties.\"","\"Yes,\" Du Fan replied, understanding that her mind was made up. He didn’t attempt to dissuade her further. Instead, he bowed respectfully and turned to carry out her orders.","Alone for a moment, Feng Jiu’s hand gently caressed a book lying on the table – a book he used to sit there and read often. \"Mo Ze, is that you?\" she whispered, her voice barely audible. \"If it is you, why haven’t you returned? Are you seriously injured? Or is there some other reason?\" Seeing the book now, it was as if he had never left her side, an ever-present memory in the quiet study.","The East Sea Spirit Realm stretched out, a vast and enigmatic expanse of ocean. Its waters, a deep, fathomless blue, remained perpetually calm, with barely a ripple or a whisper of wind throughout most of the year. However, over the past year, cultivators had begun to notice a peculiar and recurring phenomenon.","Once every three months, powerful waves would inexplicably surge in this specific area, and even more astonishingly, the beasts inhabiting the nearby forests would converge upon the shore, kneeling and howling in unison.","This strange occurrence ignited rampant speculation among cultivators. Could it be the manifestation of some rare and powerful treasure within the sea’s depths? Or perhaps the birth of an ancient divine beast, signaling a momentous event in the world? Alternatively, was it merely the appearance of some unique, strange treasure in this realm? Many were deeply intrigued by the mystery. In recent months, large numbers of adventurous souls would strategically avoid the specific day when the beasts performed their strange ritual, instead arriving at the sea to try and salvage any treasures that might have been swept to the ocean floor.","However, the Lingyu Sea was renowned for being both bottomless and treacherous. Even those possessing formidable strength hesitated to venture into its abyssal depths in search of riches. This caution intensified significantly after several daring adventurers, risking their lives in small boats, were tragically swept into the sea’s profound depths, never to be seen or heard from again. Consequently, most people now dared only to observe from a safe distance, unwilling to risk their lives.","It took Luo Yu and Gu Mo more than half a month to reach the Spirit Realm in the East Sea. Upon their arrival at the sprawling seaside, they were met with a surprising sight: numerous groups of cultivators and mercenaries already gathered, creating a bustling, almost festive atmosphere. They couldn’t help but exchange a knowing glance.","\"I heard that this sea area is exceptionally dangerous, but I didn’t expect that so many people would be unafraid of death and come here to join the excitement,\" Luo Yu remarked, raising an eyebrow with a slight smile. He nudged Gu Mo beside him with his elbow and asked, \"What do you think? How should we go down into the water?\"","\"Didn’t we bring water-repellent pearls?\" Gu Mo responded, his gaze scanning the surroundings. \"Let’s enter the sea from over there! There are fewer people in that direction, so we won’t draw unnecessary attention or cause a commotion.\" He subtly motioned for Luo Yu to look towards another part of the beach.","Luo Yu followed his gaze and saw that the indicated section of the beach was partially sheltered by large rocks, indeed with significantly fewer people. If they were to enter the water discreetly, that would undoubtedly be the most advantageous spot. He pondered for a moment, then glanced up at the darkening sky. \"We’re not familiar with this area, and it’s dangerous to go into the sea at night,\" he concluded. \"It’s already late, so let’s wait until tomorrow. Tomorrow, when it’s light, we’ll quietly go into the sea and find out what’s truly going on.\""]},{"number":4704,"title":"Chapter 4704: Heavy","paragraphs":["Gu Mo nodded in agreement, then glanced around the secluded area. \"Let’s go rest over there!\" he suggested.","So, the two walked to a more secluded spot where the beach was entirely deserted. Upon reaching it, they proceeded to set up two tents, preparing to spend the night there.","Just as they were in the midst of pitching their tents, several independent cultivators approached, settling down on the sand nearby. \"Are you two independent cultivators as well?\" one of them asked, his gaze assessing. \"Are you also here for the treasure at the bottom of the sea?\"","Luo Yu finished setting up his tent and looked over at the group of independent cultivators, who seemed intent on resting right beside them. He couldn’t help but frown. \"This place is big enough,\" he stated plainly. \"Stay away from us and don’t disturb our rest.\"","Their plan had been to enter the sea discreetly the following day, when fewer people would be around. They had specifically chosen the most remote part of the beach to avoid any disturbances or unwanted attention. They certainly hadn’t anticipated a few unruly loose cultivators showing up.","\"Hehe, I didn’t expect you to have such a bad temper!\" one of the loose cultivators sneered. Seeing that Luo Yu and Gu Mo didn’t answer their questions and seemed clearly annoyed by their presence, their expressions turned cold. It wasn’t entirely their fault for being oblivious; after all, both Luo Yu and Gu Mo were skillfully concealing their true strength. These few wandering cultivators weren’t particularly powerful themselves, so they couldn’t discern the true abilities of the two.","On the contrary, they mistakenly assumed Luo Yu and Gu Mo were just like them—fellow wandering cultivators who had heard the rumors and come to explore for treasures. They had initially intended to recruit the two into their own group, but instead of a favorable reception, they had been rebuffed, naturally causing their expressions to turn hostile.","Compared to Luo Yu’s somewhat blunt words, Gu Mo’s response was far more direct and unequivocal. He didn’t bother engaging in further conversation with the unwelcome group. Instead, he simply released a fraction of the immense pressure from his body. In an instant, the scattered cultivators, who moments ago had been standing with bravado, found themselves immobilized under the overwhelming force. They involuntarily crumpled to their knees, cold sweat beading on their foreheads, their faces paling dramatically, and their eyes wide with profound fear.","\"Are you leaving or not?\" Gu Mo’s voice was icily calm, yet his aura pressed down on them like an insurmountable mountain, making it impossible for them to straighten their backs. The sheer power of his presence caused their qi and blood to surge violently within their bodies, creating a suffocating sensation that threatened to choke them.","\"Spare our lives... We’ll leave, we’ll leave right away...\" The leader of the loose cultivators managed to stammer out a plea for mercy, enduring the crushing pressure. As he spoke, he could already feel blood welling up in his throat, coating his tongue with its metallic taste.","Gu Mo had no intention of taking their lives. He promptly withdrew his immense pressure, watching as the terrified group scrambled away, crawling desperately until they were out of sight. With the nuisance dealt with, he calmly sat down at the entrance of his tent.","\"Tsk, tsk, that was impressive,\" Luo Yu grinned, patting Gu Mo on the shoulder. \"I’ll definitely learn from you next time.\"","Listening to his playful remark, Gu Mo didn’t respond directly. Instead, he gazed out at the vast sea, his expression thoughtful. \"Tell me,\" he began, his voice quieter now, \"if Hell’s Lord is really here, could he be in the sea? If that’s the case, then he...\"","He trailed off, unable to complete the sentence. The implications were immense. A living person, regardless of their power, could not simply remain indefinitely in the depths of the ocean without needing to surface. Unless, of course, there was some kind of hidden underwater secret palace or ancient ruins beneath the waves. How else could someone possibly block all six senses and sustain themselves in the ocean’s crushing depths without ever needing to emerge?","Luo Yu, who had been teasing moments before, sobered significantly upon hearing Gu Mo’s words. He, too, looked out at the dark, expansive sea. \"No matter what,\" he stated, his voice firm with conviction, \"I believe that Hell’s Lord is still alive. As long as he is alive, there are endless possibilities.\""]},{"number":4705,"title":"Chapter 4705: Discovery","paragraphs":["The two sat in silence by their tent, their gazes fixed on the rhythmic crash of waves against the shore, lost in their thoughts.","Early the next morning, as soon as the first light touched the horizon, Luo Yu and Gu Mo entered the sea from a secluded spot. With the water-repellent pearl in Luo Yu’s palm spinning, the sea water miraculously parted to both sides, revealing a clear path into the open ocean. They stepped forward, and as they did, the sea behind them seamlessly closed, returning to its undisturbed state. Gradually, they ventured deeper and deeper. Initially, the morning light still managed to pierce the surface, illuminating the seabed. However, as they descended further, all visibility vanished, replaced by a profound, pitch-black darkness – a realm where sunlight could not penetrate. The deepest parts of the sea were imbued with an undeniably mysterious aura.","As they explored the ocean’s depths, some cultivators with higher cultivation levels on the surface also sensed a subtle disturbance. They rose into the air and employed their divine sense to scan the seabed. What they detected slightly surprised them.","\"Someone has entered the sea?\" one exclaimed.","\"Judging from the movement of the sea, they must possess a water-repellent pearl.\"","\"What? A water-repellent pearl? Who could possibly have such a treasure?\" Those on the shore, hearing the stunned exclamations, couldn’t help but gaze out at the vast sea. Yet, they saw nothing extraordinary—only faint ripples on the water’s surface that quickly dissipated without a trace.","As time wore on, Luo Yu and Gu Mo steadily expanded the scope of their search across the vast ocean floor. The two released their powerful aura, ensuring that no sea monster dared to approach them. Protected by the invaluable water-repellent pearls, they remained safe throughout their exploration.","The two continued their diligent search from early morning well into the evening. At the bottom of the sea, the distinction between day and night was irrelevant, so they had no plans to return to the surface for rest. Instead, they pressed on, continuously extending their divine sense to probe the murky depths.","\"Wait!\" Gu Mo suddenly interjected, pulling Luo Yu to a halt in front of him.","\"What’s wrong? Did you find something?\" Luo Yu stopped and turned back, asking intently.","\"Over there,\" Gu Mo replied, holding a night pearl in one hand to illuminate their path and pointing into a particularly deep, dark direction. \"My divine sense seems to have encountered something we can’t get close to. Let’s go check it out.\"","\"Alright, let’s go.\" Luo Yu adjusted their course using his water-repellent pearl, heading toward the area Gu Mo indicated.","As they drew nearer, vibrant water plants, colorful corals, and intriguing rock formations came into view beneath their feet. The water surrounding them was incredibly clear and a pristine blue, made even more beautiful by the soft glow of the night pearl. Finally having made a discovery, the two hurried towards the location. As they drew closer, however, they realized they could not advance further. Approximately ten meters ahead of them, a powerful, invisible aura was shielding a central point, effectively preventing their approach. Not only were they physically blocked, but even their divine sense proved incapable of penetrating this formidable barrier to explore what lay deep within.","\"This aura appears to be that of an ancient divine beast, and it seems somewhat similar to the aura of the Green Dragon,\" Gu Mo remarked thoughtfully, gazing at the profound darkness before him, his heart stirring with a mix of awe and speculation. \"Hell’s Lord, could he possibly be inside there?\" He looked at Luo Yu, posing the question.","\"You’re asking me? Who else can I ask? We can’t even get through, and our divine sense can’t penetrate it either.\"","Luo Yu rolled his eyes, a hint of frustration in his tone. After a moment of thought, he added, \"Let’s go up first.\""]},{"number":4706,"title":"Chapter 4706: Inspection","paragraphs":["Gu Mo looked at Luo Yu and asked, \"Aren’t we going to investigate further?\"","\"How can we investigate?\" Luo Yu retorted. \"That aura is so powerful; how could you possibly get close to it? Moreover, if Hell’s Lord is truly inside, we can’t just force our way in, can we? If we accidentally hurt Hell’s Lord, how would we ever explain that to our Master?\" Luo Yu glanced at the shimmering barrier. \"Let’s go up first and leave a mark here. We’ll wait for Master to decide after we notify her. After all, just because we can’t get close doesn’t mean Master can’t.\"","Hearing this logical reasoning, Gu Mo nodded. \"Let’s go!\"","Luo Yu, holding the water-repellent pearl, and Gu Mo gathered their energy and propelled themselves upward from the seabed, directly towards the surface. Their ascent from the ocean floor to standing on the sea’s surface took approximately half an incense stick’s worth of time.","\"I didn’t expect it to be so deep,\" Luo Yu exclaimed in surprise once they breached the water. \"If it weren’t for the water-repellent pearl, I’m afraid we wouldn’t have been able to enter the deep sea at all.\" After they emerged, they glanced around, only to find that the coastline was no longer visible. The sky had completely darkened, making everything pitch black and severely obstructing their vision.","Gu Mo retrieved an airship from his spatial ring, and the two of them promptly jumped aboard. The airship didn’t fly away immediately but instead remained hovering directly above the spot where they had emerged from the sea.","\"I wonder if Master has finished refining the medicinal pills,\" Luo Yu mused as he took out his communication jade tablet. \"I’ll contact Du Fan or Leng Shuang first and tell them what we’ve discovered here.\"","\"You stay here and keep watch!\" Gu Mo instructed. \"I’ll go and scout the area to see how far we are from the coast.\" With that, he gathered his qi and flew off with his sword, heading in the direction where his divine sense had detected signs of human presence.","An Unexpected Encounter","As night deepened, some cultivators patrolling the sea discovered the illuminated airship. The cultivators exchanged glances, their curiosity piqued, and approached it cautiously.","\"This is the East Sea Spirit Realm. We are patrolling the sea on the orders of the Southern Emperor,\" a voice full of authority resonated from above. \"Who are you? Why has your airship landed in the East Sea Spirit Realm? If you have no important business, please leave immediately.\"","Luo Yu, who had been in the midst of communicating with Du Fan and the others, paused his conversation. He put away his communication jade tablet, stepped to the edge of the airship, and calmly addressed the patrolling cultivators. \"I am Luo Yu, one of the eight Phoenix Guard leaders under the Ghost Doctor. I am here in the East Sea Spirit Realm on my master’s orders. You can patrol your waters; simply leave me be.\"","Hearing that he was one of the esteemed leaders of the Phoenix Guards under the formidable Ghost Doctor, the patrolling cultivators were visibly taken aback. They carefully scrutinized Luo Yu, and after a moment of respectful silence, they bowed deeply. \"We did not know that one of the leaders of the Phoenix Guards under the Ghost Doctor was here. Please forgive our offense. However, recently, the East Sea Spirit Realm has been a little unsettled...\"","\"I know about that. There are quite a few cultivators gathering by the sea,\" Luo Yu stated in a calm, authoritative voice, his gaze unwavering as he looked at them. \"As sea guards, you should naturally go and deal with it.\"","Perhaps it was the clear disparity in their cultivation levels, or simply the weight of his words, but the few cultivators didn’t dare to say anything more under his piercing gaze. Instead, they bowed once more and promptly departed. Once they were a safe distance away, they quickly retrieved their own communication jade tablets and sent the news back to their superiors.","After resting on the airship for a while, Luo Yu saw Gu Mo return. He took a spirit fruit from his interspatial ring and tossed it to him, asking, \"How is it? Have you scouted the way?\""]},{"number":4707,"title":"Chapter 4707: It’s Here","paragraphs":["\"Don't worry, I've found them. They're some distance from the coast,\" Gu Mo confirmed, taking the spirit fruit and settling down beside Luo Yu.","\"Have you contacted Du Fan and the others?\"","\"Yes, we've contacted them, and they're already on their way. Master is also coming!\" Luo Yu grinned, a broad smile spreading across his face. \"Du Fan said that Master's medicinal pills have been refined. As soon as she heard the news that we were coming to the East Sea, she brought them with her. They're only a few days behind us, but at their speed, they should arrive here early tomorrow morning.\"","\"That's great!\" Hearing this, Gu Mo couldn't help but smile, a rare expression of relief on his usually stoic face.","\"But a few sea patrols just came by,\" Luo Yu mentioned, his expression turning thoughtful. \"They said they were under the command of the Monarch Nancheng. I sent them away.\" He paused, pondering. \"Does this East Sea Spirit Realm belong to Monarch Nancheng? I seem to recall that this place isn't included in his jurisdiction.\"","\"The four seas to the east, south, west, and north are not typically included in direct monarchical jurisdiction, but it's perfectly normal for there to be patrols,\" Gu Mo explained, his gaze fixed on the dark, distant sea. \"After all, there are many treasures in the sea. If there were no patrols, the treasures at the bottom of the sea would be plundered sooner or later.\"","\"Let's get some rest tonight! Next, we'll wait for Master and the others to arrive,\" Luo Yu said, stretching his waist before heading into the cabin to rest.","The next day, around noon, Feng Jiu and her entourage arrived.","Luo Yu and Gu Mo had been waiting patiently at the seaside since early morning. When they spotted them, Luo Yu's face broke into a wide grin, and he quickly walked up to greet them. \"Master!\" he exclaimed, his voice filled with genuine warmth.","Feng Jiu smiled, nodding at him. She glanced around, her keen eyes taking everything in, and then asked, \"Where's Gu Mo?\"","\"Master, Gu Mo is waiting in the airship above the sea. I'll take you there right away,\" Luo Yu replied. With a respectful nod to Du Fan, Leng Hua, and Leng Shuang, he led the group towards the location of the airship.","\"Isn't that the Ghost Doctor? How did she get here?\" someone among the gathered cultivators whispered, recognizing Feng Jiu's distinctive presence.","\"It is the Ghost Doctor. Could it be that there really is treasure in the sea? Is that why she came here?\" another speculated, a hint of greed in his voice.","\"Who is the Ghost Doctor? What kind of treasure hasn't she seen before? In my opinion, this isn't a simple matter at all,\" a more discerning cultivator commented, understanding the gravity of Feng Jiu's appearance.","\"How about we follow them? They seem to be heading towards the center of the sea,\" someone optimistically suggested, contemplating the idea of tailing the powerful group. However, no one agreed with him. In fact, everyone else looked at him as if he were an idiot, and the brief surge of curiosity he had finally mustered quickly faded away under their scornful gazes.","On the Airship","On the other side, Feng Jiu and her companions followed Luo Yu to the airship. As soon as Gu Mo saw her, he stepped forward, bowing respectfully. \"Master,\" he greeted.","\"Master, you must not have had much rest on your journey,\" Luo Yu said solicitously, inviting her onto the airship. \"Please sit down for a moment! We'll tell you what we found.\"","Seeing their consideration, Feng Jiu nodded, boarded the airship, and sat down. Once settled, she immediately cut to the chase. \"You only mentioned on the communication jade that there was a powerful aura below that you couldn't get close to, but that the aura felt like the Green Dragon's? What exactly is going on?\"","\"Master, we searched the seabed for a long time,\" Luo Yu began, explaining the discovery. \"But when we reached a certain place, we couldn't go any further, and even our divine sense couldn't penetrate the barrier. However, the aura emanating from it was very similar to that of the Green Dragon. We were wondering if Hell's Lord might be at the bottom of the sea.\" Luo Yu glanced at her, seeking her guidance. \"Master, shall I take you down there to have a look?\"","\"Down from this current position of the airship?\" Feng Jiu clarified, her gaze already fixed on the dark waters below.","\"Yes, it's directly below this location,\" Luo Yu and Gu Mo replied in unison, their voices resonating with a renewed sense of hope and anticipation."]},{"number":4708,"title":"Chapter 4708: I’m Here","paragraphs":["Chapter 4708: I’m Here","Hearing this confirmation, Feng Jiu immediately stood up, walking to the side of the airship. She closed her eyes and released her divine sense. As her spiritual perception extended downward, it reached a certain point and encountered a familiar aura. Her eyes snapped open.","“It’s him! He must be down there!” she declared with certainty, her heart swelling with a mixture of excitement and profound relief. However, as the initial thrill subsided, it was replaced by an even deeper confusion. While she had indeed sensed the unmistakable aura of the Green Dragon, Mo Ze’s own aura was exceptionally weak. How badly had the lightning tribulation injured him that day? And why was he sinking in the vast expanse of the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm?","“Move away a little, don’t stay right here. I’ll go down and take a look,” Feng Jiu instructed, turning back to face her companions.","“Master, don’t you need us to accompany you?” Luo Yu asked, stepping forward with concern.","“No need, just wait here,” she replied, shaking her head. She then retrieved a water-repellent pearl from her interspatial ring and, without further hesitation, leaped into the sea.","Seeing her descend alone, Luo Yu couldn’t help but feel a pang of worry. He leaned over the side of the airship, watching for a moment, then turned back to the others. “Will it be okay for Master to go down alone? She hasn’t rested since we left. Is she alright?”","“Don’t worry! Master knows what she’s doing,” Du Fan reassured him with a calm smile. He then turned to Gu Mo. “Let’s move the airship away a little, lest Master causes any commotion that affects the airship.”","“Mm,” Gu Mo replied, and without further delay, he maneuvered the airship to a safe distance.","On the other side, the Nancheng Monarch was slightly surprised to learn that Feng Jiu’s people had gone to the East Sea Spirit Realm. He had initially just instructed his patrols to keep an eye on them and observe their activities. However, it wasn’t long before news came back that even Feng Jiu herself had appeared in the East Sea Spirit Realm, which greatly piqued his curiosity. What was she doing in the East Sea? Could the recent strange phenomena in the East Sea have something to do with her presence?","Consequently, he ordered his men to continue their surveillance and report back immediately if there were any new developments. He specifically cautioned them not to interfere; after all, the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu was no ordinary person and could not be treated in an ordinary manner.","Compared to the speculation and curiosity unfolding above, Feng Jiu was now deep within the sea’s abyssal embrace. A water-repellent pearl floated gracefully in front of her, accompanied by a night pearl that cast a soft, ethereal glow through the darkness. The spiritual energy swirling around her created a subtle stream of air, preventing the surrounding seawater from touching her.","She took slow, deliberate steps forward, cautiously approaching the source of the surging energy. As she drew closer, she confirmed her earlier suspicion: the area was indeed sealed off by a powerful defensive barrier. Although the night pearl’s light illuminated their immediate vicinity, its reach into the vast darkness was limited.","Closing her eyes, she concentrated her divine sense on the barrier directly ahead. In that moment, she felt the pure spiritual energy of the sea gently surging and seeping into the place protected by the airflow, as if something within was actively absorbing this pristine energy.","The ancient aura of the Green Dragon surged around the barrier. Her divine sense even perceived that at the very center of the protective shield, the Green Dragon’s aura was meticulously safeguarding a sleeping figure. That person was none other than the husband she had tirelessly searched for: Xuanyuan Mo Ze!","“Mo Ze, Mo Ze...” she called out softly, her voice echoing only in the silent chambers of her heart, repeating his name over and over, trying desperately to rouse him. But he continued to sleep peacefully, seemingly oblivious to her presence, as if his five senses and six consciousnesses were completely sealed off.","She slowly opened her eyes, withdrawing her divine sense, and felt a wave of profound bitterness well up in her heart. She whispered softly into the vast, silent depths, “Mo Ze, I’m here.”"]},{"number":4709,"title":"Chapter 4709: It Won’t Be Long","paragraphs":["Chapter 4709: It Won’t Be Long","Her voice, a mere whisper in the vast, silent depths of the ocean, was almost inaudible. She stood there quietly, taking a moment to compose her emotions before extending her hand to touch the shimmering barrier before her.","The spiritual energy and ancient pressure radiating from her body surged as she meticulously mobilized her internal power. Pure spiritual energy poured forth from her palm, causing the surrounding seawater to churn violently under the immense pressure emanating from her. With a precise rotation of her palm, a clear, resonant shout escaped her lips.","“Break!”","The commanding cry, filled with overwhelming pressure and raw energy, echoed through the water, causing the sea to surge with even greater intensity. On the surface, the waves grew increasingly fierce, mirroring the unseen power being unleashed below.","As soon as Feng Jiu’s voice faded, a wave of spiritual energy, visible even in the dim light, spread out from her palm. Beneath the water, a faint cracking sound reverberated, and immediately afterward, the isolated aura dispersed into the vast sea, vanishing without a trace. With the barrier gone, the scene ahead gradually became clear under the illuminating glow of the night pearl.","She gazed at him, suspended effortlessly in the water, a pure spiritual energy surging from his form. The majestic Green Dragon’s energy was intricately entwined around him, protecting him meticulously. She quickly stepped forward, reaching out to embrace him, but the moment her hand made contact, she froze. Her eyes widened in utter disbelief, and a look of profound panic etched itself onto her face.","“Mo Ze...”","She watched in horror as her hand passed directly through him. He was undeniably right there, floating before her, yet she couldn’t touch his body. Or rather, he didn’t possess a tangible body at all; he was merely an illusory existence.","“How could this be? How could this be? Mo Ze, Mo Ze, wake up! It’s me, I’m here. Open your eyes and look at me...” she cried out to him, her heart consumed by an overwhelming fear and helplessness.","He was clearly present, right in front of her, yet she couldn’t reach him, as if an immense, invisible chasm separated them. She called out to him again and again, her voice filled with desperate urgency, but he remained peacefully asleep, without the slightest flicker of reaction.","Gradually, she noticed that his ethereal body was beginning to fade, a realization that intensified her panic. She instinctively reached out to touch him once more, but again, her hand passed harmlessly through him.","“Mo Ze, what’s wrong with you? How can I save you? How can I save you?” Tears streamed uncontrollably from her eyes. As her tears fell onto his illusory form, his body, which had been subtly fading, seemed to solidify slightly.","The seawater that had been repelled by the water-repellent pearls began to flow back towards him, drawn by the surge of the Green Dragon’s aura, completely enveloping him. As his body was surrounded by the ocean, his fading form returned to its previous state, appearing as if he were simply lying there quietly asleep.","Witnessing this miraculous transformation, Feng Jiu took a step back, swiftly wiped the tears from her eyes, and declared softly but with unwavering determination, “No matter what it takes, I will wake you up!”","Looking at the powerful Green Dragon aura still surrounding him, Feng Jiu spoke softly, a sense of profound gratitude in her voice. “Green Dragon, you are protecting him, aren’t you? Thank you for protecting him for me. He has not disappeared from this world, so he will definitely stand at the peak again! That day will not be long!”"]},{"number":4710,"title":"Chapter 4710: Nurturing the Soul","paragraphs":["She gazed deeply at Xuanyuan Mo Ze, then slowly retreated step by step. Finally, she formed an ancient seal with her hands and re-sealed the area. As the new barrier she had erected settled into place, a layer of water rippled around them. In the next moment, she flicked her sleeves, put away the night pearl, clutched the water-repellent pearl in her hand, spun gracefully, and ascended swiftly towards the sea surface.","Du Fan and the others waited anxiously on the airship. They watched as waves crashed against the sea surface, layer after layer, even witnessing some rise several meters high. They couldn't help but wonder if their Master had indeed found Hell's Lord down there. As time passed, they noticed other cultivators not far from them, seemingly watching their movements, their curiosity piqued by the unusual activity.","After a while, a vivid red figure spun up from the depths, rotating elegantly in midair. As she spun, water droplets flew outwards, and in no time, her previously damp clothes were completely dry, without a single trace of water.","\"Master!\"","Seeing her emerge from the sea, the people on the airship couldn't help but let out cries of joy and relief. However, after the initial surge of excitement, they quickly realized that their Master had come out alone. Hell's Lord was still nowhere to be seen. For a moment, the people exchanged uncertain glances, and the smiles on their faces gradually faded.","Feng Jiu stood above the sea, her red robe fluttering in the wind, her black hair dancing around her. Her exquisite face held a slightly cold, resolute aura, and her eyes, which carried the inherent authority of a high-ranking official, swept lightly over the curious onlookers before she gathered her energy and flew back to the airship.","\"Send a message back and call a Phoenix Guard over here to patrol,\" Feng Jiu ordered indifferently, her voice firm.","Hearing this, the others exchanged glances. Luo Yu gently nudged Du Fan beside him with his elbow, subtly motioning for him to ask the questions they all harbored.","Seeing the unspoken prompt, Du Fan responded, \"Yes, I'll send word back and call a Phoenix Guard over.\" He paused briefly, then, gathering his courage, asked, \"Master, did you find anything at the bottom of the sea? Is the Lord of Hell down there?\"","\"He's down there, but the situation isn't good,\" Feng Jiu said softly, her voice tinged with both helplessness and unconcealed worry. \"I can't bring him up, so I had to leave him there.\"","She continued, her voice gaining a touch of resolve, \"The Green Dragon's true qi is protecting him and nourishing his soul. I've set up another barrier down there, and I've ordered our people to patrol the surrounding waters to make sure no one disturbs him.\"","\"Yes, I understand,\" Du Fan replied, his earlier questions answered. He looked at her, sensing her mood, and said nothing further, instead turning and heading into the cabin to make the necessary arrangements. Once inside, he immediately took out his communication jade and informed Qi Kang and the others about what had transpired, reiterating the order to dispatch a Phoenix Guard to the location.","\"It seems that Hell's Lord is in really bad shape. Even Master couldn't bring him up from the bottom of the sea,\" Luo Yu couldn't help but voice his concern to Gu Mo. \"How badly do you think the lightning tribulation injured him? How long will it take to nourish his soul?\"","Leng Hua glanced at him, understanding the gravity of the situation. \"The Master isn't in a good mood,\" he advised softly. \"Let's just do as she said! The other masters didn't say anything, so we shouldn't ask too many questions right now.\"","\"Yes, I understand,\" Luo Yu replied, sighing as he looked out at the vast sea, the mystery of Hell's Lord's condition weighing on him.","\"Should we park the airship here or go to the coast?\" Gu Mo asked the others, seeking a decision on their immediate next steps.","Du Fan thought for a moment, then concluded, \"Let's park here first! Otherwise, some cultivators with bad intentions might take the opportunity to sneak into the sea.\""]},{"number":4711,"title":"Chapter 4711: Leave","paragraphs":["That day, Feng Jiu didn’t emerge from the cabin after she entered it. Du Fan and the others understood that she must be in a very low mood, so they dared not disturb her. At such a time, they knew she needed to be left alone. Feng Jiu remained in the cabin for an entire day. During that time, she thought deeply, contemplating many things, and finally made up her mind. It wasn’t until early the next morning that she finally came out.","\"Master, are you awake? Please sit down and let me pour you a cup of water,\" Leng Shuang said with a gentle smile when she saw Feng Jiu emerge.","\"No need to bother,\" Feng Jiu replied, walking to the side of the ship and gazing out at the sea. \"Call everyone out! I have something to tell them.\"","\"Yes,\" Leng Shuang responded, then went to knock on the doors of the other cabins where everyone else was resting.","\"Master.\"","Du Fan and the others soon emerged, approached her, and bowed respectfully.","Feng Jiu turned to face them. \"I’m going out to travel and temper my mind in preparation for ascension,\" she announced. \"I called you out to give you instructions. Guard this place well and don’t let anyone disturb him in the sea. After the Pheonix Guards arrives here, one of you must take the lead in guarding this place at regular intervals.\"","Hearing her words, everyone was stunned for a moment. They exchanged quick glances, then replied in unison, \"Master, rest assured, we will protect this sea area and not let anyone disturb the soul of the Lord of Hell.\"","After their solemn promise, Luo Yu couldn’t help but ask, \"Master, how long will you be traveling? When will you return?\"","Feng Jiu shook her head. \"I don’t know,\" she said softly. She turned to look at the sea once more. \"What I lack is an opportunity. Moreover, too many things have happened in the past few years, and I have too much on my mind. I have to travel around, see the world, temper my mind, and prepare for my ascension.\"","She then looked up at the sky, her eyes hardening slightly. \"When a Supreme Being ascends, if they succeed, they will live as long as heaven and earth and rule over the world. But if they fail, all their cultivation will be destroyed, and they will never have a second chance. Mo Ze failed to ascend because those above wanted to kill him. If Old Man Tianji hadn’t risked his life to save him, his soul would not have been able to hide in the depths of the sea to nurture itself.","As for me, I have ascended through 9981 lightning tribulations, and I am only allowed to succeed, not fail!\" She emphasized her resolve. She didn’t have a second chance, nor would she allow herself to fail! Because up there, not only were their children waiting for her, but also the enemies she wanted to destroy!","Upon hearing her resolute words, Du Fan immediately knelt down on one knee, his voice resounding and powerful: \"Please rest assured, Master! We swear to protect Hell’s Lord with our lives and will not let anyone harm his soul! We will wait here for Master’s return! We will celebrate Master’s successful ascension and live as long as heaven and earth!\"","Hearing this heartfelt vow, Feng Jiu looked at them, the corners of her lips curving slightly upward into a faint smile. \"Get up!\" she commanded. \"I believe you will do what I have asked of you.\"","The group stood up and looked at her. She leaned against the ship’s railing, her expression calm and her gaze distant, as if lost in deep thought. They stood quietly, their eyes fixed on her, none of them speaking. At that moment, their Master gave them the distinct feeling that she would depart at any moment, that they couldn’t hold onto her.","Feng Jiu remained on the airship in the East Sea for three more days. Three days later, in the early morning, she left them a message and, as they watched her walk away alone."]},{"number":4712,"title":"Chapter 4712: Competition","paragraphs":["At Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor was currently taking his three disciples on a journey to prepare for their annual competition.","The three disciples sat with him on a flying artifact, soaring through the sky after leaving Yunxiao Mountain. They gazed down at the many landscapes passing beneath them, but their master remained silent about the specifics of the upcoming annual competition.","Since they began their training under the Azure Emperor, they’d participated in smaller, semi-annual competitions, which served as friendly exchanges of skills among themselves. However, their master hadn’t offered a single word about this particular, larger competition, leaving them completely in the dark about what to expect.","Yue’er, nestled between her two brothers, remembered how much their master doted on her. She playfully rolled her beautiful eyes and, with a bright smile, asked, \"Master, what is this big competition that happens once a year? Are you taking us to compete with other people?\"","The Azure Emperor sat quietly, his eyes closed. When he heard her question, he didn’t even open them, simply stating with indifference, \"Don’t worry, you’ll find out soon enough.\"","Hearing this, Yue’er exchanged a glance with her two brothers and playfully stuck out her tongue in exasperation.","Around noon, the Azure Emperor finally opened his eyes and looked at Muchen and Muyue. \"I will give you one month,\" he announced. \"After one month, you must bring back 100 crystal cores that you hunted yourselves and return to Yunxiao Mountain alone. You cannot use or rely on flying to return; you must walk back on foot. If you fail to return to Yunxiao Mountain after one month, then you will have to accept punishment.\"","\"Master wants us to hunt beasts and obtain 100 crystal cores, and then return to Yunxiao Mountain alone on foot? We can’t even travel together?\" Muchen couldn’t help but ask, clearly bewildered. It had taken their master’s flying artifact an entire morning just to reach their current location. If they had to walk, how long would it possibly take them to get back to Yunxiao Mountain?","\"Yes, you cannot travel together. You must walk back alone,\" the Azure Emperor reiterated with an air of indifference. He then looked at them and continued, \"I will divide three strands of my divine consciousness and place them on each of you. I will know everything you do. If there is danger, you must learn to save yourselves, but when you encounter danger that you cannot resolve, you may call for me to save you. However, should you call for my intervention, that person will automatically withdraw from the competition and must return to Yunxiao Mountain to accept the punishment for failure.\"","Hearing this, Yue’er blinked her eyes, a spark of curiosity in her gaze. \"Master, what is the punishment if we fail?\" she inquired.","The Azure Emperor glanced at her. \"The punishment for the two of you is that for the next year, you can only eat fasting pills and cannot consume any food. Furthermore, you must be separated from each other and cannot meet or practice cultivation with the other two.\"","Upon hearing this, Muchen and Muyue’s young faces immediately became serious. The thought of eating fasting pills was unappealing, but the idea of being separated and unable to see each other was far worse. They yearned to practice together every day, share conversations, and grow up side-by-side. The prospect of a year apart, alone, was something they couldn’t even begin to imagine.","\"I don’t want to be separated from my brother and Big Brother,\" Yue’er said hurriedly, her voice earnest. \"I want to cultivate with them, play with them, and grow up together.\"","\"Then work hard in this competition,\" the Azure Emperor said slowly, his gaze sweeping over them. \"If you can all return to Yunxiao Mountain within a month, you will not need to accept punishment.\""]},{"number":4713,"title":"Chapter 4713: Be Careful","paragraphs":["The Azure Emperor glanced at the two younger disciples, then fixed his gaze on Hao’er. \"Yun Chen,\" he began, \"you are stronger than them, so you must hunt for 300 crystal cores. You, too, must return to Yunxiao Mountain on foot within a month. If you fail, the punishment will be the same, with the addition of not being allowed to see your mother for a year.\"","He understood precisely what his three children valued most. This punishment, though seemingly harsh, targeted their deepest affections, making it profoundly effective. Sure enough, upon hearing his words, Hao’er nodded solemnly. \"Master, rest assured, your disciple understands. Your disciple will definitely return to Yunxiao Mountain within a month.\"","The Azure Emperor nodded. \"All three of you must act alone and not help each other. I have chosen beasts of different ranks for you. Yun Chen, you go first! The beasts in this forest are quite powerful, so be careful.\"","\"Yes,\" Hao’er replied, then looked at Muchen and Muyue. \"You two be careful too. See you on the mountain.\"","\"Mm hmm, Big Brother, you be careful too~\"","Muchen and Muyue said in unison as they watched Hao’er summon his flying sword and soar alone towards the forest below. Before long, he disappeared from their sight.","\"Are you afraid?\" The Azure Emperor looked at the two remaining disciples and asked.","\"No, we’re not afraid.\"","The two shook their heads. Although young, they had already experienced many trials. When they were even younger, they had been separated from their mother and had followed their Big Brother. More recently, after reuniting with their mother, she had taught them invaluable lessons. They had also learned a great deal from their master during the past year they had spent with him. At the very least, when faced with danger, they now knew how to defend themselves. What’s more, their master had promised to divide a strand of his divine consciousness to protect them, and they also had their contract beasts for support, so fear was not an overwhelming emotion.","However, not being afraid didn’t mean they weren’t worried. After all, this was their first time undertaking such a solo mission, and it would last for an entire month.","Seeing the mixture of determination and slight apprehension in their eyes, the Azure Emperor’s lips curved slightly. \"Don’t worry, go down!\" he instructed.","He then sent the two of them to different parts of the forest and didn’t linger. He simply told them to be careful and departed.","The three children were now in the same expansive forest but in completely different locations. When they found themselves truly alone, a sense of isolation and helplessness settled over them. Apart from themselves, there were only towering trees, dense weeds, and the faint, unsettling roars of unseen beasts.","After landing, Hao’er quickly began exploring the forest in search of prey. Acquiring 300 crystal cores meant he had to kill 300 beasts and then traverse the long journey back on foot, all within a single month. It was clear that time was a very tight constraint. Even though his strength had significantly increased over the past year, he dared not be careless in this formidable forest. Instead, he gathered his resolve and proceeded with extreme caution.","Meanwhile, not far from where Muchen had landed, a fierce beast lurked hidden in the tall grass. When it spotted the human child, it cautiously began to approach, baring its sharp teeth and preparing to pounce. But just as it coiled to strike, the human child, who had been standing motionless, suddenly sprang forward with a subtle movement of his toes, expertly straddling the beast’s back. In the same fluid motion, a cold dagger was plunged into its neck.","\"Swish!\"","A sharp, hoarse scream pierced the air, echoing loudly through the forest. Immediately, a strong, metallic scent of blood began to spread, signaling the swift and decisive end of the encounter."]},{"number":4714,"title":"Chapter 4714: Showing Their Skills","paragraphs":["Fresh blood dripped onto the ground, staining the weeds trampled under the fierce beast’s feet a dark red. Muchen’s knife hadn’t delivered an immediate killing blow, and the creature began to thrash violently, desperate to throw off that little human clinging to its back.","Muchen clamped his legs tightly around the beast’s body, hugged its head with one hand, and with the other, plunged the dagger deeper. He didn’t dare pull it out, instead clamping the beast’s body even tighter and increasing the force in his hand. A guttural howling rang in his ears, and the fierce beast’s movements gradually slowed until, with a few final shakes, it collapsed with a heavy thud.","Muchen gasped for breath, sweat beading on his forehead. He climbed down from the fallen beast and checked again, confirming its death. Only then did he breathe a sigh of relief. He quickly used his dagger to dig out the beast crystal before swiftly departing the area.","On another side of the forest, Yue’er walked leisurely. When she spotted a good number of low-grade spiritual herbs, a joyful smile lit up her face. She carefully picked them, storing each one in her interspatial ring.","It was midday, and some beasts were out foraging for food. A spiny boar with formidable tusks emerged from the dense trees and immediately spotted the little human crouched on the ground, diligently digging for spiritual herbs. Drool began to trickle from its mouth, and its breathing grew heavy and ragged as it stared with undisguised hunger at the little human.","Yue’er heard the noise and looked up to see the tusks-bearing beast, resembling a large pig, staring at her and drooling. She couldn’t help but blink, staring back at it blankly for a moment. Her mind raced. The boar was immense, with black fur that bristled like sharp spines, and its two sharp, curved tusks protruding from its mouth looked incredibly dangerous.","Her beautiful eyes quickly scanned its body, and she realized that this fanged pig would be very difficult to defeat in a direct confrontation. She immediately stood up and quickly backed away.","\"Roar!\"","The fanged boar saw her movement and let out a savage roar, then leaped forward, pouncing towards Yue’er.","Seeing this, Yue’er quickly pointed her toes, took a deep breath, and sprang onto a large tree. She looked down at the pig below, which was now circling the tree, attempting to break it down. Recognizing her precarious position, she used the momentum to jump again, landing on a higher branch. Only then did she pat her chest and let out a light sigh of relief. \"Phew, that scared me to death.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, a loud crash reverberated from below, and the tree shook slightly. Swaying precariously on the branch, she was startled into hugging the tree tightly to steady herself.","Looking down, she saw the wild boar repeatedly charging at the tree, causing large chunks of bark to peel off the trunk. Seeing this relentless assault, her beautiful eyes darted around, and a sly gleam, like that of a fox, flashed across them.","She took a slingshot from her spatial ring, pulled out an iron ball, aimed directly at the fierce beast’s head below, and fired it with all her might. The iron ball struck the beast’s head. Although it wasn’t a fatal blow, it was certainly painful, causing the boar to roar and bellow even more furiously.","However, after Yue’er fired several more iron balls in quick succession, she watched as the fierce beast raised its head and roared angrily at her. She pulled back the slingshot in her hand again, and this time, a pill flew out, directly hitting the fierce beast’s mouth as it roared.","\"Yes! I hit it!\" Yue’er clapped her hands happily, her beautiful eyes sparkling with a triumphant smile."]},{"number":4715,"title":"Chapter 4715: Harvest","paragraphs":["From her angle from high in the tree, she observed as the formidable beast consumed the dart she had expertly fired into its gaping maw. It lowered its head, a roar escaping its throat, uncannily human-like in its agony, as if it were struggling to expel the foreign object. A faint smile touched her lips as she drew back her slingshot, launching yet another iron ball towards it.","\"Roar!\"","The fierce beast looked up and roared at Yue’er, brimming with what appeared to be pure rage. It scraped its hoofed feet against the earth, then coiled its powerful body, leaping as if to launch itself into the tree. Yet, for all its ferocity, it remained, at its core, a wild boar with imposing tusks. Even as a ’fierce beast’ of this world, the natural limitations of its form prevented it from scaling trees.","After two futile attempts, it let out a frustrated howl, then, to Yue’er’s surprise, spun around and bolted.","As the fierce beast continued its panicked escape, the effects of Yue’er’s potent concoction gradually took hold. Its frenzied pace began to falter, its powerful strides losing their momentum, until, with a resounding crash, it collided violently with a large tree.","\"Hee hee~\" A soft chuckle escaped Yue’er’s lips as she trailed behind. She maintained a cautious distance, however, opting instead to pick up a sturdy tree branch and prod the incapacitated creature. Confirming its stillness, she then approached it directly.","She drew her gleaming dagger, its sharp edge glinting in the dappled sunlight, and expertly slashed at the neck of the boar-like beast. As the blade severed its carotid artery, the creature twitched once, a desperate, final spasm as if attempting to rekindle its life force. But the swift, fatal blow had already ended all hope.","With practiced efficiency, she extracted the valuable crystal core. Next, she retrieved some low-grade spiritual herbs she had diligently gathered earlier, crushing them between her fingers to release their essence. She then carefully dripped the potent juice onto the body of the fallen beast. She then took out some intricately carved flags used for setting up arrays from her own space. She meticulously arranged them in a protective circle around the carcass, completing the setup, and then sought out a discreet hiding place nearby.","She understood her own limitations, she was small and physically weaker than her two older brothers. Gathering a hundred crystal cores through brute force alone would be an arduous, if not impossible, task for her.","However, Yue’er possessed a keen intellect and an innate understanding of how to leverage her knowledge. By employing strategy and the skills she had painstakingly acquired, she wouldn’t have to worry about the formidable challenge of hunting a hundred fierce beasts.","The three siblings had dispersed, each positioned in a different corner of the vast forest. They knew, with absolute certainty, that their master would discreetly watch over and protect them. This assurance freed them from external anxieties, allowing them to focus entirely on their individual tasks.","Six days later, Yue’er was in a small secluded cave, carefully counting the crystal cores she had accumulated over the days in a serious manner.","\"Forty-eight, forty-nine, fifty... fifty-three.\" Her eyes gleamed with undisguised excitement as she gazed at the small, vibrant pile of colourful crystal cores before her.","\"Fifty-three! Only forty-seven more to reach a hundred.\" She carefully enumerated on her fingers, a soft murmur escaping her lips. \"Fifty-three... it took six days. I’ve killed almost nine fierce beasts a day. If I want to collect a hundred crystal cores in ten days, then for the next four days, I have to, I have to...\"","She blinked her eyes in concentration, her tiny fingers still moving as she calculated, her earnest, focused expression was profound yet comical on her little childish appearance.","Finally, after a considerable mental effort, she arrived at her conclusion. She carefully returned all the crystal cores to her spatial pocket, then produced a spirit fruit, which she consumed with relish. Reinvigorated, she stood up and, with her two short legs, ventured back outside. She had set numerous traps in the surrounding area and now it was time to check if any unsuspecting beasts had fallen into them.","The past few days of living in the wilderness had left her looking disheveled. She had tied her hair into two small, neat braids, which swung rhythmically as she walked. The clothes she wore were not their usual attire, perfectly suited for the demands of the forest.","As she approached one of the traps she had meticulously prepared, she stepped into the clearing. To her surprise, she found not only seven or eight fierce beasts ensnared within the array but also, inexplicably, a human figure."]},{"number":4716,"title":"Chapter 4716: Little Boy","paragraphs":["She glanced at the unconscious person but did not approach. Instead, she first checked the beasts to ensure they were all unconscious from her poison. Only then did she use her dagger to kill them and extract their crystal cores.","After dealing with the beasts, she walked over to the man and took a look at him. He was a little boy who looked about seven or eight years old, covered in wounds, some of which looked like they were caused by beast claws, but others looked like they were caused by swords.","She had been studying medicine for some time, so she could naturally tell that the sword wounds were very serious and that someone was determined to kill him.","She took out a small bottle from her space, opened it, and held it to the boy’s nose so he could smell it. After a while, his eyelashes fluttered slightly, and he opened his eyes.","However, as soon as he opened his eyes, he instinctively pushed her away with both hands. She wasn’t prepared and fell directly to the ground.","\"Why did you push me?\" Yue’er glared at him unhappily, patted her clothes, stood up, and said with an aggrieved tone, \"I saved you!\"","The little boy was startled, as if he had just realized that the person in front of him was a little girl even younger than him. He suddenly became a little nervous and embarrassed, and said, \"I’m sorry, I, I, I didn’t mean to.\" As soon as he finished speaking, the little boy lowered his head, his eyes reddened, and tears fell down his cheeks.","Yue’er was taken aback and hurriedly said, \"I didn’t hit you or scold you, why are you crying?\"","Yue’er shouldn’t have asked. As soon as she did, the little boy began to cry loudly, \"I... I... I’m stuck here and can’t get out. I’ve been stuck here all night, and there are several fierce beasts. I’m so scared they’ll eat me.\"","Hearing this, Yue’er blinked, looked at him, and asked somewhat dumbfounded, \"How did you run in here? You ran into this formation, and these fierce beasts weren’t unconscious when you came in? So you stayed with several fierce beasts all night?\"","\"Someone wanted to kill me, so I ran away, but I kept running around in circles and couldn’t get out. There were several fierce beasts in here, and the wounds on my back were scratches from those beasts. I climbed up a tree to avoid being eaten, but then I fell down and fainted.\" He wiped away his tears and cried, his voice choked up, but he was still able to speak clearly.","Yue’er listened, feeling a little embarrassed as she scratched her pigtails and said sheepishly, \"Um, I set up this formation. I used it to catch fierce beasts. I didn’t expect anyone to break in.\"","She had placed medicine in the array to lure the fierce beasts, as well as some medicine that would cause them to fall unconscious and powerless after smelling it for a long time. It was a miracle that this person had entered her array and not been eaten by those fierce beasts.","\"You... you set up the array?\" The little boy stared at the little girl in front of him, who was even smaller than him, somewhat incredulous.","\"Yes! My master taught me this array formation. Not even a Golden Core Cultivator could escape it.\" She said with a smile, staring at his wounds and said, \"Let me bandage your wounds! You need to clean the wounds caused by the fierce beasts, or they will become infected.\"","Without waiting for him to respond, Yue’er took out some medicine and helped him clean and bandage his wounds. Hearing his stomach growl, she said with a smile, \"Let me treat you to some meat! I’ve been here for several days and haven’t seen a single person. You’re the first person I’ve met!\"","Hearing this, the little boy was stunned and asked blankly, \"You’re here by yourself? What are you doing here?\""]},{"number":4717,"title":"Chapter 4717: Lying in wait","paragraphs":["Chapter 4717: Lying in wait","Yue’er smiled at him and didn’t answer, but said, “It’s dangerous in here, you’d better leave quickly! Otherwise, you’ll run into fierce beasts and get into trouble. I know where the way out is, I’ll tell you!”","The little boy paused, a flicker of hesitation in his eyes. “I can’t go back the way I came in,” he confessed, his voice barely a whisper. “Those people must be guarding the entrance. If I go out there, they’ll surely kill me.”","“Don’t worry, there’s more than one way out of here!” Yue’er said with a smile, taking a piece of dried meat out of her space and handing it to him. “I roasted this yesterday. You can eat it.”","“Thank you,” the little boy replied, taking it and tore off a piece and began to ate while asking, “Are you coming out with me?”","“I’m not leaving yet,” she said, shaking her head. “I still have things to do here! I have to stay for four more days.” She shook her head, walked over and removed the array as she was busy collecting the small flags.","Then she walked with him for a while, pointed in a direction, and said, “If you keep going in this direction, you’ll be able to get out. I’ve checked, and there’s a mountain path outside. If you follow the mountain path, you’ll be able to get out.”","However, the little boy made no move to leave. Instead, he hesitated, his shoulders slumping slightly. “I don’t dare to go by myself,” he admitted, his voice small and fearful. “I’m afraid I’ll encounter fierce beasts. I can’t fight them.”","Hearing this, Yue’er blinked, her beautiful eyes fixed on him for a long moment. A little frown creased her delicate face, a sign of her internal struggle. She seemed genuinely distressed by his predicament. “You don’t dare to go by yourself? I can’t take you out now because it will waste my time; I still have to collect more crystal cores. Otherwise, why don’t you stay here with me for a few more days, and then you can come out with me?”","“Alright.” The little boy nodded readily, a spark of hope in his eyes. He looked at her directly. “My name is Lin Yang. What’s your name?”","“My name is Yun Qi,” Yue’er replied with a bright smile. “I’m going to look for more fierce beasts now; do you want to come with me?”","“Look for fierce beasts? Aren’t you afraid?” he asked, a blank look of surprise on his face.","“No, I’m not afraid, because I’m very powerful~” she stated with utmost confidence.","Lin Yang hesitated for a moment, then, driven by curiosity and a lingering sense of safety near her, he made his decision. “Then I’ll go with you and take a look!”","And so, after several solitary days in the vast wilderness, Yue’er finally had a little friend to talk to. She led Lin Yang towards another of her strategically chosen formation points, eager to see if any more fierce beasts had been successfully trapped.","When they arrived at another spot and entered the formation, they saw five fierce beasts lying motionless on the ground. She happily walked forward and said, “Maybe I can leave here and go back in three more days.”","As she spoke, she walked towards the fierce beasts and took out her dagger, preparing to stab them again. Suddenly, one of the fierce beasts lying motionless on the ground jumped up, growled, and lunged at her.","“Be careful!” Lin Yang saw this and was so frightened that his face turned pale, and he instinctively cried out","Yue’er also didn’t expect that there would be a fierce beast lying in wait here. However, her reaction was remarkably swift. Almost at the same time the beast pounced towards her, she took a step to the side and dodged its jaws.","“Hurry up and climb the tree! Quick!” Yue’er shouted to Lin Yang, who was still standing on the other side, momentarily frozen in a daze of terror.","“Oh, oh!” Lin Yang came to his senses, but his small face was pale, and there was obvious fear in his eyes. The more panicked he became, the more flustered he became, and after two attempts, he was still unable to climb the big tree."]},{"number":4718,"title":"Chapter 4718: Stunned","paragraphs":["Chapter 4718: Stunned","“Roar!”","“Quick, climb the tree! That fierce beast is a sacred beast, climb the tree!” Yue’er shouted anxiously. Seeing the fierce beast roar and pounce toward Lin Yang, she didn’t even think to dodge, but instead gathered her strength and flew to his side, quickly pulling him away as the beast lunged forward.","“Get up, quickly!” Yue’er pushed him, using her hand to help him climb the tree first. After he jumped up and climbed the tree, she turned back and saw that the fierce beast was instantly pouncing towards them.","“Yun Qi, get up here! Hurry up!” Lin Yang cried out in alarm. Seeing the fierce beast lunging at her, he thought she was doomed, but to his surprise, she didn’t dodge, but instead held the dagger in her hand and charged forward.","“Yun Qi, are you trying to get yourself killed?” he shouted, frantic as an ant on a hot pan.","At this moment, Yue’er ignored him and focused all her energy on the fierce beast. Although she had been using medicine to deal with those fierce beasts and easily dug out their crystal cores, she had also been trained by her master and two brothers. Even if she was not as good as her two brothers, she was not that weak.","The fierce beast was now determined to pounce on her, and avoiding it again and again would not solve the problem. Since that was the case, she might as well fight with all her might!","“Roar!”","The sacred beast’s roar echoed, making her ears ring. Though she had an ancient divine beast within her, her master had sealed away their divine beast’s aura to avoid detection. Otherwise, not even a divine beast would dare approach her.","She used the exquisite body techniques she had trained for a year to dodge, and took the opportunity to stab the sacred beast’s hindquarters with the cold dagger in her hand. The sharp blade pierced the sacred beast’s hindquarters with a whistling sound, accompanied by its agonized scream.","The fierce beast became even more violent due to the wound on its hindquarters and charged at Yue’er. She took advantage of her small and agile body to dodge it. Seeing it charging towards her, she gritted her teeth, bent backwards and dived under the fierce beast, stabbing it with the sharp blade in her hand.","“Roooaar!”","Blood spurted out like a fountain, splattering Yue’er all over. After stabbing the sacred beast, she nimbly turned and dodged out from under it, quickly retreating to safety.","The sacred beast roared and scrambled around for a few meters before collapsing with convulsions. Soon, the ground was stained red with blood, and the fierce beast twitched a few times before stiffening and dying.","Seeing this scene, Yue’er took a deep breath, her hand holding the dagger trembling slightly. She had stabbed it too hard, with such force that she could hardly open her hand.","However, seeing the fierce beast lying on the ground, covered in blood and motionless, she knew that this time, it was dead.","Thinking that she could get not only the crystal core on its head but also the inner core inside its body, she couldn’t help but feel a little excited. After taking a deep breath, she walked forward.","Lin Yang, who was clinging to a tree and hiding above, saw the scene below and was unable to recover for a long time. His eyes were wide open, as if he didn’t recognize the little girl below who was even smaller than him. He just watched her swallow hard, looking dazed..."]},{"number":4719,"title":"Chapter 4719: Shock","paragraphs":["Chapter 4719: Shock","Especially when he saw that tiny person holding a dagger and digging out the crystal core of the sacred beast, then slitting open its abdomen and taking out a medicinal pill inside, the bloody scene and that tiny person looked very strange.","At this moment, he couldn’t help but wonder who Yun Qi’s parents were. She was clearly younger than him, and she was just a little girl, so how could she be so brave?","“Lin Yang, let’s roast some meat to eat today! The meat will be tender and delicious when it’s freshly roasted, and this is a sacred beast, so we can make jerky out of its meat.” She said with a smile, staring at the sacred beast on the ground and already thinking about how to eat it.","However, after a long time, she didn’t hear any movement, so she looked up and saw him hugging the big tree, pale and stiff. She waved her hand and called out, “Come down quickly! Wait, you help me pick up the branches. You have to work to eat!”","“Alright, alright.” He swallowed hard and responded, then climbed down from the tree and walked carefully over to her. He looked at her and asked, “Yun Qi, who are you? How could you kill such a sacred beast?”","“Hehe, I told you I was very powerful!” She smiled mysteriously, quickly dealt with the other fierce beasts, put away the crystal cores, and then said, “Help me drag this sacred beast back to the cave, then go pick some branches. I’ll teach you how to roast meat.”","Seeing that she didn’t say anything, he could only agree and help her drag the sacred beast out of the formation and into a small cave.","“Is this where you live?” Lin Yang looked at the cave. It was only about two meters deep and surrounded by trees, making it difficult to spot.","“Mm-hm, I’ve been living here for the past few days,” Yue’er nodded.","“Then I’ll go pick some branches first.” Lin Yang said, then went to pick branches from the surrounding area and carried them back to the cave.","Yue’er cut off a piece of meat, placed it on a rack over the fire, and roasted it with skilled and natural movements. Lin Yang watched with wide eyes, somewhat incredulous.","“Do you often roast meat? You look very skilled,” he asked, looking at her.","“I learned it after a long time! My master said that I must learn the skills to survive on my own, so not only can I roast meat, but I can also start a fire without a fire striker by rubbing two pieces of wood together!” She said with a smile and added some branches to the fire.","“You’re so amazing, even though you’re younger than me...” he said in a daze.","“My senior brother and second senior brother are even more amazing,” she said, lifting her small face with a proud look on it. When she was outside and talking to people she wasn’t familiar with, she remembered her master’s words and referred to Big Brother and Brother as senior brother and second senior brother.","“Who is your master? Where do you live? Where are you going after you leave here?” Lin Yang asked.","“After I leave here, I will naturally return to the mountains. As for who my master is, my master said that I cannot use his name to show off.” She stuck out her tongue and said with a smile, “So, I can’t say, I can’t say.”","Hearing this, Lin Yang hugged his knees, rested his chin on his knees, looked at the fire and said softly, “After I leave this forest, I will go find my grandfather. Once I find him, I will be safe.”","Yue’er looked at him, blinked her eyes and said, “Someone wants to kill you. Does he know that you are going to find your grandfather? If he does, then aren’t you in danger too?”"]},{"number":4720,"title":"Chapter 4720: Vigilance","paragraphs":["Chapter 4720: Vigilance","Hearing this, Lin Yang was taken aback and said uncertainly, “It shouldn’t be, right?”","Yue’er thought about it seriously and said, “Unless the person who wants to kill you doesn’t know where your grandfather is, otherwise they would know that you would go to find him and would definitely intercept and kill you on the way.”","For a moment, Lin Yang didn’t say anything, just stared at her and asked, “How do you think the person who wants to kill me would intercept me on my way to my grandfather’s house? You’re so young, how could you think of that?”","“Hee hee, because my mother taught me! My mother said that when you encounter something, you have to use your brain. If you don’t use your brain, sometimes you won’t even know how you died.”","Thinking of her mother, a happy smile appeared on her little face: “My mother is a very powerful person. She taught me many things. Although I haven’t learned everything yet, my mother said that I am very smart and will learn everything slowly on my own.”","Lin Yang was silent, lost in thought. He didn’t say anything, just stared blankly at the fire.","Next, Yue’er spent three days collecting 100 crystal cores. When she had collected all 100, she couldn’t help but take out the communication jade to send a message to her two brothers, telling them that she had collected all 100 crystal cores and was ready to leave.","That day, Yue’er took Lin Yang to the small path leading out of the forest. When they passed the water source, she called out to Lin Yang to wait nearby while she went to change her clothes and wash her face.","At the small spring by the water source, she changed out of her clothes and put on a pink dress. After wiping her body, she washed her hair, dried it, and braided it into two pigtails.","“Lin Yang, I’m ready. Go change your clothes too!” Yue’er called out, walking out with quick steps and a smile on her face.","Lin Yang looked back and saw that she looked refreshed after washing herself. She looked very pretty, especially in the pink dress, which made her look cute and innocent, with no trace of the fierceness she had shown when she killed the fierce beast.","“I... I don’t have any clothes, only the ones I’m wearing.”He looked down at his dirty clothes, which were so dirty that their original colors were unrecognizable, and fidgeted with the corners of his clothes, feeling a little uncomfortable.","“Hee hee, I didn’t tell you to wear your own clothes.” Yue’er smiled slyly, took out a set of her clothes from her space, and said, “My mother prepared a lot of clothes for me, including clothes for every year. Here, you can wear this one.”","“That’s a skirt. I’m a boy, how can I wear that?!” He shook his head and waved his hands violently.","“Don’t you want to live?” Yue’er looked at him and said seriously, “If you go out wearing those clothes, you’ll definitely be killed before you find your grandfather. But if you dress up as a girl, it’s not certain. Those who want to kill you will only look for little boys, not little girls.”","“What?” He stared at her, not expecting her to give him such an idea.","“Hurry up and put it on! Once you leave here, pretend to be a girl until you find your grandfather.”","Yue’er stared at him with her beautiful eyes, trying hard to look serious so that he wouldn’t notice that she actually wanted to see what boys looked like in dresses before coming up with this idea.","Hearing this, Lin Yang paused for a moment before taking the clothes from her and walking to the water source to change..."]},{"number":4721,"title":"Chapter 4721: First","paragraphs":["Chapter 4721: First","After a while, Lin Yang, who had changed into girls’ clothes, came out a little embarrassed. He walked while pulling at his skirt, his little face slightly red, looking shy.","“Hey? You look pretty good in girls’ clothes!” Yue’er’s eyes lit up, and she looked at him with a smile.","“But, but I feel weird.” He tugged at the skirt and looked at the beautiful sky blue dress, feeling indescribable emotions in his heart.","“No, no, it’s fine. Let me help you tie your hair.” Yue’er walked towards him with a smile and took out a ribbon of the same color to tie his hair. Since she was helping someone else, she didn’t braid his hair, but let it fall down, half covering his face, making him look even more like a girl.","Yue’er led him down a small path, and it took them most of the day to get out of the forest. When they reached the mountain road outside, Yue’er looked around and saw that there was no one around, so she said to him, “Let’s hurry up and go! Let’s see if we can find a place to stay before it gets dark.”","“Mmm? Oh, alright.” Lin Yang had just responded when he saw her speed up, startling him so much that he hurriedly lifted his skirt and ran after her.","At the same time, Hao’er and Muchen, who were still in the forest, received Yue’er’s message. They were taken aback for a moment, then smiled.","They didn’t expect that the fastest of the three was their sister. They didn’t know how she managed to collect all the crystal cores so quickly.","Thinking that she had already left the forest, they began to take stock of their achievements over the past few days. Muchen counted and saw that he was still thirteen crystal cores short of a hundred. Seeing that it was not yet dark, he put the crystal cores away and walked into the forest, preparing to see if he could hunt a few more before nightfall, then hunt some more tomorrow, so that he could leave this place the day after tomorrow at the latest.","Hao’er was still far behind, because he needed 300 crystal cores. Even though he had worked very hard these past few days, he was still 60 to 70 crystal cores short. Similarly, seeing that it was still light out, he also went into the forest to continue hunting fierce beasts. He even thought to himself that he could try to hunt some beasts that came out to hunt at night.","The fierce beasts in his area were of a higher grade, with most of them being at the Sacred Beast level. Over the past few days, the beasts in this large area had become increasingly scarce. He thought that after finishing hunting today, he would have to find another place tomorrow.","What he didn’t know was that a group of disciples from a sect were also training in this area under the guidance of their sect elders. However, as they walked through the forest, they were somewhat surprised.","“Strange, why are there so few beasts in this area? Moreover, there seem to be traces of battle around here,” said a middle-aged man leading the group. He looked at the elder beside him and said, “Third Elder, should we change locations?”","“Let’s walk around some more. Perhaps a family with experience has been here,” said the elder, pausing in his footsteps as he heard the faint roars of beasts coming from the forest.","“There are beast roars. Should we go take a look?” asked the middle-aged man.","“We sent the disciples here to gain experience, so let them go investigate.” The elder turned around and looked at the two disciples behind him, saying, “The two of you go check out the situation ahead. No matter what you see, don’t alarm anyone. Come back and report.”"]},{"number":4722,"title":"Chapter 4722: Frightened","paragraphs":["Chapter 4722: Frightened","“Yes.” The two young disciples responded and rushed forward.","“Rest here!” the elder said to the others.","The two young disciples followed the sound and felt a rush of air before they got close. They glanced at each other and hid behind a large tree before looking forward. What they saw startled them so much that they forgot to hide and even forgot the elder’s orders. They flew forward and cried out in alarm.","“Be careful!”","Hao’er, who was about to attack, glanced at the source of the voice and frowned. He saw the fierce beast at the peak of the sacred beast realm rushing towards him fiercely. He twisted the dagger in his hand, shifted his feet, and immediately rushed forward.","His speed was extremely fast, and the dagger stabbed right at the fatal point of the sacred beast. With his exquisite footwork and precise and strange moves, he hit the fierce beast with one strike. There was a loud roar that shook the entire forest.","“No! That’s a peak sacred beast! They’re in danger!” The elders sensed the fluctuation of pressure and feared that their disciples had angered the fierce beast, so they immediately gathered their energy and rushed toward the sound.","Those who had entered their sect were all disciples from century-old families. This outing was meant to broaden their horizons and give them some practical experience, as they had little opportunity to do so while staying in the sect. However, the prerequisite for this outing was that they had to ensure the safety of their disciples. If anything happened, there would be trouble, as the families behind each disciple were not to be trifled with.","When they arrived at the source of the sound, they saw their two disciples standing motionless to the side. In front of them, a powerful fierce beast was lying on the ground, twitching and gasping for breath. Next to the beast, a small boy dressed in powerful armor was holding a dagger and stabbing the beast repeatedly. Only after the beast was dead did he skillfully dig out its crystal core and inner core.","Even the elder and the middle-aged man were stunned for a moment when they saw this scene. It took them a while to recover, and after watching the little boy put the items away, the elder finally looked at the two young disciples and asked, “What’s going on? Are you guys alright?”","“We’re fine,” the two said after recovering, but their astonished gazes were still fixed on the little boy.","“Elder, there’s no one else around, only this child,” the middle-aged man said in a low voice. He had just released his divine sense to scan the surroundings and found that apart from them, there was only this child. He didn’t seem to see any adults around the child.","Hearing this, the elder took a deep breath, walked forward, and asked, “Child, who are you? How did you get here?”","Hao’er looked at the horns on the head of the fierce beast, preparing to use his dagger to cut them off and take them to the city to exchange for money. When he heard the old man’s voice, he glanced at him, then glanced at the people beside him and behind him, frowned, and said with a cold expression, “Stay away from me.”","Hearing this, everyone was taken aback. They didn’t expect the child to say something like that.","“We are from the Heaven’s Sun Sect. Don’t be afraid, we mean you no harm.” The middle-aged man tugged at the corners of his mouth and smiled, trying hard to look more affable."]},{"number":4723,"title":"Chapter 4723: Lost in thought","paragraphs":["Chapter 4723: Lost in thought","Hao’er was somewhat aloof by nature, and he didn’t have a good impression of the Heaven’s Sun Sect, so he said, “I don’t want to know who you are, nor do I want to get to know you. Stay away from me and don’t bother me.”","Hearing such words from a child, the young disciples’ faces betrayed a hint of displeasure. After all, they were all scions of prominent families and the pride of their sect—how could they tolerate such disrespect from a child?","Just as they were about to scold him, their elder spoke up, and everyone immediately held their tongues.","“He he, child, did you kill this fierce beast?” The elder asked with a smile, his gaze falling on the fatal wound of the beast. “I wonder who your master is? There are many connections between sects and families, so it’s possible that your master and I are old acquaintances.”","Hearing this, Hao’er ignored him. An old friend of his master? Did that mean they knew each other? What a joke.","Who was his master? He was someone that even the great immortals of the Upper Immortal Realm had to bow and smile at. How could he be an old friend of an elder from a sect?","Moreover, they weren’t even in the same league. However, if he brought up his master’s title, even if these people hadn’t seen him, they would have heard of his name.","However, his master had also said that he shouldn’t use his name to scare people unless it was absolutely necessary.","Hao’er cut off the two horns with his dagger, thinking to himself. These days, it was rare to hunt a beast at the peak of the sacred beast realm, not to mention that this one, apart from its two valuable horns, would also fetch a good price for its skin. However, skinning it would be too much trouble.","After cutting off the two horns, he cut off one of the fierce beast’s hind legs, preparing to roast it and eat it. After throwing everything into his space, he didn’t even glance at those people and walked away.","“This kid is too arrogant, he’s a little conceited,” said one of the disciples.","“He’s also very brave to dare to walk around here alone. Judging from his skilled movements, it seems like he’s done this hundreds of times,” said another disciple thoughtfully.","“That kid looks like he’s only about eleven years old. How can he be here alone? His parents must be very trusting. Aren’t they afraid he’ll encounter danger?” A young girl looked in the direction the child had left, her delicate little face unable to hide her concern.","At this moment, the two young disciples who had arrived first and were standing to the side took a deep breath and said, “You don’t know, this child is extremely fast. Just now, we thought he would be bitten to death by that fierce beast, but unexpectedly, in the blink of an eye, the fierce beast fell down. That was a peak-level sacred beast with astonishing fighting power, but we didn’t see how the child did it. When we came to our senses, he had already stabbed the fierce beast in its vital spot with a knife.”","Hearing this, everyone fell silent. Although they hadn’t seen it, they had just seen the child skillfully cut and extract the crystal core and inner core. His technique didn’t look like that of a novice, but rather that of a veteran.","“Could it be a powerful person who has regained his youth?” one disciple couldn’t help but speculate.","“No, that child’s bone age is indeed only around eleven, but he has already reached the Nascent Soul stage. He’s probably the son of some powerful family,” the elder said slowly, stroking his beard thoughtfully."]},{"number":4724,"title":"Chapter 4724: Surprise","paragraphs":["Chapter 4724: Surprise","“Elder, should we follow him?” asked one of the disciples.","The elder recovered and glanced at him, asking, “What are we going to do by following him?”","Hearing this, the disciple’s face turned slightly red, and he moved his mouth but didn’t dare to speak.","“Elder, look at the meat of this fierce beast...” The middle-aged man looked at him and smiled expectantly.","“It’s fresh and just killed, and it’s a fierce beast at the peak of the sacred beast level. Have the disciples carry it away and prepare it for dinner!” The elder said, looking in the direction the child had left, and sighed softly, “What an outstanding child. I wonder whose disciple he is?”","Hearing the elder’s words, everyone picked up the fierce beast and carried it away, finding a place to roast it for dinner.","On the other side, Hao’er saw that it was not yet dark, so he searched for a while longer and finally killed three more first-level sacred beasts before returning to the cave to rest.","He roasted the meat in the cave and ate it, rested for a while, and watched as the sky darkened. He faintly heard a beast roar outside, so he got up and went out.","Although it was best to hunt beasts during the day, as his vision was better, he had to learn to adapt to the darkness and hunt in the dark, so he decided to give it a try.","He knew very well that there should be some second-level sacred beasts in this area, so the danger was relatively low.","Not far from Hao’er, the people from the sect were resting when they suddenly heard a noise coming from the forest. They were so startled that they jumped to their feet.","“No way! Who would be out hunting beasts at this time of night? Could it be that kid from earlier today?” One of the disciples muttered with wide eyes.","“There’s only him in this area besides us, so it’s obvious that it’s him,” said another young man with a slight sigh. “It really makes you realize how inferior you are compared to others. You’re both human, so how come that kid is so much stronger than us? He’s really brave to dare to come in here alone. If it were me, I wouldn’t dare even if you paid me.”","“Listen, listen, there’s another fierce beast’s cry. Tsk, tsk, this kid is something else!” Another young man said curiously, listening to the fierce beast’s cry echoing in the night, his heart filled with curiosity about the kid.","“Enough, everyone hurry up and rest.” The middle-aged man scolded, then walked around with his hands behind his back, suppressing the urge to go and take a look. He came to the elder’s side and sat down.","They spent the night listening to the faint roars of beasts. Surprisingly, apart from the noise over there, there was not a sound on their side. They had been worried that the smell of blood would attract other fierce beasts, but they waited until dawn and did not see a single beast attack them.","By dawn, Hao’er had already gone to another area. There were no more beasts in this area, and even if there were any that had slipped through the net, they had been scared away and didn’t dare to stay in this area. He couldn’t catch anything here anymore, so he had no choice but to move on.","When the Heaven’s Sun Sect disciples woke up the next day, they felt that the forest in this area seemed quieter for some unknown reason. They didn’t hear a single beast roar, and that feeling made them feel uneasy.","“Why is it so quiet? Could it be that those fierce beasts were all killed by that little pervert?” a young disciple couldn’t help but say."]},{"number":4725,"title":"Chapter 4725: Parting Ways","paragraphs":["Chapter 4725: Parting Ways","Hearing this, many people’s expressions changed slightly. One of them said, “That shouldn’t be possible. This place is so big, how could a child hunt down all the fierce beasts in this area? It’s impossible.”","However, they continued walking forward and even spread out to search the surrounding area, releasing their divine sense. In the end, they came to the conclusion that there really wasn’t a single fierce beast in the entire area.","“What a little freak, he actually killed all the fierce beasts in this area?” The middle-aged man leading the group couldn’t help but say, looking at the elder and asking, “Should we go north and take a look?”","The elder pondered for a long time and said, “There’s no other choice, let’s go!”","So, everyone headed north...","The next evening, when Muchen saw that he had enough crystal cores, he tidied up, sent a message to his Big Brother, and left the forest alone.","At this time, on the other side, Yue’er and Lin Yang had also arrived at a small town. Looking at Lin Yang, who was panting heavily beside her, Yue’er smiled and said, “You need to practice more. You can’t even run as fast as me! If someone wants to kill you, you won’t be able to escape at that speed.”","Lin Yang took a breath, wiped the sweat from his forehead with his sleeve, and explained that he had been rushing nonstop and had been chasing her the entire way, which made him even more exhausted.","“Yes, you’re too fast.” He was already considered fast among his peers, but compared to her, he was left in the dust in an instant. However, after spending the last few days with her, he knew that she was not only fast, but also had amazing fighting skills. He couldn’t treat her like a normal child.","“Hehe, let’s go eat something first! It’s getting dark. Let’s find a place to rest for tonight, and we can go our separate ways tomorrow.” She said with a smile, “I want to be the first one back to the mountain. The first one back gets a reward.”","Lin Yang followed her to the small town. After finding a place to eat, the two went to an inn to rest. Early the next morning, Yue’er was eating hot meat buns when she saw Lin Yang walking over.","“Yun Qi, I have to go. Will we see each other again?” Lin Yang looked at her, his little face filled with reluctance.","Yue’er shook her head and said, “I don’t know, but I don’t think we’ll have much chance to meet again because my master doesn’t usually let us go down the mountain.” As she spoke, she ate the buns, her cheeks puffed out like a little squirrel, and she looked at him and asked, “Do you want a bun? I’ll treat you, or you can take it with you for the road.”","As soon as she finished speaking, she looked around and called the waiter to pack two baskets of buns and handed them to him. “Here, take these! You must live well and don’t die. Remember what I told you.”","Lin Yang looked down at the bag of buns she had handed him, his eyes slightly reddened. “Yes, I will. I will definitely live on, and I will never forget what you said.” He sniffed and said, “Then I’ll be going. Take care of yourself.”","“Yeah.” Yue’er seemed heartless, without a trace of reluctance, still smiling at him.","After he left, looking back every few steps, Yue’er asked the waiter to pack two more steamed buns, paid, and walked out, preparing to take a look around town to see if there was anything she could buy before continuing on her way."]},{"number":4726,"title":"Chapter 4726: Interesting","paragraphs":["Chapter 4726: Interesting","She asked the waiter in the morning and found out the distance. Calculating her walking speed, if nothing unexpected happened, she could walk back to Yunxiao Mountain in ten days.","She wasn’t worried about Lin Yang because she had told him to hire some mercenaries in town to protect him on the road, which would naturally make him much safer.","Humming a tune, she strolled through the small town with light steps. She bought some food to store in her spatial pocket and some seeds. By midday, she finally left the town and headed toward the mountain path.","“Little girl, where did you come from? Why are you alone? Where are your parents?” Several wandering cultivators riding their contract beasts leisurely along the mountain road saw a little girl and couldn’t help but be surprised.","Yue’er looked up at them, revealing an innocent and harmless smile, and said mysteriously, “I’m not alone!”","Hearing this, the few cultivators were taken aback. They glanced at each other and looked around, but they thought there were shadow guards following them in the dark. However, they didn’t find anything. When they looked back at the little girl, she had already picked a fruit and was eating it as she walked.","“Little girl, where are you going? Come on, we’ll give you a ride,” said one of the cultivators with a smile as he bent down and reached out his hand to her.","“No, I’ll walk back myself,” said Yue’er, shaking her head and continuing on her way.","Hearing this, the wandering cultivator laughed loudly, “How far can a little girl like you go? Besides, there are three roads leading out of this town, and it takes a whole day to reach the next town on foot. You can’t walk that far.”","Yue’er finished the fruit in a few bites, took out a small handkerchief and carefully wiped her mouth. She put the handkerchief away, looked up and smiled at the group, “I’m leaving, uncles, goodbye.”","With that, she waved her small hand at the group, and in the next moment, her spirit energy rose, and she began to move quickly. In the blink of an eye, she was a hundred meters away.","“This...”","The few loose cultivators riding their contract beasts were taken aback, somewhat stunned: “This little girl is hiding her true abilities!”","“What an interesting little girl, let’s go! Let’s chase after her and ask who she is.” A man laughed loudly, looking with interest at the small figure in front of him that was getting farther and farther away, and called his mount to quickly chase after her.","“Hahaha, you’re right, let’s go, let’s go and see.” The few loose cultivators laughed and hurriedly rode their mounts to follow.","They were idle people who traveled around without constraints. The difference was that they were not loose cultivators without a family, but loose cultivators who had left their families to travel and see the world. Naturally, they didn’t have to worry about cultivation resources and could do whatever they wanted.","Yue’er walked with the footwork her mother had taught her, and her speed was naturally fast. After a while, she changed to the steps her master had taught her and began to glide forward, her feet barely touching the ground, only occasionally using her toes to tap and push forward.","She was fast and she did it effortlessly. She thought that her master had told them to walk back on their own so that they could practice their footwork more.","Noticing the commotion behind her, she turned to look. Seeing the few loose cultivators riding their contract beasts, her beautiful eyes flickered with surprise, as if she hadn’t expected them to follow her."]},{"number":4727,"title":"Chapter 4727: Can’t Shake Them Off","paragraphs":["Chapter 4727: Can’t Shake Them Off","“Hey, little girl, wait for us!” A loose cultivator waved at her with a friendly smile. “It’s a long way to go, so let’s chat for a bit.”","“Little girl, where did you come from? Your footwork is truly exquisite. Who is your master?” Another loose cultivator asked, surprise evident in his voice as he stared intently at her swift and constantly changing steps. He was frankly astonished; this young girl was so incredibly fast that he couldn’t even discern how her footwork flowed or transitioned.","“This little girl is no ordinary girl!” exclaimed a third. “All of us almost missed her entirely. Tell us, who is your master? And what is the name of your impressive footwork?”","Yue’er, the subject of their curiosity, simply glanced at them with a playful smile, a hint of mischief sparkling in her eyes. “I won’t tell you~” she declared cheekily.","As she spoke, she suddenly accelerated, her speed increasing even more dramatically than before. In the blink of an eye, she had effortlessly pulled away from them. She even turned back, her small frame silhouetted against the horizon, and made a funny face at them. They were so utterly stunned by her sudden burst of speed and playful taunt that they stood frozen for a moment. Then, she shot forward again, moving so rapidly that she appeared to be almost flying on a sword, leaving them trailing far behind.","“Tsk, tsk, her footwork is truly exquisite,” remarked one of the lone cultivators, a glint flashing in his eyes and a satisfied smile spreading across his lips. “I can’t even guarantee that I could catch up with her if we were to compete solely on footwork. I genuinely want to discover where this little girl came from. Who is her master? She’s so young, yet so incredibly powerful!”","As soon as he finished speaking, he gathered his energy, sweeping his sleeves to pull his mount back into his spatial storage. Then, with a surge of power, he swiftly chased after the small, receding figure in front of him. This was Shen Seventeen, a formidable and determined cultivator, now fully engaged in the pursuit.","“It seems that Shen Shiqi is serious,” another cultivator noted with a grin. “Well, I have nothing else pressing to do, so let’s follow and see what unfolds!” This individual, equally intrigued, also put away his contract beast, a loyal magical creature he had bonded with, and gathered his energy to join the chase.","When it came to footwork alone, they naturally couldn’t match the little girl’s unparalleled precision and agility. However, they possessed the significant advantage of higher cultivation levels, which meant they were ultimately faster than her in raw speed. In no time at all, the few of them caught up to the young girl. Yet, they didn’t overtake her. Instead, they cleverly positioned themselves to stay right by her side, watching her closely and examining her with newfound scrutiny.","As they observed her, a hint of genuine surprise flashed across their eyes. Earlier, they hadn’t paid much attention to her specific features, only noticing that the young girl was undeniably cute and pretty. But now, upon closer inspection, they realized something astonishing: her appearance had been subtly altered. Someone must have cast a powerful spell to hide her true face. The cute and pretty face she now presented might very well not be her real appearance at all.","The entire group was astonished by this revelation. It seemed this young girl had a significant background and was far more mysterious than they initially thought. After all, ordinary people wouldn’t resort to using such complex secret techniques to conceal their appearance. Furthermore, the person who had cast the spell must be exceptionally powerful—only cultivators of considerable skill could discern that her current appearance wasn’t her true form.","Yue’er, now caught up by the persistent group, felt her small face wrinkle in annoyance. She glared at them, a clear look of exhaustion and helplessness in her eyes. Their strength was far greater than hers, and they would definitely not be slower than her. But did these people truly have nothing better to do with their time? Why were they so determined to follow her?","“Little girl, come talk to us!” one of them cajoled, a playful tone in his voice.","“Hahaha, little girl, what’s your name?” another chimed in, equally amused by her predicament.","“Hehe, look at her,” a third grinned, observing her “bitter” expression. “This little girl with a bitter look on her face, she looks so helpless, how funny.” As he looked at her plump, pink little face, he felt an almost irresistible urge to reach out and gently poke her cheek.","Hearing the people around her asking questions non-stop, their voices a continuous stream, Yue’er’s heart stirred, and she suddenly stopped ."]},{"number":4728,"title":"Chapter 4728: Little Fox","paragraphs":["Chapter 4728: Little Fox","“Why have you stopped? Are you tired and need to rest?” one of the men asked with a smile, stopping his pursuit as well.","“What are you following me for?” Yue’er frowned, walking to the grassy verge by the side of the road and sitting down. She then pulled buns from her spatial storage to eat. Spirit energy was very consuming, making her hungry, especially given her young age.","Seeing her eating the meat buns, the men smiled. “We are idle cultivators,” one explained. “We usually just travel around and have nothing particular to do. We happened to come across such an interesting little girl, so we decided to keep you company so you won’t be bored on your journey.”","Hearing this, Yue’er continued eating her bun and didn’t respond, merely looking at them with her beautiful, large eyes.","“Little girl, what’s your name? It’s alright to tell us, right?” one of them asked with a smile.","After swallowing her bun, Yue’er slowly replied, “It doesn’t really matter if I tell you my name, but you don’t look like good people. My mother told me that when I’m out, I shouldn’t tell strangers my name.”","Hearing this, the group paused for a moment, exchanged glances, and then, with strange expressions, one of them asked, “Do we look like bad people?”","“Bad people don’t write it on their faces,” Yue’er continued, glancing at them. “Besides, you’ve been following me. It’s very suspicious. You’re not kidnapping children, are you?” As she spoke, a hint of genuine fear flickered across her small face.","“Hahahaha, you little girl, you’re really interesting!” The man named Shen Shiqi looked up and burst into laughter, clearly pleased. He said with great interest, “Don’t worry, we’re not bad people. My surname is Shen, and I’m the seventeenth child in my family, so my friends call me Shen Shiqi. Little girl, what’s your name?”","“Shiqi? Seventeen?” Yue’er blinked. “I have a bodyguard who is also called Seventeen.”","“Oh? It seems we have quite a connection,” he smiled, looking at her. “What about you? What’s your name? It’s alright to tell us, right?”","Yue’er stared at them for a moment, then thought about it. “My name is Yun Qi. My master named me.”","“Yun Qi? Hehe, see what I said? I told you we had a connection. I’m Shiqi, and you’re Little Qi.1” He smiled lightly, looking at her with a friendly and familiar expression. “Little Qi, what’s your master’s name?”","Yue’er glanced at him, stuffed another bun into her mouth, shook her head, and said, “I can’t just tell you my master’s name. It would scare you to death.” They wanted to find out her master’s name? She wasn’t going to tell them!","When the others heard this, they looked at each other and chuckled. One of them said, “It’s alright, we’re very brave and won’t be easily scared. Who knows, maybe we even know your master!”","Yue’er ate several buns in a row. Seeing that there were only a few left, she put them away, stood up, glanced at them, and said with a smile, “I’m not a three-year-old child. I said I won’t tell you, so I won’t tell you. It’s useless to coax me!”","As soon as she finished speaking, she darted several meters away, made a funny face at them, and smiled slyly like a fox. “I’m leaving! You guys rest here for a while!”","Hearing this, the group suddenly had a very bad feeling..."]},{"number":4729,"title":"Chapter 4729: Choose","paragraphs":["When the cultivators saw the little girl dart away into the distance, they immediately raised their spirit energy to give chase. However, as they did so, a wave of dizziness washed over them, and their figures swayed precariously.","\"Is this the lowest grade of soft bone powder?\" one of them exclaimed, wide-eyed and seemingly unable to believe that the little girl had actually used poison on them while their guard was down.","Another person’s face darkened considerably. He quickly sat down cross-legged to regulate his qi, saying, \"How could it be the lowest grade of soft bone powder? That kind of poison has absolutely no effect on people with our cultivation level. This poison has been expertly refined by a true master.\"","The others also quickly sat down cross-legged, a grim realization dawning on them. Shen Shiqi sighed, shaking his head. \"How incredibly careless of us! When did that little girl manage to do it? How could none of us possibly notice anything?\"","\"What are you talking about? Hurry up and get the medicine out of your system, then catch up with that little girl and teach her a proper lesson!\" another cultivator urged, closing his eyes and regulating his breathing to forcefully expel the poison from his body.","Given their immense strength and high cultivation, it wouldn’t even take half an incense stick’s time—a short measure of time, typically around five to ten minutes—to force the medicine out and fully recover. Once they were back to their full strength, catching up with that little girl would only be a matter of time and a simple exercise in speed.","Originally, the cultivators were just bored and had been playfully teasing her, genuinely curious to follow her and inquire about her background. They wanted to know what kind of family she came from, how she could be so exceptionally well-taught at such a young age, or, more specifically, who her mysterious master was. They were simply fascinated that someone so young possessed such extraordinary footwork. Now, after experiencing the little girl’s cunning trick, their curiosity had transformed into a firm determination to catch her. They weren’t angry, but rather more intrigued than ever.","Yue’er, who had left first, waited until she could no longer see the distant figures of the cultivators before she finally let out a relieved breath and patted her chest. She knew she wasn’t as strong as them and certainly couldn’t outrun them in a straightforward chase, so she had to find a clever way to make them lose her. However, those few people seemed to be incredibly powerful. She hadn’t dared to use any overly potent drugs, fearing they might detect them immediately. Thus, she could only use colorless, odorless, and relatively mild drugs to buy herself some crucial time to escape.","\"They’ll definitely catch up with me,\" she muttered to herself, a flicker of worry in her eyes. \"If they do, I’ll be in big trouble.\" She kept running, employing her fastest and most intricate footwork, pushing herself to the very limit.","She continued until she came to an intersection up ahead, where she finally stopped.","There were two distinct roads before her: one that continued straight ahead, and another that branched off sharply to the left. Originally, she had planned to take the road straight ahead. However, turning left would lead her back to the small town she had passed earlier and then, eventually, to another road leading in a completely different direction. Choosing the left road would mean taking a significantly longer route to return to Yunxiao Mountain, which would undoubtedly cost her valuable time.","She bit her lip, her gaze flitting between the two diverging paths in front of her. She gritted her teeth, a fierce determination hardening her small face, and finally chose one of them.","Moments later, when the pursuing cultivators caught up and arrived at the same three-way intersection, they also came to a halt.","\"There are two roads here, which one will that little girl take?\" one of them pondered aloud.","\"She should go straight, right?\" another suggested, pointing to the road ahead. \"The road on the left is the way back, and that little girl probably won’t go back, so I think she should go straight ahead.\"","\"That’s true,\" Shen Shiqi mused, rubbing his chin thoughtfully. \"But that little girl is small but cunning, and she certainly can’t be treated like an ordinary child. You think she’ll go that way, but she might do the exact opposite, right?\"","The person next to him heard this and paused for a moment, a look of disbelief on his face, before responding, \"No way! How old is that little girl? How could she possibly think of so many twists and turns?\""]},{"number":4730,"title":"Chapter 4730: Tricks","paragraphs":["\"There are footprints on the ground! That little girl must have stopped here,\" one of the cultivators exclaimed, pointing to the distinct marks in the dirt. He chuckled, \"Look, these footprints are heading towards the road on the left. It seems that the little girl really did run that way.\"","\"Hahahaha, well, she’s so clever! But no matter what, she’s just a child, and she didn’t even think to wipe away her footprints, leaving us a perfect trail! Let’s go! We’ll chase after her and properly meet this little girl. It’s been a long time since we’ve encountered such an interesting little one.\" Shen Shiqi burst out laughing as he immediately chased after her as he took the path to the left.","At this exact moment, Yue’er was indeed on the road to the left, but she wasn’t running wildly along it. Instead, she had found a cleverly hidden spot, concealing her aura and watching from the shadows to see if those persistent cultivators were chasing her down this particular path.","After a while, when she saw the few men chatting and laughing as they effortlessly swept along the mountain path, heading directly toward the road she had seemingly taken, a triumphant smile involuntarily spread across her eyes. Her face lit up with a mischievous grin, like a cunning little fox .","She lay perfectly still, not moving a muscle, waiting until the figures of the cultivators were completely out of sight. Only then did she quickly get up, turn back, return to the three-way path, and head swiftly down the straight road. She was determined to be the first of her two brothers to return to the mountain, so taking the longer route was simply not an option. She had to deceive them first, create a diversion, and then double back.","Once she passed this straight road and reached the small town up ahead, the roads would split into multiple directions, making it significantly more difficult for them to catch up with her. Thinking of this, she quickened her pace even further. She knew that if they chased her for too long and didn’t find her, they might eventually realize what had happened.","While rushing back, Yue’er’s heart was pounding as if running for her life, feeling a mix of nervousness and exhilaration.","On the other side, after successfully leaving the dense forest, Muchen also followed a different mountain road. Relatively speaking, he hadn’t encountered anyone or any trouble during his travels. Additionally, he was typically a man of few words, so he didn’t mind not speaking for ten days or even half a month if it meant a peaceful journey.","Their master had deliberately abandoned them in different parts of the forest. Even if they all managed to get out, the three of them were expected to take different paths back to Yunxiao Mountain, ensuring there was no chance of them meeting each other along the way.","On the road, Muchen efficiently used the swift steps his mother had taught him to travel quickly. After walking for a while without seeing a soul, he gradually began to encounter other travelers. Some were wandering cultivators, gracefully flying with their swords or riding magnificent contract beasts, while others were seated comfortably within elaborate flying artifacts. There were even more people sitting in grand spirit beast carriages, accompanied by numerous guards and servants, giving them the appearance of members from a large, wealthy family traveling in luxury.","As it grew dark, one of the large spirit beast carriage convoys stopped to rest for the night. Muchen also decided to rest not far from them. He reasoned that by staying close to the well-protected spirit beast carriage convoy, he wouldn’t encounter any significant danger.","In one of the stopped spirit beast carriages, the elegant curtain was gently lifted by a pair of delicate hands. A beautiful woman, dressed as a noble lady, looked out at the darkening sky. She was about to lower the curtain when her gaze caught a fleeting glimpse of a small figure behind one of the spirit beasts. A look of surprise flashed across her eyes. She leaned closer to the window and glanced backward, only to confirm she had indeed seen a small child. She couldn’t help but pause for a moment, her curiosity piqued.","\"Take these pastries to that child,\" the beautiful woman said in a gentle voice, handing a plate of exquisitely prepared pastries to the maid serving her.","\"Yes,\" replied the maid, respectfully accepting the plate and carefully stepping out of the luxurious spirit beast carriage."]},{"number":4731,"title":"Chapter 4731: Good Intentions","paragraphs":["Muchen was sitting by the roadside, munching on a spirit fruit when he saw a young lady in a blue dress approach him.","\"Little boy, this is from my mistress.\" She squatted down, as she smiled and asked: \"Why are you here all alone? Where are your parents?\"","As she spoke, she handed him the pastry. \"Here, eat this!\"","Muchen glanced at the pastry in her hand and said, \"No, thank you.\"","\"It’s alright, my mistress is kind, just take it!\" The young girl said, looking at him and asking, \"Do you have any bag to put it in?\" The girl, however, insisted, explaining her mistress’s generosity and, seeing his reluctance to take it, decided to leave the plate of pastries with him, promising to retrieve it the following day. Muchen paid little attention to the offering, instead focusing on his spirit fruit before closing his eyes to rest.","Inside a nearby carriage, she recounted her meeting with the little boy. \"Madam, that child seems to be alone, with no adults around. I gave him some pastries, but he said he didn’t want them, so I left the plate there. I’ll go back and get it later,\" the maid said softly as she came to her side to help her boil tea and pour water.","Hearing this, the lady lifted the curtain and took a look, then said, \"Such a small child, his parents really trust him.\"","\"Madam, I think this child is very smart! He knows to follow our carriage, so at least he won’t run into any trouble.\" The maid said with a smile as she poured her a cup of tea and asked,","\"Madam, it’s not completely dark yet. Shall we get out and take a walk?\"","\"That’s a good idea. We’ve been sitting all day.\" The lady said, and with the help of the maid, she got out of the carriage.","She walked around for a while, then came to the little boy and looked at him sitting on the grass with his eyes closed, resting. She couldn’t help but smile gently.","\"Are you tired? Come rest in my carriage!\" Looking at this child who was only about five years old, pity flashed in her eyes: \"You’re so young, you’ll easily catch a cold sleeping here at night. There’s only me and a maid in my carriage. Why don’t you sleep in my carriage for the night?\"","Muchen opened his eyes and looked at her. Seeing her gentle expression and the soft look in her eyes, he was inexplicably reminded of his mother. Perhaps because of this, he softened his refusal a little and was no longer as stiff as before.","\"I’ll rest here.\"","Seeing this, the lady smiled and said to the maid beside her, \"Go ask the guards to set up a small tent.\"","\"Yes.\" The maid replied and left. Before long, she returned with a small tent.","\"This is for you! Since you don’t want to rest in my carriage, you can rest in the small tent so you won’t catch a cold at night.\" She smiled gently and said, \"Our convoy is going to Palatial City. If you’re going the same way, you can follow us! At least it will be safer.\"","Looking at the small tent, Muchen didn’t refuse. Instead, he stood up and bowed to her and said politely, \"Thank you.\"","Seeing this, the lady couldn’t help but smile, \"You’re welcome.\" With that, she turned and returned to the spirit beast carriage to rest.","After watching her leave, Muchen set up the small tent and crawled inside to rest. As night fell, the excessive silence in the air made Muchen, who had closed his eyes to sleep, open them again.","Understanding his reluctance, the mistress instructed her maid to set up a small tent for him. The maid promptly returned with a tent, which the mistress presented to Muchen, explaining it would protect him from the night cold if he preferred not to use her carriage. She also offered their convoy’s direction, Palatial City, suggesting he could follow them for safety if their paths aligned.","Muchen, seeing the tent, accepted the gesture. He stood up and bowed, expressing his gratitude. The mistress smiled, acknowledging his thanks before returning to her carriage. Once she was gone, Muchen set up the tent and entered it to rest. However, as night fully descended, the profound silence unsettled him, causing him to open his eyes once more."]},{"number":4732,"title":"Chapter 4732: Something Happened","paragraphs":["Despite his age, Muchen possessed an acute awareness of danger, honed by challenging experiences, particularly these ten days spent surviving in a forest alone. This instilled in him a cautious nature, preventing him from falling into deep sleep even at night.","On this particular night, the unusual silence – the complete absence of insect sounds – immediately alerted Muchen that something was amiss. He quietly exited his small tent and detected a faint, unsettling scent in the air. A quick glance around revealed that only four night watchmen were awake in the caravan, and they appeared listless and prone to yawning, suggesting they were affected by something. Muchen’s small face tightened; despite his lack of medical expertise, he instinctively knew the pervasive scent was wrong.","His gaze settled on the spirit beast carriage, and he quickly deduced that the lady inside was the intended target. His suspicions were confirmed when he witnessed a guard, ostensibly asleep by the fire, secretly throw something into the flames. This action intensified the strange aroma in the air, sending a chill down Muchen’s spine. He realized this was a joint effort to harm the lady, noting the complicit guard and the eerie silence of the surrounding natural environment, which indicated assassins were likely lurking nearby.","Logically, Muchen should have quietly retreated to avoid entanglement. However, memories of the lady’s kindness – her offering of pastries and the small tent, and her gentle gaze that reminded him of his own mother – made it impossible for him to abandon her. He moved stealthily under the cover of darkness towards the spirit beast carriage. Just as he was about to climb in, the night watchmen suddenly collapsed, and a signal flare whizzed into the night sky.","\"Hurry up and leave! Someone is trying to kill you!\" Muchen shouted as he quickly entered the carriage. Fortunately, its windows and doors were sealed, preventing the drug from fully permeating the interior. The sudden intrusion woke the lady and her maid.","The maid, startled, pulled back the curtain to peer outside. She gasped upon seeing over a dozen black-robed men rushing towards them and cried out, \"Madam, hurry up and leave! There are assassins!\"","The lady was also taken aback, seemingly caught off guard, but there was no panic on her face. Instead, she smiled gently and said to Muchen, \"Thank you, but don’t worry, everything will be fine.\"","She said softly, adjusted her clothes, and got out of the spirit beast carriage on her own. At the same time, she said to Muchen and the maid, \"Don’t get out, just stay in the carriage!\"","Muchen was taken aback for a moment, but seeing that she looked calm and unperturbed, he calmed down for some unknown reason. However, he did not stay in the spirit beast carriage, but followed her out and stood beside it.","\"Madam, wait for me, I’ll get down too.\" The maid said and followed her down, but she had only just gotten off the spirit beast carriage when she fainted from the smell in the air.","Muchen glanced at the maid, then looked at the lady, and finally calmed down.","\"The smell of tendon-binding flower. It seems you were prepared.\" The lady said softly, her gaze sweeping over the unconscious guards, the accomplice, and the dozen or so black-robed men who had appeared.","The lady calmly assessed the situation, her gaze sweeping over the unconscious guards, the treacherous accomplice, and the newly arrived black-robed assailants. \"The smell of tendon-binding flower,\" she mused softly, adding, \"It seems you were prepared.\"","The leader of the black-robed men, observing her standing unfazed without any signs of abnormality, expressed his surprise: \"You’re not unconscious?\""]},{"number":4733,"title":"Chapter 4733: Soul Search","paragraphs":["The lady raised her eyes and glanced at the man, asking, \"Who sent you to kill me?\"","\"Hah! Why don’t you go down to hell and ask!\" The leader sneered, and with a movement of his hand, a dozen black robed men rushed towards her.","As the killing intent surged from their bodies, a powerful aura spread through the air, the sharp, bloodthirsty energy whistling past like countless sharp knives.","\"Move aside,\" the lady said to Muchen. In the next moment, a spinning crescent knife appeared in her hand. When the crescent knife appeared in her hand, the leader of the black-robed men’s eyes narrowed.","\"Seven Star Crescent Knife! You, you’re a Moon Lover!\" The leader of the black-robed men cried out in shock, fear flashing in his eyes.","Muchen, who was standing nearby, heard the black-robed man’s words and couldn’t help but glance at the lady. He saw that her aura changed greatly when the crescent knife appeared in her hand. The gentleness disappeared from her expression, replaced by an intimidating killing intent.","The crescent moon blade in her hand flew out, spinning and slitting the throats of several black-robed men. Those men didn’t even have time to dodge before they stiffened and fell to the ground.","Her attack was extremely fast, and the spinning crescent moon blade was aimed at her opponents’ vital points, killing them with a single blow, clean and neat.","In the blink of an eye, half of the dozen black-robed men were dead. The remaining few didn’t dare to attack again. Instead, they retreated, thinking of retreating, but even they didn’t know if they could retreat safely and survive.","The reason was simple: the mysterious master of the Seven-Star Crescent Blade, Shiyue, had been famous for years but remained elusive, never revealing himself. Anyone who had seen him had died, so no one knew whether he was male or female, old or young.","They had accepted this mission thinking that they were only going to kill a noble lady from a family, but they never expected that it would be the mysterious existance of the Seven Star Crescent Blade, Shiyue!","Shiyue’s strength was such that even if their boss came, he might not be able to kill her.","\"Retreat! Quickly retreat!\" They were really doomed this time! At this moment, they didn’t even think about killing her, they just wanted to get back alive.","\"You want to leave? Don’t you know that everyone who has seen my Seven Star Crescent Blade is dead?\"","She revealed an inexplicable smile as she watched the group retreat. With a twist of her palm, the crescent blade flew out, and at the same time, she flew away, swooping toward the leader.","Muchen listened to her words, his eyelids twitching slightly, but he remained standing still, just watching her easily kill the dozen black robed men and the traitorous bodyguard with her overwhelming power, leaving only the leader, who had broken his jaw and crippled him, standing there. She then extended a finger and gently touched the man’s forehead.","Soul search!","Seeing that scene, the first thing that popped into his mind was the words \"soul search.\" A soul search could reveal everything in the mind of the person being searched, but it was an extreme technique that cultivators would not use lightly because after a soul search, the victim would suffer damage to their divine sense and become an idiot at best, or die outright at worst.","He watched silently, his gaze sweeping over the corpses on the ground, all of whom had been killed with a single blow. It could only be said that this lady’s strength was truly formidable. After all, these black-clad assassins were no pushovers."]},{"number":4734,"title":"Chapter 4734: Shiyue","paragraphs":["Chapter 4734: Shiyue","After a while, the last black robed man was also killed. The lady put away the seven-star crescent knife in her hand, lifted her skirt, and saw that it was not stained with blood. Only then did she smile with satisfaction.","She turned and walked back to Muchen, looked at him, and said softly, “Are you scared? Don’t be afraid, I don’t kill people often.”","Hearing this, Muchen’s tense face twitched imperceptibly. Don’t often kill people? She expects him to believe that? Even a fool wouldn’t believe that.","“The night is nice tonight, and we have nothing to do, so why don’t we chat?” The lady said with a smile and looked up at the night sky.","Muchen looked up. In the sky, dark clouds half-covered the moon, and a few stars twinkled faintly in the night. To be honest, it wasn’t a particularly beautiful night, not to mention that there were corpses all over the ground!","“Didn’t you say that everyone who saw your knife died? Why don’t you kill me?” Muchen asked, looking at the lady who slowly walked over and sat outside the spirit beast carriage.","“You won’t tell anyone, and besides, I told you, I don’t kill people often.” She smiled lightly and looked at him, asking, “You haven’t told me your name yet!”","Seeing that he was only looking at her without saying a word, with a hint of wariness in his eyes, she smiled gently and said, “My name is Qian Moyue. My husband is Xiao Zhenling, the second young master of the Xiao family. I also have another identity, which is the Mysterious Master of the Seven Star Crescent Blade, Shiyue. Even my husband doesn’t know about this identity. I didn’t expect a child like you to know.”","She smiled lightly and looked at Muchen, saying, “You’re not simple either, are you? At such a young age, you have such courage and wisdom. You must come from a prestigious family. And your little face is covered by a powerful disguise that hides your true appearance, making you seem mysterious.”","“I’ve told you all this, shouldn’t you tell me your name?” She looked at Muchen and waited for him to speak.","Upon hearing this, Muchen glanced at her, thought for a moment, and then said, “My name is Yun Yuan.”","“That’s it?”","“Yes, that’s it.” Muchen nodded and said.","Seeing this, she smiled and said, “Alright! Since you don’t want to say more, I won’t ask. However, if you’re going the same way, you might as well come to the carriage and keep me company. After all, it’s still a long way to go!”","She smiled lightly and said, “If you have time, why don’t you come with me to the Xiao family and stay for a few days?”","“No need,” said Muchen, “We’re not going the same way.”","“Alright! Then you go to the carriage with me and get some sleep. We’ll figure out what to do tomorrow.” With that, she carried the fainted maid back into the carriage and motioned for Muchen to get in as well.","“Are we just going to leave those bodies there? What about them? They’re still unconscious. Shouldn’t we do something?” Muchen asked, pausing for a moment.","“Just leave them there! We’ll deal with them tomorrow when they wake up.” She smiled and said, “In their eyes, I’m just the second wife of the Xiao family, not someone powerful. If I go and deal with them or wake them up, it will be even more troublesome to explain later. Let’s just leave them there! Tomorrow, when they wake up and ask, just say that we also fainted and don’t know anything.”","Hearing this, Muchen nodded and replied, “Mm.”","To avoid trouble, he also got into the car to rest, and woke up the next morning amid cries and chaos."]},{"number":4735,"title":"Chapter 4735: Intercept","paragraphs":["Chapter 4735: Intercept","He sat in the spirit beast carriage, listening to the lady outside talking to her guards. She was probably saying that black robed men had attacked in the middle of the night, and she had gotten out of the carriage to check, only to find that a mysterious master had saved them. However, she had fallen into a deep sleep for some unknown reason and didn’t know what had happened after that.","Perhaps because there were no losses and the black-clothed assassins were all dead, the guards disposed of the bodies on the ground and prepared to continue their journey.","Muchen got out of the spirit beast carriage and bowed to the lady, saying, “Thank you for your kindness, but I have to leave and cannot accompany you.”","Seeing this, the lady just looked at him and said, “Be careful on your way, and we’ll see you again someday.”","“Mm.” Muchen replied, glanced at her, and then quickly left on his own.","Watching the child leave, the maid couldn’t help but say, “Lady, that child’s footwork looks very exquisite, and he’s very fast. I don’t think it would be easy for us to catch up with him!”","“Mm, that child is not a simple person.” The lady smiled, a hint of pleasure appearing on her lips. “I didn’t expect to meet such an interesting child on this trip. It’s just a pity that we didn’t have much time together.”","“Perhaps you will meet him again in the future?” The maid smiled and said, “Madam, please sleep a little longer. I will wake you when we reach the next rest stop.”","“Mm.” The lady replied and rested in the spirit beast carriage.","The convoy moved forward slowly. Because of what happened last night, everyone was on high alert today, not daring to be the slightest bit careless or relax...","A few days later, Hao’er finally gathered all the crystal cores in the forest. After sending a message to his younger brother and sister, he also set off to find the way out of the forest.","However, just as he was about to leave the forest, he was stopped by a group of mercenaries.","“Hehe, kid, you must have gotten a lot of crystal cores these past few days, right? Hand them over and call us Grandfather, and we’ll let you go.” A man with a large sword on his shoulder revealed a greedy look and stared at Hao’er with a wicked gaze.","Hao’er stopped in his tracks, his small face expressionless, without a hint of fear. He turned slightly to the side and glanced at the Heaven’s Sun Sect members that had been following him. Seeing that they were hiding behind the trees and did not seem to be planning to show themselves, his heart stirred and his mind raced.","Behind them, the hidden group watched the scene unfold in front of them. Some of the disciples looked slightly moved, as if they couldn’t bear to watch, but most of them looked like they were enjoying the show.","“Elder, are we really not going to help? He’s so small, he definitely can’t beat that group of mercenaries. He got those crystal cores by hunting fierce beasts, and these mercenaries are even picking up a child’s crystal cores. This is really too much!” a young girl whispered, her eyes filled with indignation and injustice.","The elder stroked his beard, narrowed his eyes, and said slowly, “What is there to help? Have you forgotten how abnormal this kid is?! He hunted down almost all the fierce beasts in the forest. Now those people are looking for trouble with him, what does that have to do with us? You must understand that he is not a disciple of our sect, so he is not under our protection.”","Hearing this, the young girl couldn’t say a word and could only feel anxious."]},{"number":4736,"title":"Chapter 4736: A Tough Nut to Crack","paragraphs":["Chapter 4736: A Tough Nut to Crack","The world is vast, and the strong prey on the weak—it is an unchanging truth. Such acts of robbery were not unprecedented, nor were they the first time they had witnessed such a scene. Yet, upon seeing it now, they still felt an inexplicable sense of urgency.","After all, in her eyes, no matter how skilled the child might be, he would not be a match for those few individuals. However, as the elder had said, he was not a disciple of their sect, and thus was not under their protection.","“However, if he is willing to give us half of his crystal core, we might be able to help him,” said the elder, narrowing his eyes.","Hearing this, the young girl was taken aback and immediately stepped forward and shouted, “Hey, kid, our elder said that if you give him half of your crystal core as a reward, he will protect you and let you leave safely.”","“What nonsense!” The elder glared at the young girl in embarrassment and said, “Come back, don’t meddle in other people’s business!” He did want the crystal core, but he couldn’t just take it like that. Otherwise, if he took the child’s crystal core today, his reputation would naturally be damaged tomorrow. What’s more, he didn’t know what sect this child belonged to, so why would he meddle in other people’s business?","Hao’er glanced back without saying a word, just holding the dagger in his hand and looking at the two or thirty mercenaries in front of him: “If you want to die, come over here!”","“Hahahaha! What a big mouth!”","Seeing this, the mercenaries couldn’t help but look up and laugh loudly. One of them rolled up his sleeves, stepped forward, glanced contemptuously at the small Hao’er, and said, “I think you’re the one who wants to live too long. Even if you’re good at hunting fierce beasts, you want to fight us? You’re still too young!”","As soon as he finished speaking, he took a step forward and grabbed Hao’er with his big hand, “Let me see how strong you really are!”","Hao’er stared at his movements and saw his big hand reaching for his collar. A cold look flashed in his eyes, and in the next moment, he moved instantly and slashed upward with the dagger in his hand.","A sharp cold light refracted, and a fierce air blade accompanied by a whistling sound and the mercenary’s scream rang out.","“Arghhhh! My hand!!!!”","The mercenary staggered backward, clutching his bleeding wrist, which was still twitching slightly.","The smell of blood filled the air, and the mercenaries who smelled it and saw the scene were filled with a murderous intent.","The leader of the mercenaries stared at Hao’er and said coldly, “I told you all, this little brat has some skills, don’t underestimate him, but you wouldn’t listen.”","The mercenaries stared at Hao’er, becoming more and more angry the longer they looked at him. “Who would have thought that such a little brat would have such skills?”","“You two go up there and be careful. I don’t believe it. It doesn’t take so many of us to deal with a little brat.”","“Yes!”","The two mercenaries who were motioned forward responded with a look of excitement on their faces. He stared at Hao’er and said with a hint of eeriness in his voice, “The skin on this kid’s body should be tender. I wonder if we can tear off his hands and feet first without killing him?”","“He’s just a little brat, what can he do? Watch me, I’ll catch him in three moves!”","As soon as he finished speaking, he quickly struck Hao’er with a fierce palm strike, and under the palm strike, a hidden weapon flew out with a whistling sound."]},{"number":4737,"title":"Chapter 4737: Escape","paragraphs":["Chapter 4737: Escape","Seeing this, Hao’er’s eyes flashed slightly. These mercenaries were not weak. He had only been able to kill them when they were off guard. Once they became alert, he would have no chance to strike again.","If he couldn’t beat them, he had no choice but to run.","So, when he saw them strike at him with a palm and throw hidden weapons, he immediately dodged, quickly darting ten metres away. He paused for a moment, glanced at the mercenaries and the Heaven’s Sun Sect disciples who were watching the spectacle, and in the next moment, changed the direction he had originally planned to take out of the forest and turned around, quickly darting into the depths of the forest.","“Chase him!”","Seeing this, the mercenaries let out a fierce cry and quickly gave chase.","After they left, the people from the sect also came out. The elder and the middle-aged man watched the scene and shook their heads slightly. “What a pity, that child will not survive.”","Those mercenaries were people who had been on missions in forests like this for many years. They were skilled and accustomed to fighting in the jungle. No matter how clever that child was, it would be difficult for him to survive at their hands.","“Let’s go!” The elder turned around and led the disciples inside the gate in another direction.","Some disciples looked back with pity in their eyes, but they didn’t say anything and just quietly followed.","On the other side, Hao’er led them deeper into the forest. He darted ahead, his small figure shuttling between the trees like a shadow that couldn’t be caught.","“That little brat is really fast! When I catch him, I’ll skin him alive!” One of the mercenaries cursed as he swiftly darted through the forest.","They were people who lived in this forest, and in a forest where they had to avoid trees, their speed was considered extremely fast. However, now they were being left behind by that little brat, which was really infuriating.","“This kid seems to be leading us deeper into the forest. What the hell is he up to?” The leader of the mercenaries said with some confusion, feeling that something was wrong.","“What can he do? He’s just a kid. What kind of tricks can he pull?” Another mercenary said dismissively.","Hearing this, the leader of the mercenaries suppressed his doubts.Indeed, he was just a kid, and there were no powerful people protecting him in secret. They could just kill him and be done with it. What could he possibly do?","It was probably just his imagination. What could a ten-year-old kid do? Even if he really did manage to lure them into the forest, he would only end up dead.","So, everyone sped up and continued the chase. They all knew that the little brat had a lot of treasures on him, and now that they had him in their sights, there was no way they were going to let him get away.","However, just then, they saw the little brat who had been running ahead suddenly stop and turn toward them, as if waiting for them to come closer.","“Hahahaha! Little brat, can’t you run anymore?” A mercenary laughed loudly, staring at the child in front of him, revealing a bloodthirsty and cruel sneer: “You want to run? Isn’t that what you want? Try running again!”","“Run? Who said I want to run?” Hao’er said coldly, a cold gleam flashing in his eyes: “I just don’t want to give you a chance to escape.”","“What do you mean?” The leader of the mercenaries was already a little suspicious, and now, hearing his words, the uneasiness in his heart grew stronger and stronger."]},{"number":4738,"title":"Chapter 4738: Silver Wolf Appears","paragraphs":["Chapter 4738: Silver Wolf Appears","Hao’er stared at the mercenaries, his mouth slightly open, before he called out in a cold voice, “Silver Wolf!” The moment the name left his lips, a ray of light seemed to emanate from his body. With a powerful leap, a majestic silver wolf materialized directly in front of the startled mercenaries.","“Awooooooooooo!” A resounding wolf howl ripped through the air, and the creature’s immense aura immediately spread outwards, instantly engulfing the surrounding area. The powerful and terrifying aura of a Super Sacred Beast washed over them. Even the mercenaries, who possessed extraordinary strength, turned pale and froze in place, unable to move. Some of the weaker ones completely lost control of their legs and crumpled to their knees.","“Super Sacred Beast...” They stared in utter shock, their eyes wide with disbelief, at the creature that had appeared before them. In that precise moment, they finally grasped why the little brat had led them to this location. It was clear now: he had summoned the Super Sacred Beast with the explicit intention of killing them!","“Whoosh!”","Hao’er took advantage of their shock and the overwhelming presence of the silver wolf that held them captive. A long sword appeared in his hand, and a fierce burst of sword energy swept out as he moved. His small figure moved with deadly efficiency, like a demon, relentlessly taking their lives.","Meanwhile, the Heaven’s Sun Sect elders and their group, who were traveling in the opposite direction, couldn’t help but stop and look back when the distinct wolf howls reached them.","“Elder, what’s wrong?” asked the middle-aged man, noticing the elder’s sudden pause.","“Didn’t you hear that?” The elder frowned, turning to him.","The middle-aged man offered a sheepish smile. “I heard it, but it’s just wolves howling. They should be far away from us.”","“No, these wolf howls are a little different,” the elder mused, “and besides, we’ve already passed through this area; there shouldn’t be any more fierce beasts.” He pondered for a moment, then his expression suddenly changed as if he’d realized something significant. “Let’s go! We need to go back and take a look!” As soon as he finished speaking, he quickly darted forward, heading back the way they came. The people behind him, unsure of what was happening, exchanged glances and swiftly followed.","On the other side, Hao’er wiped the blood from his sword and put it away. He then proceeded to systematically take all the valuable items from the mercenaries’ bodies. He instructed the Silver Wolf to pile the corpses together, then retrieved some corpse-dissolving water from his space and sprinkled it over the bodies.","Just as he observed the corpses dissolving into pools of blood seeping into the ground, the Silver Wolf’s voice came from behind him.","“Someone’s coming, and there are quite a few of them.”","“You go back first,” Hao’er instructed, allowing the wolf to return to his space. He then quickly put away his remaining things and departed the scene. As a Super Sacred Beast, the Silver Wolf’s howl was extraordinary. While the disciples of the Heaven’s Sun Sect might not have been able to discern its true nature, the old man certainly could. To avoid any potential trouble, Hao’er even took the precaution of cleaning up the corpses on the ground.","Shortly after Hao’er left, the elder of the Heaven’s Sun Sect arrived. However, upon reaching the clearing, he found only subtle traces on the ground and the lingering scent of blood in the air.","“Elder? How is it? Did you find anything?” The middle-aged man and his disciples hurried to catch up, looking around but seeing nothing conclusive.","The elder thoughtfully stared at the ground, stroking his beard. “Someone must have just died here,” he stated, “but the body has been disposed of.”","“Could it be that the mercenaries killed that kid?” the middle-aged man inquired, “and then destroyed the body to cover their tracks and prevent his family from finding out?”"]},{"number":4739,"title":"Chapter 4739: Commission","paragraphs":["Chapter 4739: Commission","The elder remained silent, his gaze sweeping the clearing for a long time, but he found nothing out of the ordinary. Finally, with a sigh, he simply said, “Let’s go!” and turned to depart with his men. Only he knew that a lingering question, an unshakeable sense of unease, remained unanswered in his heart.","Two days later, in a bustling town, several wandering cultivators were taking a much-needed rest in a teahouse. One of them let out a deep sigh. “I never expected this!” he exclaimed, shaking his head.","“That’s right. That little girl is far too cunning,” another agreed, a hint of frustration in his voice.","“She’s so small and looks so cute, yet she’s incredibly scheming.” The mere thought of how they had been outmaneuvered by the child made them all shake their heads and sigh once more.","“I can’t find that little girl; I feel so uneasy!” Shen Shiqi mused, rubbing his chin. “Which family does she belong to? Yun Qi? Could ‘Yun’ truly be her family name?”","“Hehe, Old Shen, don’t even bother,” another person chuckled, patting him on the shoulder. “That little girl is like a little fox. I bet she just made up that name to trick us.” He then pressed, “Tell us, what’s our next move? We can’t find her, and we don’t know where she went. I guess we won’t be able to find her in the future, will we?”","“Can’t find her?” Shen Shiqi raised an eyebrow, a strange smile spreading across his face. “Just because we can’t find her doesn’t mean that others can’t.”","“Oh? What’s your plan?” Several of the cultivators looked at him, their interest piqued.","“Put out a commission,” he said with a laugh, his eyes gleaming with cunning. “I don’t believe that little brat can simply fly away.” He looked at the others, waiting for their reaction. “What do you all think of my idea?”","“Oh, that’s is a good idea. When the time comes, whoever sees that little girl can help us capture her first,” one of them conceded, but then hesitated. “But she’s just a child. Isn’t a commission a bit too much?”","Upon hearing this, Shen Shiqi glanced at them and let out a laugh. “She’s just a little fox. If she were truly that simple and ordinary, would the five of us have fallen into her hands? How could she slip away right under our noses? Besides, I think even if we put out the commission for her, those people might not be able to catch her. That little girl is cunning! At most, it’ll just buy us some time and let us know where she is.”","Another cultivator considered this, then offered a suggestion. “If we want to use a wanted poster, I think we can say that we are looking for a runaway sister. That way, those who go after her won’t hurt her and will know how to handle her. After all, she’s just a little girl, so they can’t go too far.”","“Alright, let’s do that!” Shen Shiqi grinned. “Hurry up and finish your tea, then let’s get to work.”","At this very moment, Yue’er had no idea that these persistent individuals had not given up and were still actively searching for her! She was comfortably seated in a quiet corner of the market in another small town, happily eating hot buns. Her attention was captivated by an old woman nearby, who was milking several sheep and selling the fresh milk.","Yue’er looked at the frothy milk and couldn’t help but lick her lips, a hint of pure, childlike greed flashing in her eyes. After finishing her steamed buns, she wiped the corners of her mouth, clapped her hands together, and confidently walked up to the old woman. “Grandma, how much is this sheep’s milk?”","“This is spirit sheep’s milk, very nourishing,” the old woman replied with a warm smile, picking up a bottle to show the girl. “Ten gold coins for a bottle.”"]},{"number":4740,"title":"Chapter 4740: Trying to pass off fake as genuine","paragraphs":["Chapter 4740: Trying to pass off fake as genuine","“I’ll take one bottle,” Yue’er said with a bright smile, pulling out ten gold coins and handing them to the old woman.","“Good, good, good, do you want this one, or would you like me to squeeze another for you?” the old woman asked kindly.","“Just this one!” Yue’er replied, recalling how she’d watched the old woman milk the sheep just moments before, assuring herself there’d be no issues with freshness.","“All right, dear. Take it, and give it to your parents to boil. It’ll taste even better with a little salt,” the old woman suggested.","“Yes, I know,” Yue’er affirmed, a memory of having tried it before flashing through her mind.","Clutching the bottle of spirit sheep’s milk, she then spent a few more gold coins to borrow the kitchen of a nearby restaurant. There, she boiled the milk, drank a satisfying bowl, and carefully packed the remainder for her journey.","After exploring the town and purchasing a few necessities, Yue’er was about to continue her travels when something caught her eye. A man was sticking a picture onto a wall. Once he left, she approached for a closer look. Her eyes widened in genuine shock, and with a swift, almost imperceptible movement, she leaped up, tore the picture down when no one was watching, and quickly tucked it into her bosom.","“Those bastards actually want to capture me with a wanted poster!” she muttered, wrinkling her nose. She then glanced down at her current attire, and her eyes lit up with a sly smile. In the next instant, she darted away, a new plan forming in her mischievous mind.","At the same time, wanted posters depicting Yue’er were swiftly being plastered in towns and villages throughout the surrounding region. Muchen, who had just entered a different town, frowned slightly as he noticed the image on the wall at the entrance. He walked closer for a better look, and the longer he stared, the colder his expression grew.","Upon entering the town, he found a place to rest and immediately pulled out his communication jade to inquire if his sister had encountered any problems. Soon, a message came back through the jade. Hearing his sister’s reassuring words, he finally relaxed, though he still urged her to be careful and informed her of his current town’s location. As anticipated, the two had not taken the same route, and the towns they were in were quite far apart. It was almost impossible for them to meet up and continue their journey together, especially since their master had already instructed them to return independently.","When Yue’er set off again, she had undergone a complete transformation. Gone was her beautiful dress, replaced by the simple, worn clothes of a beggar. She had often heard her father recount tales of her mother’s past—how mischievous she had been, how she disliked pretty dresses, and how she loved to wander around disguised as a beggar. With such a rare opportunity, Yue’er decided to emulate her mother and embrace the role of a little beggar herself. Besides, this way, even if those pursuing her appeared, they likely wouldn’t recognize her.","Indeed, Shen Shiqi and his companions truly had not anticipated this little girl’s clever disguise. At that very moment, they were listening to various reports from those who had responded to the reward. Some claimed to have seen the girl they were looking for, while others even boasted that they had already captured her and were simply awaiting their arrival.","However, as they listened to the conflicting news pouring in from all directions, they couldn’t help but exchange bewildered glances. “Shouldn’t we add one more detail,” one of them mused, “that she should be taught a lesson for impersonating someone else?”","“No, it’s the people who posted the reward who didn’t do their job properly. They didn’t check before passing on the information,” Shen Shiqi countered, narrowing his eyes and letting out a cold, sharp smile. “It seems that they didn’t take this matter seriously. Perhaps they think we’re just ordinary cultivators. It appears we have to do something to get results faster.”","Upon hearing this, the others exchanged knowing glances and smiled in unison."]},{"number":4741,"title":"Chapter 4741: Chased Away","paragraphs":["Chapter 4741: Chased Away","The following day, Shen Shiqi and his companions arrived in the small town where Yue’er had recently been. They wandered through the streets, confident in their gathered intelligence. “According to our information,” Shen Shiqi declared, “that little girl was last seen in this town, but it seems she’s no longer here. However, it’s easy to figure out her next move, as there’s only one road leading south out of town.”","“In that case, let’s go!” another companion said with a smile. “The big city is to the south. That little girl should be a member of a family in that city, so it should be easier to find her.” He glanced around at the other cultivators, a shared determination in their eyes, and then continued on their way.","Meanwhile, Yue’er, believing that her pursuers wouldn’t be able to track her, had relaxed her pace, feeling less weary. As evening approached and the sky began to darken, she spotted a village ahead, nestled amidst cornfields. She decided to seek rest and a meal there.","However, her chosen disguise proved to be a double-edged sword. Because she was dressed as a beggar, she was met not with hospitality, but with scorn. Before she could even get close, she was chased away by a group of mischievous children from the village.","“Go away, go away! Stinky beggar, don’t come into our village!” the children shouted, pelting her with small stones.","Yue’er froze for a moment, then swiftly dodged the incoming stones, backing away. “Don’t throw stones at me, don’t hit me!” she cried out.","“Little beggar, get out of here! You’re not allowed in our village. Hurry up and leave, or I’ll let Big Yellow bite you!” one of the children yelled, then turned and shouted, “Big Yellow, Big Yellow, come out!”","Yue’er watched as a large yellow dog came bounding out, barking ferociously at her. Seeing the dog charging, she instinctively backed away, then turned and shouted, “Control your dog! Otherwise, I’ll kill it and eat it!”","“Big Yellow, bite him! Big Yellow, bite him!” the children cheered, clapping their hands in excitement.","Yue’er spun around and fled. After running a short distance, she saw an old beggar walking toward the village, using a tree branch as a walking stick. Seeing him, she called out a warning, “The children there won’t let beggars come near them, and there’s a big yellow dog that bites people. Old beggar, run away!”","The old beggar merely glanced at her, a faint smile playing on his lips. “You run first. This old beggar will go get something to eat.” With that, he continued his steady walk towards the village.","Yue’er didn’t linger. She continued her retreat to a mountain path. After running a considerable distance and realizing the big yellow dog was no longer pursuing her, she found a secluded spot to rest in the woods beside the path.","“These kids are so mean, bullying people like that,” she muttered, wiping sweat from her forehead with her sleeve. She pulled out some water from her interspatial ring to drink, then took out some other provisions.","Seeing only pastries and dried meat, she frowned, letting out a silent sigh. “I want to eat a proper meal. I don’t want pastries and dried meat anymore.” After all, the food she had eaten on the road had been haphazard at best, and the constant diet of pastries and dried meat had become tiresome. She tucked the items back into her spatial pocket, pulled out a fruit to eat, and then agilely leaped onto a tree branch, intending to sleep.","The small forest was quiet, save for the faint rustling of leaves in the gentle breeze. However, after some time, a tantalizing aroma of cooked meat began to drift through the air. The smell made Yue’er, who had only eaten a piece of fruit and had just closed her eyes, swallow hard. Her eyes snapped open, and she sat up, looking around, her hunger suddenly reignited."]},{"number":4742,"title":"Chapter 4742: The Old Beggar","paragraphs":["Chapter 4742: The Old Beggar","“It smells so good!” Yue’er sniffed the air, inhaling the rich aroma that filled the forest. Her eyes gleamed with delight as she followed the enticing scent.","Underneath a tree in a small grove, an old beggar was leisurely sipping wine and cooking meat. In front of him sat a pot, chipped at one corner, from which steam and fragrant vapors continuously rose. A fire still flickered beneath it, indicating the meat inside was not yet fully cooked.","“Old beggar?” A hint of surprise flickered in Yue’er’s beautiful eyes as she recognized the figure. She trotted forward, inhaling deeply from the pot, her eyes closing in pure bliss as she savored the fragrance.","“That’s the smell! Old beggar, what kind of meat are you cooking? Why does it smell so good?” she asked, acting as if they were old acquaintances. She settled herself comfortably next to the old beggar on a wooden bench, craning her neck to peer at the simmering meat under the lid, swallowing her saliva like a hungry cat.","The old beggar glanced at her. “Didn’t you manage to get any food?” he inquired.","“No, they set their dogs on me, so I ran away and didn’t get close to the village!” Yue’er replied, shaking her head. Her gaze remained fixed on the fragrant pot. “Old beggar, can you share some of the meat in the pot with me? I’m starving!”","The old beggar stirred the fire with a stick, his aged voice slow and indifferent. “You’re a beggar, and I’m a beggar. Why should I share my food with you?”","“I can give you money!” Yue’er’s face brightened. She took out a gold coin, offering it to him with a smile. “I’ll give you money, and you can share your food with me. I won’t take advantage of you.”","The old beggar cast a quick glance at the coin, then extended his skinny hand to take it. “Do you have a bowl?” he asked.","“I brought one!” Yue’er chirped, her voice loud and clear as she pulled a bowl from her bosom.","The old beggar lifted the lid, and an even richer aroma of meat wafted out, permeating the air and making Yue’er’s mouth water profusely. She couldn’t help but swallow hard, bringing her bowl closer in anticipation.","“Pass it over here,” the old beggar instructed. He scooped a generous spoonful of meat into Yue’er’s bowl, then another for himself. He replaced the lid and used two small, sharpened twigs as chopsticks to begin eating.","Yue’er, having her own chopsticks, carried her bowl of meat back to her seat and sat down to eat. With her first bite, the rich aroma of the meat filled her mouth. She parted her lips slightly to exhale the hot steam before lowering her head to continue eating with gusto.","The old beggar drank his wine and ate his meat, occasionally glancing at the little beggar beside him. Seeing her bowl empty, he generously scooped another large spoonful for her.","Yue’er ate three full bowls of meat before finally stopping. She hugged her stomach, leaning back against the large tree, breathing lightly, her small face radiating pure satisfaction. “Old beggar,” she asked curiously, “what kind of meat is this? Why is it so fragrant? I’ve eaten a lot of meat in my life, but I’ve never had this kind of stewed meat. It’s truly delicious.”","“It’s dog meat,” the old beggar said slowly, taking a sip of his wine.","Yue’er was stunned for a moment, almost instinctively crying out, “Dog meat? This is dog meat? Where did you get a dog?” As soon as the words left her mouth, a sudden realization struck her, and her eyes widened in shock.","The old beggar took another bite of meat. “It’s the big yellow dog from the village entrance,” he explained. “I just happened to stew a pot of it.” As he spoke, he glanced at her, a playful smile flashing in his otherwise cloudy eyes. “What’s the matter? You don’t eat dog meat? You said it was delicious just now, and you even ate three bowls.”"]},{"number":4743,"title":"Chapter 4743: Appreciation","paragraphs":["Chapter 4743: Appreciation","“I... I’ve just never eaten dog meat before,” Yue’er said, a sudden frown creasing her brow. “I’ve eaten all kinds of spirit beast meat, but never dog meat. I didn’t know it tasted like this. Also...” She trailed off, instinctively lowering her head and tugging at her hands.","“Also what?” the old beggar prompted.","Yue’er sighed dramatically, like a tiny adult. “It’s actually quite tasty, and the meat you stewed is really fragrant.” Yet, the thought of having eaten dog meat still made her feel a little uneasy.","“This is a local breed of dog, perfect for stewing,” the old beggar remarked, stretching his waist. “I’ve eaten a lot of dog meat in my time, and I figured out this stewing method myself. No one else can replicate the taste. You’re lucky to have had this today, otherwise you wouldn’t have been able to eat the old beggar’s dog meat.”","Yue’er glanced at the pot, noting there was still some left. It seemed a shame to waste it. “What about the rest?” she asked.","“Don’t worry, there’s none for you. The old beggar will eat it in the middle of the night.” With that, he hugged his wine gourd, leaned against the tree, and promptly fell asleep.","Early the next morning, as Yue’er emerged from the mountain path, ready to continue her journey, she spotted the old beggar slowly walking behind her. She stopped, a smile spreading across her face. “Old beggar, are you also going to the city? Then we’re going the same way! Let’s go together! We can talk and chat on the way.”","Feeling that she wasn’t far from Yunxiao Mountain, she had relaxed her pace, no longer in such a hurry.","“I’m used to being alone, so it doesn’t matter if there’s one more person,” he said, using a tree branch as a cane. Despite his age, he didn’t walk particularly slowly.","The two walked together, Yue’er chattering non-stop like a little bird following her parent. The old beggar listened quietly, offering only occasional responses, and the journey proceeded peacefully, without incident.","However, at noon, as Yue’er and the old beggar rested by the side of the mountain road, drinking water, they saw the group of cultivators who had been pursuing them riding their contract beasts directly towards them. Yue’er was so startled that she choked on her water, quickly scrambling to hide behind the old beggar.","The old beggar observed this, casting an emotionless glance at the approaching group. He then slowly shifted his gaze away, resuming his quiet sip of wine.","“That brat runs pretty fast. We didn’t see her the whole way here,” a man on a contract beast commented, scanning the surroundings. When his eyes briefly landed on the old man and child by the road, he didn’t linger, quickly looking away.","“That little girl is cunning! She might have already returned to her family, but heh heh, once we get to the city, even if she hides in her family, I’ll still be able to find her,” Shen Shiqi said with a confident smile. His gaze also swept over the two beggars, an old man and a child, resting by the roadside. He merely glanced at them before dismissing them, not even considering that the little beggar could be the girl they were so relentlessly pursuing. In their eyes, that little girl must have come from a very privileged and doted-upon family. How could she possibly be associated with a dirty little beggar?","“Little beggar, here’s some food for you.” Shen Shiqi waved his hand, and two large cakes flew through the air, landing in the little beggar’s arms.","Yue’er kept her head down, desperate not to be recognized. When she heard Shen Shiqi’s voice and saw the two large cakes flying towards her, she couldn’t help but feel her lips twitch slightly."]},{"number":4744,"title":"Chapter 4744: Missed","paragraphs":["Chapter 4744: Missed","Yue’er remained silent, simply taking the pancake and nodding her head, feigning gratitude.","“Hehe, Old Shen, don’t throw things like that, you’ll scare the little beggar,” a man behind Shen Shiqi remarked, glancing at the seemingly timid child and laughing.","Hearing this, Shen Shiqi, who had already looked away, turned back. He saw the little beggar with her head bowed, not uttering a word, just nodding repeatedly. He raised his eyebrows, about to speak, when the old beggar’s joyful and grateful voice interrupted him.","“Thank you, gentlemen. My granddaughter is mute and very timid. I am thanking you on her behalf,” the old beggar said.","Mute? Yue’er’s body stiffened, but she maintained her act, huddling closer to the old beggar with her head bowed, clutching the two large cakes tightly in her hands.","“It’s okay, it’s no big deal,” Shen Shiqi replied. “By the way, have you seen a little girl around five years old? She was wearing a pink dress and looked very cute and mischievous.”","“Yes, that little girl even gave me a gold coin,” the old beggar confirmed, taking out the gold coin Yue’er had given him the previous night and holding it open in his palm.","Seeing this, Shen Shiqi and the others’ eyes lit up. They exchanged knowing glances and smiled. “I knew it! That little girl has no other choice but to take this road. I guess she wants to go back to the city.”","“Old beggar, how long ago did that little girl leave?” another person asked.","“I met her yesterday. Last night, my granddaughter and I spent the night in the woods, so I don’t know where she went,” the old beggar said, shaking his head.","“Let’s go! We’ll hurry up, and we might still be able to catch up,” Shen Shiqi declared with a smile, spurring his contract beast forward.","The group rode their beasts, kicking up a cloud of dust on the mountain road. Only after they were completely out of sight did Yue’er finally raise her head, exhale softly, and pat her chest with one hand.","“That was close,” she gasped, then looked at the old beggar. She handed him one of the flatbreads she held, a grateful smile on her face. “Old beggar, you have good reflexes! Here you go.”","The old beggar glanced at her. “Keep it for yourself!” he said. With that, he stood up, cane in hand. “Those people are not ordinary cultivators. How did you provoke them?”","“You don’t know, those guys were bored out of their minds and were just looking for trouble,” Yue’er said, glaring at him helplessly. “I didn’t provoke them; they came to provoke me. They kept following me, and it was so annoying that I had to pretend to be a beggar. They kept chasing me, and I didn’t know what they wanted.”","“Then why are you still going forward? Aren’t you afraid of running into them?” the old beggar asked.","“I have to keep going because I’m going to the city ahead,” she explained with a smile. “They won’t recognize me. They didn’t recognize me just now, did they? But I don’t think I can walk with you anymore. If you’re not in a hurry, you go to the city by yourself. I’m in a hurry to get back!”","As she spoke, she darted several meters away and waved at him. “Old beggar, goodbye. If I see you again, I’ll treat you to a big meal.” Her voice grew fainter and fainter as she quickly moved away.","The old beggar watched her leave, a faint smile appearing on his aged face, and he continued walking forward slowly."]},{"number":4745,"title":"Chapter 4745: No Fleas","paragraphs":["Chapter 4745: No Fleas","Two days later, while Shen Shiqi and his group were still combing the city for Yue’er, she had already arrived at the foot of Yunxiao Mountain. A joyful smile spread across her small face as she gazed at the familiar surroundings. With light steps, she darted towards the mountain like a playful bird.","Yunxiao Mountain was completely inaccessible to outsiders. Not only were there intricate formations within the mountains, but the entire area belonging to Yunxiao Mountain was enveloped by a powerful barrier. Outsiders were only aware of its general location but could never pinpoint its exact whereabouts.","“Hehe, am I the first one back?” Yue’er mused aloud as she walked. The thought of being the first to return filled her with cheerful anticipation.","“Little sister.”","Just then, a voice came from behind her. She froze, then looked up to see her brother, Muchen, emerging from a forest path. Her eyes widened in disbelief.","“Brother? What are you doing here?”","Muchen smiled. “I arrived before you. I came this morning, and when I saw you weren’t back yet, I decided to wait for you on this mountain path.”","“When you sent me a message last time, weren’t you still far away? How did you get back faster than me?” she asked, surprised. She walked up to him and sat down on the stone steps of the mountain path, resting her chin in her hands, a look of disappointment on her face. “I thought I was the first one here!”","Muchen sat down beside her. “Did you have a smooth journey back? Did the people who were following you give you any trouble?” As he spoke, his gaze fell upon her beggar’s clothes, a hint of curiosity in his small face. “Did you dress up as a beggar the whole way back?”","“Hehe, I shook them off, brother. It turns out that dressing up as a beggar is really fun!” she said with a grin. “Those people were following me, but when I dressed up as a beggar, they didn’t recognize me. Next time I go out, I’ll dress up as a beggar again.”","“Big Brother hasn’t come back yet. He was delayed on the road and will probably be back in two days, but he should be back within a month,” Muchen explained, looking at her. “When I came back, I reported to Master’s cave abode. Since you’re here, you should also go tell Master that you’re back.”","“Yeah~” Yue’er nodded, then stood up and followed her brother up the mountain.","Upon arriving at the cave abode, Yue’er stood before it and called out, “Master, I’m back!”","When they didn’t hear an immediate response and thought that their master wouldn’t emerge, the cave abode’s barrier array suddenly opened, and their Master, the Azure Emperor, slowly walked out from within.","“Back?” The Azure Emperor glanced at the two of them, sensing a subtle change in their auras. He nodded discreetly, acknowledging that they seemed to have gained something valuable from their journey.","“Master, we’re back, but my brother arrived first, and I just got here,” Yue’er stepped forward, smiling and narrowing her eyes playfully at him.","Seeing his little disciple dressed like a beggar, the Azure Emperor rubbed his brow. “How many days have you not bathed?” he inquired.","Hearing this, Yue’er paused for a moment. She lifted her arm, pulled at her clothes, sniffed intently, and then responded with serious conviction, “Master, my clothes are still clean. I only smell of sweat; there are no fleas on me.”"]},{"number":4746,"title":"Chapter 4746: Careless","paragraphs":["Chapter 4746: Careless","“Alright, hurry up and go take a bath!” The Azure Emperor waved his hand, motioning for the two disciples to leave. “Practice on your own these days, and wait for your Senior Brother to return before coming to see me.”","“Yes,” the two replied, bowing respectfully before retreating.","On their way back to their respective cave abodes, Yue’er excitedly recounted to her brother, Muchen, everything she had encountered during her days outside, including how she had cleverly acquired those crystal cores.","“Brother, did you encounter anything interesting outside?” Yue’er asked, her eyes wide with curiosity.","At her question, Muchen’s expression shifted. “I met a lady,” he began. “She looked very weak, but she was actually incredibly strong and powerful. Meeting her made me understand something.”","Yue’er blinked, her curiosity piqued. “What did you understand?” she asked.","Muchen looked at her, his expression serious. “You can’t judge things by appearances. The more delicate a woman seems, the more powerful she may be, and the more deceitful she is.”","“Deceitful?” Yue’er was taken aback for a moment, then her beautiful eyes crinkled with a smile. “Brother, Yue’er doesn’t often deceive people! Yue’er only deceives bad people occasionally.”","Muchen’s lips curved slightly, his small face softening a little. He reached out and playfully ruffled her “bird’s nest” hair. “Mm, big brother knows that Yue’er has always been very good and very smart.”","“Big brother, I’m going to go take a bath and change my clothes first. I’ll buy a lot of good food when I come back, and we can eat under the tree,” Yue’er said, waving at him as she headed towards her cave abode.","On the other side, Hao’er found himself in a dire predicament.","In a quiet alley in a small town, he had spotted a medicine peddler selling some rare and unknown seeds on the ground. Intrigued, he squatted down and carefully selected a few, planning to take them back to Yue’er. Unexpectedly, just as he finished paying and was about to stand up, he was suddenly struck by a stick. Before he could even react, he was knocked unconscious.","In the brief moment before he lost consciousness, he was filled with regret and self-reproach. He had been careless, foolishly believing that nothing untoward would happen in such a seemingly ordinary place. It was precisely this carelessness and complacency that had landed him in danger.","When he finally came to, he found himself confined within a small, pitch-black room. He couldn’t see anything in the oppressive darkness, but he could hear the distinct sounds of disordered breathing and suppressed sobbing coming from nearby.","He exerted himself, managing to sit up in the corner, and cautiously checked his body to see if anything was missing. He discovered that his cosmos sack had been taken, but to his relief, his interspatial ring was still present. Most of his valuable and essential items were stored within this ring, which was no ordinary piece of jewelry. Of the three siblings, only Yue’er possessed an interspatial bracelet, while he and Muchen wore interspatial rings. These rings had been specially modified and upgraded, each possessing a hidden function. As for the contents of the cosmos sack, it held nothing of significant value apart from some daily food and a few gold coins, so he wasn’t particularly concerned about its loss.","But where was he now? Who had captured him? What exactly did they want? These questions swirled ceaselessly in his mind. Although a wave of anxiety washed over him, he had faced many challenges in his life, and gradually, he managed to calm himself.","“Who are you? How did you get here?” he whispered, directing his question to a little boy he sensed was beside him in the oppressive darkness."]},{"number":4747,"title":"Chapter 4747: Shock","paragraphs":["Chapter 4747: Shock","“Woo woo, we don’t know how we got here,” a child’s voice sobbed from the darkness. “I was just walking along when someone knocked me unconscious. When I woke up, I was here. Woo woo... I want to go home. I want to go home...”","“Woo woo... I want to go home too. I’m scared. Mother, I’m scared. Woo woo...” another joined in.","One child’s cries quickly triggered others, and in an instant, the already dark room descended into chaotic wails.","Hao’er listened intently, discerning that among the weeping voices were not only boys but also girls. For a moment, his heart skipped a beat as a chilling thought crossed his mind: Could they have encountered human traffickers?","However, in the days that followed, he realized his initial assumption was wrong.","He dared not reveal his cultivation level, fearing it would alarm his captors, so he could only wait. To his surprise, this wait stretched for several days.","The small, dark room held about thirty children, ranging in age from six or seven to around ten. Since their capture, they had been kept in absolute darkness, unseen by anyone. No one paid them any attention, nor did anyone bring them food or even a sip of water. Initially, everyone cried out for their homes and their mothers, but as the days dragged on, they grew so weak from hunger and thirst that they barely had the strength to move.","Hao’er remained in his corner, uncertain if there were powerful individuals observing them. He didn’t dare to move, but secretly regulated his breathing, calculating how long they had been imprisoned.","After approximately three days, the door to the small, dark room finally creaked open from the outside.","“Come out, it’s time to eat,” a voice shouted from beyond. Hearing this, the children, with what little strength they had left, gritted their teeth and painfully pushed themselves to their feet, leaning against the wall for support as they shuffled out.","Once outside, they discovered they were in a much larger prison-like area. Small, dark rooms, identical to the one they had just left, were arranged in a circle. Children were emerging from every single room, though their expressions and physical conditions varied slightly depending on their confinement.","The light in this larger space, though not very bright, was also not completely dark. For those who had grown accustomed to the profound darkness of their cells, it wasn’t glaring. As a result, Hao’er horrifyingly noticed that some of the children emerging from the other small black rooms carried a savage, bloodthirsty aura. Despite their tender age, they behaved like small, desperate beasts, wary of others and constantly on guard. Upon exiting their small cells, they immediately surged towards a tray holding only a dozen steamed buns, scrambling to grab and devour them. In an instant, the scene erupted into chaos: pushing, hitting, biting, and screaming filled the air.","Hao’er was shocked to observe that even though the children were out of their individual cells, they were still divided into separate areas within this larger prison. Each small black room’s occupants were separated from the others, yet each area contained about twenty to thirty children, and only a mere dozen steamed buns were provided for each group. Stealing had become their sole instinct for survival.","As he stood there, momentarily stunned, he watched helplessly as the dozen or so steamed buns in front of his own small dark room were swiftly snatched up. Some children frantically stuffed them into their mouths, others were still fiercely fighting over them, while some cried out, “Give me some, give me some, let me have a bite...”","A bitter and shocking sensation rose in Hao’er’s throat. He swallowed hard, took a deep breath, and forced his gaze away from the horrifying spectacle, striving to calm his rapidly pounding heart."]},{"number":4748,"title":"Chapter 4748: Anger","paragraphs":["Chapter 4748: Anger","Just then, a man emerged from the central area, carrying a plate covered with a lid. He walked to a half-human-tall cylindrical pillar in the center, placed the plate on it, and dramatically lifted the lid, revealing its contents.","A roasted chicken.","It was plump, glistening, and emitted an incredibly enticing aroma. For these children, who had been starving for days, even weeks, it was an unimaginable delicacy – a sight that made their eyes sparkle with desperate desire, driving them to risk everything to obtain it!","“Same as always, the winner gets to eat the roast chicken,” the man announced. Under the shining, hungry eyes of the children, he promptly put the lid back on, further whetting their appetites and their desperate urge to claim it, not allowing them to savor even a hint of the scent.","“Arghhhhh!”","As soon as the man’s voice faded, chaos erupted in several of the small black rooms. The sickening sound of fists hitting flesh, accompanied by roars, screams, and wails, filled the air. Some of the children in the adjacent cages cowered together, glancing back with palpable fear in their eyes. In several other cages, only one child stood dominant at the front of their area, while the others behind them seemed too afraid to even approach.","Hao’er pursed his lips, silently observing the gruesome scene. He watched as the children trampled and bit each other, fighting with every ounce of their being to defeat their opponents.","Finally, the iron doors at the front of each designated area swung open, and only the victorious child emerged from each. However, even these winners, having triumphed in their initial skirmishes, now faced a new challenge: they had to fight the children from the other areas.","“Begin!” the man by the pillar commanded. As his voice echoed, seven or eight children immediately plunged into a brutal melee. They possessed no refined martial arts, only crude, self-taught fighting styles. Yet, there were one or two exceptions, exhibiting a raw, untamed prowess.","In the end, a small boy, who appeared to be only eight or nine years old, managed to defeat the others. Despite his victory, he was covered in wounds, with blood trickling from the corner of his mouth. Nonetheless, he walked forward, step by agonizing step, until he reached the man. “Roast chicken, it’s mine,” he stated, his voice a ragged whisper.","“Yes, it’s yours,” the man replied with a chilling smile. He patted the boy on the head and handed him the plate with the coveted roast chicken.","The panting little boy stared at the uncovered roast chicken, swallowed hard, and then suddenly lunged forward to seize it. However, just as he surged ahead, a sword qi instantly struck out, slicing him in half in a horrifying flash.","“Arghhhhhh...”","For a moment, the terrified cries of the children reverberated through the prison, accompanied by sounds of sheer panic. The cries were filled with primal fear and terror, but they lasted only a brief moment before quickly falling silent. This was because the children had clapped their hands over their mouths, too terrified to utter another sound. They shrank back, their eyes wide with terror as they stared at the gruesome sight of the boy, now split in two, on the ground.","One moment he was alive, and the next, he was dead. And his death was unspeakably horrific.","Hao’er clenched his fists, his heart burning with incandescent rage. He gritted his teeth, desperate to maintain control, afraid that he would lose himself and act impulsively.","In that chilling moment, he knew for certain that powerful individuals were secretly protecting their captors. When the man had brutally killed the child with his sword qi, Hao’er had felt several distinct gusts of air—signatures of powerful cultivation—emanating from the shadows."]},{"number":4749,"title":"Chapter 4749: Discovered","paragraphs":["Chapter 4749: Discovered","Hao’er didn’t know how he managed to witness the horrific scene unfold. All he knew was that after a while, several black-clad, masked cultivators emerged from the central area. They selected certain children from each small, dark room and led them away, including the boy who had briefly claimed the roast chicken and a few of those he had beaten.","Hao’er watched as they took the children. He took a deep breath, casting a cold glance forward. Just as he was about to follow the others back to their small, dark room, a voice stopped him.","“Wait a minute.”","The man who had been standing next to the pillar spoke. His gaze swept over the remaining children, finally landing on Hao’er. He pointed at him. “You, come out.”","Everyone’s gaze immediately followed the man’s finger to Hao’er. In the dim light, he was an unremarkable child, but unlike the others, he possessed a stillness, a calmness that children his age simply didn’t have.","How perceptive! Hao’er’s heart sank. He knew his barely suppressed anger and piercing gaze had given him away. He forced his emotions down and, under the scrutiny of every eye, walked to the front.","A cultivator quickly rushed forward and opened the iron door of their section.","Seeing this, Hao’er stepped out and approached the man, one careful step at a time.","The man stood with his hands clasped behind his back, slowly circling Hao’er, scrutinizing him carefully. The more he observed, the more surprised he became. He glanced at the calm, expressionless child, then looked at the black-robed men beside him. “Is this the newcomer?” he asked.","“Yes, sir...” The cultivator replied respectfully. But before he could finish speaking, a wind blade materialized and instantly severed one of his arms.","The arm flew through the air, blood splattering across the ground. After a moment of instinctive screaming, the black-robed man quickly stifled his cries and knelt down, trembling.","“Do you know why I cut off your arm?” the man said coldly, his hands still behind his back, his bloodthirsty gaze fixed on the kneeling cultivator. However, the corner of his eye subtly tracked Hao’er’s expression.","“I don’t know...” the dismembered cultivator stammered, his voice quivering, genuinely unaware of his transgression.","“You don’t know? Then I’ll tell you,” the man said icily. “Look up and look at this child. Does he show even the slightest bit of panic or fear? Does he look like an ordinary child?”","Hearing this, the black-robed cultivator looked up. He saw the child’s eyes, calm and cold, fixed on him. Even with one of his arms severed, the child didn’t so much as frown. In that moment, the cultivator’s heart sank as he finally realized the grave mistake he had made.","“Get out of here!” the man commanded, no longer bothering to look at him.","“Yes.” The black-robed man, clutching his severed arm, endured the excruciating pain and staggered away.","“Which family are you from?” The man then turned his full attention back to Hao’er.","Hao’er pursed his lips, remaining silent.","“Hehe, you won’t tell me? Don’t you want to go home? Tell me, and I can have someone send you back,” he coaxed, a low laugh rumbling in his chest.","Upon hearing this, Hao’er frowned. “Do you think I’m that stupid?” he retorted. He had seen enough of this place and witnessed their brutal methods. How could he possibly believe they would let him leave?"]},{"number":4750,"title":"Chapter 4750: A Battle for Survival","paragraphs":["Chapter 4750: A Battle for Survival","“You really are naughty,” the man said, narrowing his eyes and smiling. “But since you refuse to talk, it’s alright. I’ll just kill you, and it will all be over. No one will ever know what you’ve been through, and no one will ever know where you died.” No sooner had he finished speaking than he lunged instantly towards Hao’er, intending to end him with a single, decisive blow.","However, just as he was about to strike, Hao’er, who had been on guard the entire time, swiftly dodged and pulled away from the attack.","Seeing this, the man’s eyebrows shot up in surprise. “I didn’t expect that! You’ve already reached the Nascent Soul stage? What a pity.”","He didn’t explicitly state what was a pity, but Hao’er knew precisely what he meant: it was a pity that such a talented child would die at his hands.","The powerful figures hidden in the shadows watched, but none of them revealed themselves. It seemed that not a single one took a mere child seriously. Indeed, Hao’er was just a child. No one would treat him as a genuine threat, and certainly no one would believe he could leave this place alive.","However, when they saw the child extend his hand and a long sword materialize within it, even those in the shadows registered surprise. In the very next moment, spirit energy surged from Hao’er’s small body, and he swung his sword fiercely at the man. They watched as his spirit energy coalesced on the blade, and in an instant, a fierce sword qi erupted from the edge. A whistling sound, accompanied by a palpable murderous aura, instantly targeted the man opposite him. As the sharp sword turned, its sword flower flashed with a cold, deadly light. In that brief instant, even the hidden observers couldn’t help but hold their breath.","“Whoosh! Whoosh!”","The man in front of him saw the fierce sword energy hurtling his way. The sword in the little boy’s hand moved with such incredible speed that only a blur of its shadow could be seen, not the blade itself. He couldn’t help but become instantly alert, taking the situation far more seriously. He responded while deftly dodging, but unexpectedly, when their two swords collided, a metallic clang echoed, accompanied by a fierce whistling sound. The biting coldness emanating from Hao’er’s blade was like a sharp edge, cutting several slits in his robe.","“Clang!”","“Whoosh!”","In the vast space, a large figure and a small figure engaged in a furious battle. The children around them were utterly stunned, not making a sound, pressing themselves against the iron doors, their eyes fixed on the fight. To them, they could only perceive the cold light reflecting off the blades and the flashing movements of the two figures, dazzling their eyes and filling them with shock. That child, only two or three years older than some of them, and about the same age as others, was actually able to fight with the powerful people of this place. He was incredibly strong.","Because of the commotion, the black-robed men who had left earlier returned, but they did not intervene. Instead, they stood not far from the center, silently observing the unfolding spectacle.","“Hiss!”","A gasp escaped his lips as the man was cut on the shoulder by Hao’er’s sword. Unable to hide his shock, he clutched his wound and retreated, his bloodthirsty eyes glaring at the small boy. Hao’er, too, was covered in wounds, his clothes stained red with his own blood.","At this moment, the little boy bore at least ten wounds of varying sizes on his body. Some were minor, merely superficial cuts, but one wound was deep enough to expose bone. Yet, the little boy kept his lips tightly clenched, uttering not a single sound, not even a groan. His expression remained resolute, as if he were prepared to fight to the death.","Though his opponent was undeniably far stronger, he found himself unable to withstand the boy’s seemingly reckless yet persistent attacks. A momentary lapse in concentration had left him with a painful slash on his shoulder, forcing him to retreat swiftly. But the “little devil” kept pressing forward, relentlessly pursuing him, refusing to give an inch."]},{"number":4751,"title":"Chapter 4751: Fatal Blow","paragraphs":["Chapter 4751: Fatal Blow","Hao’er gasped for breath, his teeth gritted as he stared coldly at his opponent. Suddenly, his spirit energy surged again, and his figure flashed forward with bewildering speed, delivering a deadly blow before the man could even react.","A powerful sword aura roared into the air, rising several meters in an instant. This visible sword aura materialized into a massive blade, slashing down with relentless force, filling the air with an undeniable murderous intent!","“No!”","“Be careful!”","“Quick, get out of the way!”","No one expected such a sudden turn of events. Even the few powerful individuals watching from the shadows were caught off guard by such a decisive move from a child so young. They were startled, abandoning their hidden positions and rushing forward instantly to save the man.","However, they were too far away, and Hao’er’s sword strike was so sudden and swift that even their intervention was too late. The sword would land before they could reach him.","“No!”","The man himself was startled, his eyes wide with fear. He retreated step by step, but just as he turned to flee, a powerful sword qi carrying terrifying pressure slashed down. His body froze in that moment, and in that instant of stiffness, his fate was sealed.","Death!","“Ah!”","A shrill scream ripped through the air as the terrifying sword qi descended. In the next moment, blood splattered everywhere, and the man was cut in half, his body scattered on the ground, leaving a horrifying, bloody mess.","“Hiss!”","Everyone around gasped. They had just witnessed him kill a child, and now he himself had died at the hands of another child, and in the exact same gruesome manner. This bloody, eerily similar scene shocked their hearts and stung their eyes.","“I’ll kill you!”","Among the figures who had rushed out, an old man’s eyes were bloodshot, his body radiating murderous intent. The consuming anger in his heart, combined with the sight of the bisected corpse on the ground, stimulated his nerves. He lunged forward, almost instinctively slapping his palm towards Hao’er.","That palm strike contained the powerful pressure and surging airflow of a Divine King, as well as boundless killing intent and fury. It was infused with a singular determination to kill Hao’er, and the raw power of that strike was almost equivalent to a full-force attack from a Divine King. If that palm strike landed, Hao’er wouldn’t just be dead; there wouldn’t even be a recognizable corpse left, only scattered flesh and blood.","Despite diligently practicing sword techniques with his master during this time, Hao’er was utterly unable to dodge or defend himself against a Divine King’s attack. Before he could even react, the old man’s deadly blow struck his chest with a resounding “Bang!”","“Bang!”","Hao’er’s small figure flew backward instantly, knocked back more than ten metres by the immense force. However, there was no scene of blood and flesh splattering everywhere, nor was there any sign of his internal organs being crushed, or him struggling for his life. He didn’t even have a trace of blood at the corner of his mouth. It was as if he had merely been pushed, unharmed and without a single scratch.","“Pfftttt!”","Hao’er was perfectly fine, but the old man who had delivered the deadly blow was suddenly sent flying by a mysterious, rebounding force. He crashed to the ground, his internal organs shattered, and he died."]},{"number":4752,"title":"Chapter 4752: Gamble with one’s life","paragraphs":["\"Hiss!\"","\"This... this is impossible!\"","The few figures who had emerged from the shadows, along with the black-robed men surrounding them, stared in unadulterated horror, gasping in shock as they watched the scene unfold. The profound shock reverberated through them, their hearts thundering as if their entire beings had been violently overturned. Their bodies trembled uncontrollably, and their eyes were wide with unadulterated fear.","\"Pfftttt! Cough...\"","The old man, lying on the ground, twitched violently, his life rapidly ebbing away. His complexion was deathly pale, and his entire body quickly shriveled, becoming aged and emaciated. He spat out another mouthful of blood, coughing painfully. With each agonizing cough, more blood spilled from his mouth, and his body convulsed. No one dared to approach him, for everyone present knew he was on the precipice of death.","After a long, unsettling silence, a low, cold voice echoed from seemingly nowhere: \"Someone powerful cast a defensive spell on him, so the force of that blow was reflected back as much as possible, but after that blow, the defensive spell on him was broken. If we don't kill him now, when will we?\"","At the very same moment, within Yunxiao Mountain, the Azure Emperor, who had been reclining on a soft couch in his cave abode with his eyes closed, suddenly snapped them open. A low voice, tinged with a hint of icy coldness, escaped his lips as if he were speaking to himself.","\"Someone actually dared to lay a hand on my disciple? They must be tired of living.\"","As soon as the chilling words fell, he slowly closed his eyes once more, appearing as though he had simply drifted back to sleep.","Meanwhile, Hao'er listened to the voice echoing in the air and watched as the Divine King cultivators surrounded him, stopping a few meters away. Some raised their hands, coalescing powerful air currents, while others gripped their swords. Some gathered flames in their palms. A potent, murderous aura, accompanied by immense pressure, emanated from their bodies, filling the air and knocking the children in the small black room unconscious.","\"No matter who you are! No matter what you are, today, you will not leave here alive! Die!\"","As the murderous voice faded, several individuals attacked him simultaneously. In an instant, there was a whooshing sound as air currents, searing flames, and deadly sword qi struck from three directions, rushing towards Hao'er with absolute speed and overwhelming momentum!","Hao'er felt the terrifying pressure and the suffocating killing intent. He knew he couldn't dodge or withstand such a combined assault. Despair and the chilling aura of death seemed to envelop him. Suddenly, his master's words flashed through his mind. His master had said that they were gaining experience separately, and even if he wasn't physically with them, he would still know everything they encountered and experienced. His master had also said that if he encountered something he couldn't solve or a danger he couldn't escape, he could call for him, but that would also mean he would fail the once-a-year assessment.","Therefore, in this critical moment, in this fleeting instant, countless thoughts and emotions surged through his mind. But in the end, he gritted his teeth and forced himself to endure it, simultaneously stopping the Silver Wolf that instinctively sought to emerge from his spatial realm to protect him.","He was gambling! He was gambling that his master would absolutely appear!","\"Whoosh! Boom!\"","\"Arghhhhh!\"","The sound of rushing air was followed by a loud bang, and in the next moment, a piercing scream rang out..."]},{"number":4753,"title":"Chapter 4753: Master is here!","paragraphs":["Chapter 4753: Master is here!","The air rippled as a figure appeared before Hao’er, almost like a god. With one hand casually behind his back and the other held in front of his abdomen, powerful air currents surged around him. A terrifying aura and immense pressure filled the space, captivating the very soul of anyone present.","“Master!” Hao’er exclaimed in surprise, his eyes sparkling with pure joy. He knew it, he just knew his Master would come to save him!","At that moment, the Divine Kings who had attacked Hao’er were hurled to the ground, one after another, by an unseen, powerful airflow. They spat blood, their faces pale with terror as they stared at the suddenly materialized, potent figure.","“Who are you?” one of them managed to gasp.","The Azure Emperor stood, hands behind his back, his indifferent, profound gaze sweeping coldly over the fallen Divine King cultivators. He remained silent, but simply raised his hand. Instantly, the Divine King cultivators lying on the ground were lifted into the air by a powerful, visible airflow.","“No, don’t, don’t kill us... Don’t kill... Ah!”","Before their desperate pleas for mercy could fully escape, the Azure Emperor’s raised hand spread open, then suddenly clenched into a fist. As his hand closed, several sickening cracking sounds echoed through the space, and the heads of those cultivators tilted sharply to the side. Their breaths were cut off in an instant.","“Puff!”","Further away, those black-robed cultivators were also violently shaken by the overwhelming pressure. Their meridians severed, they spat out mouthfuls of blood and collapsed, one after another.","After dispatching those individuals, the Azure Emperor raised an eyebrow and spoke in a low, indifferent voice, “You want to run? Come out!” With a wave of his sleeve, a figure was pulled seemingly from nowhere and thrown heavily onto the ground in front of him.","“Azure Emperor!”","The middle-aged man, who had been forcibly pulled out and thrown to the ground, was utterly pale, his eyes wide with fear. He scrambled to his feet and immediately knelt before the Azure Emperor. “Azure Emperor, spare my life, Azure Emperor, spare my life...”","“You recognize me?” The Azure Emperor narrowed his eyes, glancing at the man. He had no recollection of him whatsoever.","“Your Majesty, I am a subordinate of the Great Emperor of Northern Flame. Many years ago, I had the honor of seeing the Azure Emperor’s holy face.” The man quickly composed himself, hoping that merely mentioning the Great Emperor of Northern Flame’s name would at least grant him some respect and spare his life.","Unexpectedly, as soon as he finished speaking, he heard an indifferent voice, devoid of any emotion.","“Oh? So you’re from Northern Flame? Then you should be killed even more!”","The moment the Azure Emperor spoke, he waved his sleeve. The man kneeling before him seemed to be suddenly crushed by an invisible mountain. His entire body slammed forward with a resounding bang, and his head was violently severed, splattering blood across the ground. The head rolled to a stop in the corner.","This horrifying scene unfolded in an instant, so swiftly that even Hao’er, standing behind the Azure Emperor, couldn’t react in time. He was stunned, staring at the man’s severed head.","“Hurry up and treat your wounds!” The Azure Emperor turned his attention to Hao’er.","“Master, can we save them all?” Hao’er asked, looking at the children who had all fainted under the immense pressure.","“You can’t even take care of yourself, and you still have time to worry about others?” The Azure Emperor glanced at him. “I didn’t come here in my true form; only a fragment of my body appeared. If you want to save them, you have to do it yourself.”","Hearing this, Hao’er immediately asked, “Master, should we kill all the cultivators here?”","The Azure Emperor looked at him. “This place should be a training camp for death soldiers. The leaders are all dead, so you go and deal with the rest.”"]},{"number":4754,"title":"Chapter 4754: A Gift","paragraphs":["Chapter 4754: A Gift","While he was speaking, Hao’er swiftly pulled out a piece of cloth and some bleeding-stop medicine, quickly bandaging the deepest wound on his body. Only then did he respectfully bow to the Azure Emperor and say, “Disciple thanks his master for saving him.”","“Let’s go! I’ll protect you for a while longer,” the Azure Emperor said. He had originally intended to let Hao’er handle the remaining tasks himself, but upon seeing his disciple’s deep wound, he changed his mind and stepped forward.","Seeing this, a rare smile appeared on Hao’er’s face, and he replied loudly, “Yes!” then quickly followed. He didn’t know why his Master had changed his mind. He only knew that his Master, who had initially instructed him to manage the situation alone, had now accompanied him. Hao’er didn’t even need to lift a finger as his Master effortlessly dealt with all the remaining black-robed cultivators outside.","“Return to the mountain as soon as possible after this matter is resolved. We’re only missing you now,” the Azure Emperor said, glancing at Hao’er beside him.","“Yes, disciple understands,” Hao’er replied respectfully.","“Clean yourself up when you return, so the two little ones won’t worry,” the Azure Emperor added lightly.","“Yes,” Hao’er nodded, a warm feeling flowing through his heart.","As soon as his Master’s voice faded, the figure standing before him vanished. Remembering the Azure Emperor’s words about this being only a fragment of his essence, Hao’er made a silent resolution in his heart: he would work diligently to cultivate so that one day, even his fragment of power would be as formidable as his Master’s.","At that moment, he quickly refocused his mind and set about handling the immediate tasks.","Meanwhile, back on Yunxiao Mountain, in his serene cave abode, the Azure Emperor, who had been resting on a soft couch, slowly opened his eyes. He stood up, elegantly dusted off his robe, and walked outside. After leaving the cave abode, he proceeded leisurely to a stone table beneath a tree and sat down. From his spatial ring, he produced some wine and a wine cup, savoring the tranquil peace of the moment.","However, after a while, he heard a soft and sweet voice approaching from afar.","“Master, Master!” Yue’er skipped and jumped towards him, quickly reaching his front. With the eagerness of someone presenting a treasure, she pulled something from her spatial ring. “Master, Master, look, I brought you a gift when I came back.”","The Azure Emperor looked at her as she opened the small box in her hand and took out a jet-black hairpin that glowed with a subtle, moist sheen. She presented it to him as if it were the most precious item in the world.","“Master, Master, look, isn’t it beautiful? I sold some fierce beasts for money and bought this with the money,” Yue’er said with a bright smile as she offered him the hairpin.","The three children had been following their Master here for a year now. Their Master was incredibly kind and had taken meticulous care of them. So, when Yue’er went out this time, she made sure to earn some extra money, specifically intending to buy a gift for him.","When he saw the hairpin, the Azure Emperor’s eyes flashed subtly. He knew everything they had experienced during their outdoor training, so he was well aware that this little girl had meticulously collected the skins or horns of fierce beasts, or perhaps some medicinal pills, and sold them for a considerable sum. She had then visited the Eight Treasures Tower to select something, ultimately choosing this hairpin. He had initially thought it was a gift for her father, but he hadn’t expected it to be for him.","Thinking of this, his eyes softened. He picked up the black jade hairpin. “Hmm, I’ll accept this gift,” he said gently.","“Hee hee, do you like it, Master?” Yue’er asked him with a wide smile, tilting her little head back, like a child eagerly awaiting praise."]},{"number":4755,"title":"Chapter 4755: Do You Like It?","paragraphs":["Chapter 4755: Do You Like It?","The Azure Emperor glanced at her, a gentle smile gracing his lips. “It’s very beautiful. I like it very much,” he said softly.","“Great! I knew you would like it, Master!” She clapped her hands happily and cheered. Without waiting for him to speak further, she turned and ran back the way she came, shouting, “Master, I’m going to play with my brother. We’re going to wait for Big Brother to come back at the foot of the mountain!”","Watching the little girl skip away, the Azure Emperor finally withdrew his gaze and looked at the black jade hairpin in his hand. He took the white jade hairpin from his own hair and held the two hairpins, one black and one white, side by side. He shook his head and smiled indulgently, his low voice a mere whisper. “This girl, she always gives the same gifts.”","Thinking of his disciple who had endured so much and now returned to his side, growing up in the same way, a profound joy filled his heart. This time, no matter what, he vowed to protect her, ensuring she would never be hurt again, let alone suffer the pain of reincarnation.","At the foot of the mountain, Muchen and Yue’er sat on the steps. Yue’er hummed a little tune as she gazed at the winding mountain road. “Brother,” she said, “should we send someone to ask where Big Brother is? Why isn’t he back yet?”","“I asked him when you went to find Master just now,” Muchen replied, idly playing with a piece of wood. “He said he was delayed by something, but he’s already on his way back here. He probably won’t make it today, and it’ll take at least two or three days at the earliest.” He then asked, “Little sister, did he like the gift you gave him?”","“Mm-hmm, Master said the hairpin is very pretty and he likes it very much!” Yue’er said with a wide smile, clearly very happy that her gift had been well-received.","“How did you think of giving him a hairpin?” Muchen inquired.","“Because Master has everything!” she explained with a happy smile. “I didn’t know what else to give him. Medicinal pills are consumed and then gone, and Master definitely has more treasures than we do. I noticed that Master only had that white jade hairpin on his head, and he had been wearing it for so long without changing it, so I thought, ‘Does Master not have any other hairpins?’ Since he already has a white jade one, I bought him a black jade hairpin.” Her little face glowed with satisfaction. “Now my master will have two hairpins and can switch between them.”","The brother and sister chatted there until darkness fell, then they walked back to their cave abode.","A few days later, Hao’er finally arrived at the foot of the mountain. His injuries had forced him to slow his journey, but he still managed to return within the month. As soon as he reached the mountain base, he saw his younger brother and sister waiting for him.","“Big Brother!”","“Big Brother!”","The two shouted, quickly rushing to his side. However, as they drew closer, they immediately noticed that he looked considerably worse than usual; his face was notably pale.","“Big Brother, are you okay? Why do you look so bad? Are you too tired?” Yue’er asked, coming right up to him and looking him up and down. Upon closer inspection, her little face was filled with worry.","“Big Brother, are you hurt? Are you seriously injured? I can smell blood on you. Where are you hurt? Have you applied medicine?” Yue’er questioned anxiously, her voice a flurry of concern.","“Big Brother, here,” Muchen said, ever more direct. He quickly took a nourishing medicine from his spatial ring and handed it to Hao’er.","Seeing their genuine concern, Hao’er managed a weak smile."]},{"number":4756,"title":"Chapter 4756: Going Out","paragraphs":["Chapter 4756: Going Out","“I’m fine, don’t worry, it’s just a few minor injuries, and I’ve already applied medicine,” Hao’er reassured them. “I used Mother’s medicine, so the wounds will heal quickly. Maybe I’m just a little tired from rushing back here. It’s nothing serious.” He then told Muchen, “Put the medicinal pills away. Big Brother has some in his space, and we also took some on the way here.”","Hearing this, Muchen paused, recalling that their mother had indeed prepared a generous supply of medicinal pills for all three of them. He then put the pills away.","“Big Brother, come sit down and rest for a while,” Yue’er said, taking his hand and leading him to the stone steps. She then produced some water. “Big Brother, drink some water!”","“Yeah.” Hao’er didn’t refuse her kindness. He took the water and drank a few sips, feeling his throat soften a little. He then asked, “How long have you two been waiting here?”","“We came down here in the morning, but we weren’t slacking off! My brother and I were practicing our techniques here just now,” Yue’er said with a smile.","“Did you encounter any danger on your way back?” Hao’er inquired. He hadn’t asked in detail via the communication jade, so now that they were together, he wanted to know.","“There was no danger, just some things we could handle. None of us were hurt!” Yue’er replied.","“Yeah, it was just some small stuff,” Muchen added, looking at Hao’er. “Did you encounter someone very powerful, Big Brother?”","“It’s a long story. I’ll tell you all about it after we see our master!” After resting for a while, Hao’er stood up. “Let’s go see our master first.”","“Alright, Master said that once you were back, we should all go together,” Yue’er said, also standing up.","The three siblings headed up the mountain together. When they arrived in front of their master’s cave abode, Hao’er called out, “Master, your disciples are back.”","“Master, we’re here too,” Yue’er chimed in.","“Come in!” The Azure Emperor’s voice resonated from inside the cave abode.","The three outside heard him and exchanged glances before walking in. Inside, they found their master sitting at a stone table, calmly drinking tea. Next to him lay something that resembled a piece of paper.","“Greetings, Master.” The three bowed respectfully.","“Mm.”","The Azure Emperor responded faintly, his gaze sweeping over the three of them. “You all did very well in this test. You completed your tasks within a month, even though there were some unexpected incidents along the way.”","As he spoke, his gaze fell on Hao’er. “Are your injuries healed?” he asked.","“Master, all my minor injuries have healed, only one wound is a little deep and hasn’t completely recovered, but it’s no big deal,” Hao’er said respectfully. At the same time, he took a cosmos sack from his space. “Master, these are the crystal cores I hunted down.”","“Keep them for yourselves! They’re of no use to me, not to mention that you earned them yourselves,” the Azure Emperor said slowly. He looked at the three of them, continuing in a gentle tone, “Considering your good performance this time, in three days, I will take you to a banquet to broaden your horizons. In these three days, those who need to recover from their injuries should do so, and those who need to cultivate should cultivate. We will set off in three days.”","Hearing this, Hao’er and Muchen remained calm; neither of them particularly enjoyed grand events. However, Yue’er’s eyes lit up, and she excitedly asked, “Master, does that mean we can all go out and play with you?”"]},{"number":4757,"title":"Chapter 4757: Caught","paragraphs":["Chapter 4757: Caught","“Mm,” the Azure Emperor nodded, his expression softening slightly. He then produced three immortal fruits from his spatial ring. “These are rewards for the three of you. Take them back and eat them. They will increase your spirit energy by a hundred years.”","“Thank you, Master!” the three exclaimed in unison, happily stepping forward to receive the fruits. After bowing respectfully, they retreated.","At the same time, in the East Sea Spirit Realm, where Xuanyuan Mo Ze nurtured his soul, Gu Mo, one of the Phoenix Guards, was on patrol with his men. Ever since their Master left, the eight Phoenix Guards had taken turns stationed here.","Strange phenomena occurred occasionally in this realm, and even their constant vigilance couldn’t fully deter the curiosity and adventurous spirit of certain cultivators. The Phoenix Guards knew that Hell’s Lord existed within the sea, which was why they maintained their watch. However, to outsiders, this area was rumored to hold great treasures, so despite the risk of death, there were always those willing to venture in.","“Captain, we’ve caught three loose cultivators who were trying to sneak into the sea,” a Phoenix Guard reported.","Gu Mo, who was patrolling the sea, frowned. “Take them to the sandy area by the sea.” With that, he led his team back.","It was almost noon, and although approaching the East Sea Spirit Realm was strictly forbidden, quite a few cultivators still loitered in the surrounding area. Thus, when they saw the Phoenix Guards dragging three cultivators towards the sandy beach, the distant onlookers couldn’t help but turn their gazes.","“Let me go, let me go! Who are you to arrest me?” One of the captured cultivators struggled, attempting to break free. But he was held firmly by the highly trained Phoenix Guards, who would not allow an easy escape.","“We didn’t do anything, what do you want? Let us go!” another shouted, trying to maintain composure, though fear flickered in his eyes.","“This East Sea Spirit Realm isn’t your territory. So what if we snuck in? Let us go!” a third person cried out, but received no response.","The Phoenix Guards escorted them to the sandy beach, then sharply kicked them behind the knees, shouting coldly, “Kneel!” As they roared the command, they simultaneously pressed down with their hands.","“Arghhh!”","The three cultivators, caught off guard by the kick, cried out in pain as their knees buckled, forcing them instinctively to their knees.","“Captain!”","The Phoenix Guards saluted respectfully as Gu Mo returned, their voices loud and clear, audible even to the cultivators watching from a distance.","The three kneeling cultivators raised their heads and looked at the figure before them. He was dressed in a simple yet elegant purple robe with a jade belt around his waist, and a Phoenix Guard captain’s badge was pinned to his side. Looking up, they saw his handsome face, an indifferent expression, and the imposing aura of a high-ranking official. This was one of the eight Phoenix Guard captains under the legendary Ghost Doctor, Feng Jiu!","The three of them froze, their breathing becoming erratic. They trembled slightly, overwhelmed by panic and terror.","“Cultivators are not allowed to approach this area of the East Sea Spirit Realm. Don’t you know that?” Gu Mo’s voice was cold and sharp as ice.","“We... we didn’t do anything...” one of them stammered, his lips quivering slightly. “Don’t... don’t kill us, we really... we really didn’t do anything, we... we just wanted to go into the sea to see if there was an Immortal Palace...”","Hearing this, Gu Mo glanced at them indifferently. “There is no such place as what you call ‘Immortal Palace’ in this sea,” he stated."]},{"number":4758,"title":"Chapter 4758: Inquiry","paragraphs":["Chapter 4758: Inquiry","With his hands behind his back, Gu Mo’s voice was indifferent but deep. Although the spirit energy contained within it didn’t sound particularly loud, it carried clearly, reaching the ears of the cultivators observing from a distance.","“We, the Phoenix Guards, are here on our Master’s orders to guard this place. Anyone who crosses the line drawn by us will be considered an enemy of our Master, and we will not show mercy to our enemies.”","He glanced at the three cultivators kneeling on the ground and then ordered the Phoenix Guards beside him, “Destroy their cultivation and expel them from the border to fend for themselves! If anyone else crosses the border and tries to enter the East Sea Spirit Realm, kill them on the spot once they are caught!”","“Yes!” The Phoenix Guards replied respectfully, then proceeded to destroy the three cultivators’ cultivation and throw them outside the marked border.","With their cultivation destroyed, the three let out piercing screams that sent a chilling sensation down the spines of the distant cultivators. As cultivators, with their very foundation destroyed, they likely wouldn’t live much longer. After all, individuals who had cultivated to that level were already quite old, and once stripped of their power, they naturally had no means of survival.","“What do you think is in the bottom of the East Sea that is worth them guarding it so fiercely?” one cultivator whispered.","“There are no immortal treasures in the sea, yet they refuse to let anyone enter. The more secretive they are, the more it arouses our curiosity. However, you’ve seen the fate of those who were caught. Almost none of them survived.”","“I really want to know what’s in the sea.”","The cultivators murmured amongst themselves, but no matter how curious they were, they had no way of knowing what the Phoenix Guards were truly protecting.","Just then, several beams of light descended from the sky, landing on the sandy shore directly in front of Gu Mo. Gu Mo looked at the newly arrived group. There were three old men, a woman, and a middle-aged man dressed in an elaborate robe. All of them exuded immense power, but the three old men and the woman positioned themselves behind the middle-aged man, who appeared to be their master.","“Are you Gu Mo, one of the Eight Phoenix Guards?” The middle-aged man in the brocade robe smiled, looking at Gu Mo, and nodded. “As expected, the Ghost Doctor has no weak soldiers. I didn’t expect someone so young to have such cultivation.”","“Who are you? What are you doing here?” Gu Mo asked, his gaze fixed intently on the other party.","The middle-aged man waved his sleeve, instantly creating a soundproof barrier around them. Then he said, “I am Nancheng Monarch. I am here to ask you something.” He shifted his gaze from Gu Mo to the East Sea and asked, “Are you guarding this place because the Green Dragon is in the East Sea?”","Upon hearing this, Gu Mo’s eyes flashed, and he briefly glanced at the ruler. He knew that Hell’s Lord had disappeared after undergoing tribulation, and that the heavens and earth under his control had experienced tremendous upheaval. Others might not know the specifics, but the monarchs of the various realms were more or less aware.","Additionally, there had been recent abnormalities in the East Sea, and they had been ordered to guard this place. Given their intelligence, it wasn’t difficult for these rulers to guess what was happening. Therefore, Gu Mo did not hide anything and stated, “That’s right, Hell’s Lord is in this spirit realm, so my lord ordered us to guard this place.”","His Master had instructed him long ago that if any monarchs inquired about this matter, he should tell them the truth. She did not want those monarchs to disturb Hell’s Lord’s cultivation out of mere curiosity.","Hearing Gu Mo’s direct confirmation, Nancheng Monarch was slightly surprised. He had thought that even if he personally questioned Gu Mo, he probably wouldn’t reveal such sensitive information, but he did not expect....."]},{"number":4759,"title":"Chapter 4759: The Summit of the Snow Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 4759: The Summit of the Snow Mountain","“I see, thank you for telling me,” Nancheng Monarch said, nodding slightly with a smile. “Actually, I am not the only one who came to ask today. The other monarchs are also very curious, so I made this trip. I hope you will not misunderstand.”","Gu Mo’s expression remained indifferent. “My Master has already made it clear that if the monarchs of all realms come to ask, we should tell them the truth. First, it is to let you know why we are stationed here, and second, it is also in the hope that the monarchs of all realms will not disturb Hell’s Lord’s quiet cultivation and rest. Furthermore, this matter can be passed on to the rulers of all realms, but my Master has also clearly stated that if, after learning the reason, anyone still dares to come here and disturb Hell’s Lord’s rest, she will not rest until they are dealt with!”","Nancheng Monarch’s eyes flashed, his heart stirring. The implication was clear: he would convey this information, but if anyone dared to disturb the Green Dragon’s quiet rest after knowing the truth, the Ghost Doctor, Feng Jiu, would show no mercy.","Considering the formidable methods of Feng Jiu, Nancheng Monarch smiled. “I understand. After I return, I will definitely inform the other monarchs of what the Ghost Doctor said. I won’t disturb your patrol anymore. We’ll meet again someday.” He bowed, took a deep look at Gu Mo, then waved his hand to remove the soundproof barrier and departed with his entourage.","Watching them leave, Gu Mo ordered his Phoenix Guards to intensify patrols of the surrounding area and dispatched another team to patrol the sea itself. He then took out his communication jade and informed his Master, who was currently traveling, about the Nancheng Monarch’s inquiry.","On the other side, Feng Jiu was wandering alone and had recently arrived at Sky Mountain. The last time she had attempted to visit, she couldn’t enter due to a barrier. This time, however, she effortlessly entered the barrier alone. Instead of heading to the cave abode where Mo Chen was cultivating his immortal body, she ascended to the snowy peak at the top of Sky Mountain, a place where Old Man Tianji often meditated.","She sat cross-legged, her eyes closed, losing all sense of time. Her vibrant red robe became covered with a palm-thick layer of snow, and even her jet-black hair was dyed white by the accumulating flakes. She sat there motionless, as if she had become one with the heavens and the earth. Without a close inspection, it would have been impossible to discern that a living person was present.","At the pinnacle of the snow-capped mountain, a profound silence reigned, broken only by the soft whisper of falling snowflakes and the mournful howl of the wind. After an unknown duration, she slowly opened her eyes. At that moment, her eyelashes, adorned with delicate snowflakes, fluttered lightly as she raised her gaze, causing the flakes to fall gently.","Gazing at the pristine white expanse before her, she slightly parted her lips and exhaled a breath of stale air. Instantly, a refreshing sensation coursed through her entire body, as if a pure energy had flowed through her with the exhalation, leaving her feeling incredibly comfortable.","She remained seated, regulating the spirit energy within her body. As the energy flowed, the snow on her body scattered and melted away. In that moment, her dazzling red robe stood out even more vividly against the white snow.","She took the communication jade from her spatial realm and listened to Gu Mo’s message. Holding the communication jade, she gazed straight ahead, her expression inscrutable.","After a long period of contemplation, she finally stood up, gently brushing her robe, which created a beautiful arc in the air. She turned to look at Mo Chen’s cave abode and began walking towards it, one steady step at a time."]},{"number":4760,"title":"Chapter 4760: Immortal Body Condenses","paragraphs":["Chapter 4760: Immortal Body Condenses","When she arrived in front of the cave abode, Feng Jiu stopped and looked at the door covered with a barrier, her eyes flashing slightly. Old Man Tianji died because of Mo Ze, and Mo Chen died because of her. Now that it was difficult for him to condense his immortal body, she felt compelled to help him, no matter what, so that he could condense his immortal body, ascend to the heavens, and enjoy eternal life. Although she hadn’t yet ascended herself, she now possessed sufficient ability and believed she could help him.","She raised her hand and gently waved it, and the barrier in front of her shattered. She stepped inside and walked forward step by step until she saw the golden lotus sealed in ice.","On a piece of ice in the cave abode stood a half-meter-high block of ice. Within it, a golden lotus emitted a faint glow. Because it was frozen in ice, the aura of the golden lotus did not spread, but Feng Jiu, standing there, could clearly sense the familiar aura emanating from it.","“Golden Lotus incarnation, gather and ascend. Mo Chen, you have sacrificed so much for me, it is time for me to do something for you,” she murmured softly. She slowly raised her hand to touch the ice. A pure spirit energy, accompanied by the rich energy of the Primordial Blue Lotus, slowly seeped into the ice and headed towards the golden lotus inside.","A green light gradually rose from Feng Jiu’s body, enveloping her entire form. The aura of the Blue Lotus and the pure spirit energy were continuously injected into the golden lotus in the ice. The golden lotus, which had originally only emitted a gentle light, gradually grew stronger, and its half-closed lotus petals slowly began to open.","As time passed, Feng Jiu stood there, diligently controlling the Blue Lotus energy and pure spirit energy within her body, transferring it into the golden lotus. This continued for two days.","“Crack!”","The sound of ice cracking echoed through the cave abode. A small crack appeared on the cold ice, slowly extending and expanding.","“Crack!”","Another crack reverberated, and more and more cracks appeared on the ice, gradually covering the entire half-person-high block. In the next moment, the ice cracked again, and this time, it shattered directly, scattering all over the ground and turning into countless fragments that fell onto the ice stone, then transformed into water and vanished without a trace.","Simultaneously, the entire cave abode was bathed in a dazzling golden light. Feng Jiu could feel a gentle aura spreading along with the light of the golden lotus.","Feng Jiu found the light of the golden lotus a little dazzling, so she looked away slightly. But in the very next moment, she felt a powerful fluctuation in the air and a familiar aura spreading.","She turned her head abruptly and saw that the light of the golden lotus had dissipated, and even the golden lotus itself had disappeared without a trace. However, what appeared in its place was a familiar person: Mo Chen.","He was still dressed in his customary snow-white, flowing robes, his jet-black hair falling loosely, looking natural and exquisitely beautiful. A faint, golden, holy light emanated from his body, enveloping him in a radiant glow, making him appear sacred and otherworldly. Unlike before, this time his body was no longer illusory; it was a true immortal body formed from the golden lotus.","Between his eyebrows, a perfectly blooming golden lotus flower appeared, adding an air of profound sacredness to his already handsome features. He seemed like a fallen immortal, noble, pure, and utterly untouchable."]},{"number":4761,"title":"Chapter 4761: Mo Chen Ascends","paragraphs":["Chapter 4761: Mo Chen Ascends","“Ah Jiu.”","Mo Chen’s gentle voice slowly drifted out, and a faint smile appeared on his immortal face. His deep and calm gaze fell on Feng Jiu, who was dressed in red in front of him.","“Mo Chen.” Feng Jiu saw him and also smiled, “Today, I will help you ascend.”","“Congratulations on your achievement of Blue Lotus,” Mo Chen said gently, looking at her and saying, “Now that I have attained an immortal body, you no longer need to help me. Once I have endured the lightning tribulation, I will be able to ascend to immortality.”","“Ninety-nine lightning tribulations is no small feat,” said Feng Jiu.","Hearing this, Mo Chen shook his head slightly, a gentle smile on his lips: “I am an immortal body formed from the transformation of a golden lotus. The lightning tribulations will only strengthen my immortal body and will not hinder me.”","Hearing this, Feng Jiu was slightly surprised: “Ninety-nine lightning tribulations will only strengthen your immortal body?”","“Yes, you’ve forgotten that I’m no ordinary cultivator. My physical body has long since dissipated, and what has now been condensed is an immortal body. The lightning tribulation is harmless to me. On the contrary, it only has benefits.” As if sensing the changes in the sky, he looked at her and said, “The lightning is gathering, and the clouds are changing color. Ah Jiu, I have to go.”","As soon as he finished speaking, he slowly walked outside. His footsteps seemed to be stepping on the ground, but upon closer inspection, he was actually walking on the wind without touching the ground.","Feng Jiu saw him leave the cave abode and quickly followed him outside. As soon as she left the cave abode, she felt the terrifying air currents in the sky gather at the top of Sky Mountain, with clouds rolling and thunder rumbling in the clouds.","This scene was so similar to when Mo Ze advanced, that Feng Jiu’s heart leapt. However, when she thought of what Mo Chen had just said, she couldn’t help but look at him.","She saw that he looked calm and walked slowly to the top of the mountain, where he stopped and turned to look at her.","“Ah Jiu, today I am ascending, and we will only meet again in the Immortal Realm. I hope you will safely pass the tribulation and that everything will be fine.”","He spoke slowly, looked at her deeply with a calm and profound gaze, then withdrew his gaze, turned around, sat cross-legged in the snow, and placed his hands in a lotus position between his knees.","“I will. We will meet again in the Immortal Realm,” Feng Jiu said softly, stepping back a little to protect him and watch him ascend safely.","“Boom!”","In the sky, a loud clap of thunder rang out from the clouds, and the sound of the lightning tribulation and the roaring wind and clouds startled everyone at that moment.","“Boom!”","As a flash of lightning streaked across the sky, the first bolt of lightning thundered down, striking Mo Chen below and sending a powerful gust of wind rippling through the air.","Seeing that Mo Chen was still sitting quietly after being struck by lightning, she finally let go of her heart.","It seemed that it was indeed as he had said, that his ascension to immortality and the lightning tribulation would only strengthen his immortal body and be beneficial to him. With that, she felt at ease.","At the same time, the monarchs of all realms were startled by the sound of the lightning, and several of them were talking about the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm. Upon hearing the sound of the lightning, they immediately left the hall and came outside.","“Is that the sound of ascension lightning?” one of them asked in shock.","“Could it be that the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu has ascended?” Another person also looked up at the sky in shock.","“Besides her, who else could it be in this area?” Nancheng Monarch paused for a moment and said, “Why don’t we go take a look?”"]},{"number":4762,"title":"Chapter 4762: In Accordance With the Will of Heaven","paragraphs":["Chapter 4762: In Accordance With the Will of Heaven","Hearing this, the group exchanged glances and immediately said, “Let’s go!” As soon as the words left their mouths, they flicked their sleeves and instantly turned into several streaks of light that shot toward the sky...","At the same time, in the Upper Immortal Realm, when the Four Great Emperors sensed the commotion below, their expressions suddenly turned extremely ugly.","“Could it be that Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu has ascended?” They all guessed at the same time. In their opinion, the only one who could have ascended was Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu. Apart from her, no one else would dare to try, and even if they wanted to, it would be difficult to find an opportunity.","At that moment, they came to their respective water realms, waved their sleeves, and saw the person in the lower realm undergoing the lightning tribulation and ascending from within the water realm.","“Who is this person?”","They were unfamiliar with Mo Chen, so they couldn’t guess who he was at this moment. But seeing that person with his eyes closed, his outstanding appearance and refined temperament, they couldn’t help but praise him secretly.","“I didn’t expect that besides Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu, there were also such fallen immortals in the lower immortal realm. This is truly unexpected...”","“Huh? This person is already an immortal body?” An emperor took a closer look and was very surprised to see that the person below who was being tempered by the lightning tribulation was already an immortal body.","“Since he has an immortal body, his ascension is in accordance with the will of Heaven. It seems that another Great Emperor will be born in the Immortal Realm...”","Perhaps because they saw that the person below already had an immortal body, they did not cause any trouble, because they knew that once one had attained immortality, ascension was only a matter of following the will of Heaven. If they tried to stop him, they feared that Heaven would not forgive them.","Therefore, they swept their sleeves and turned to leave the water realm, heading outside to send messages to the other Emperors to discuss whether they could recruit this person after his ascension, as he would be a great asset in the future.","However, because Feng Jiu had retreated to a distance to protect Mo Chen, the four Great Emperors only saw Mo Chen there enduring the lightning tribulation and did not notice Feng Jiu in her red robe in the distance...","Elsewhere, the Azure Emperor, who had taken Hao’er, Muchen, and Muyue with him to attend the banquet, also sensed the commotion in the lower realm. With a wave of his sleeve, an image appeared before him.","“It’s Uncle Mo Chen!” As soon as Hao’er saw the person enduring the lightning tribulation, he couldn’t help but cry out and quickly rushed to his master’s side.","“I want to see too! I want to see too!” Yue’er also quickly came forward, blinking her big eyes as she looked at the person sitting quietly with his eyes closed: “It’s really Uncle Mo Chen!”","“Is he advancing?” Muchen asked in surprise.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the three disciples beside him and said slowly, “He is preparing to ascend. After enduring 9981 lightning tribulations, he will be able to ascend to immortality, rank among the Nine Heavenly Emperors, and live as long as heaven and earth.”","“Will he be as powerful as Master?” Yue’er looked up at him curiously.","“Yes, but even among the Nine Heavenly Emperors, there are differences in strength. I have cultivated for tens of thousands of years and cannot be compared to just anyone.” He spoke slowly, his voice calm and unhurried, with a hint of pride in his words.","“Master, will Uncle Mo Chen be in danger when he ascends?” Hao’er couldn’t help but ask worriedly. This was because he remembered what had happened to their father when he ascended and encountered the lightning tribulation.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the scene, a strange look flashing across his eyes, and said, “His immortal body is already complete. Ascending to the Nine Heavens is only in accordance with the will of Heaven. The lightning tribulations will be beneficial to him and cause him no harm.”"]},{"number":4763,"title":"Chapter 4763: Movements From All Sides","paragraphs":["Chapter 4763: Movements From All Sides","Hearing this, the three exchanged glances and smiled happily.","As long as there is no danger, maybe Uncle Mo Chen has ascended, and we will have a chance to see him again in the future!","“Mother? It’s Mother, Mother is there!” Yue’er looked at the corner of the screen with surprise. A red figure appeared, and although it was far away, they knew that it was their mother.","Upon hearing Yue’er’s words, Hao’er and Muchen’s hearts trembled, and their eyes filled with urgency as they hurriedly searched the screen. Sure enough, in the far corner, they saw a small red figure in the snow.","“It’s really Mother!” Hao’er and Muchen also showed joy on their faces. They hadn’t seen their mother in over a year.","“Master, master, I want to see Mother, we want Mother!” Yue’er tugged at Azure Emperor’s sleeve coquettishly, looking at him hopefully.","Azure Emperor glanced at the three children, then waved his hand and focused the main view on Feng Jiu in her red robe.","“Mother, Mother, Yue’er misses you so much!”Yue’er shouted at the image, knowing full well that her mother couldn’t see or hear her, but she continued to call out anyway.","“Mother, we miss you too,” said Hao’er and Muchen, their voices choked with emotion and their eyes brimming with tears. They missed their mother so much. When would they be able to see her again? When would they be able to be with their father and mother?","Seeing his three disciples on the verge of tears, the Azure Emperor waved his sleeve, and the image disappeared. He turned around, put his hands behind his back, and walked to the bow of the airship. “Practice hard. When your strength increases and you have the ability to protect yourselves, when your mother ascends to the Nine Heavens, you will naturally have the opportunity to see her.”","Hearing this, the three looked at each other, wiped the tears from their eyes, and nodded heavily, “Yes, Master, we will work hard to cultivate, and we will become very powerful in the future!”","Seeing this, the Azure Emperor nodded slightly and said, “Go rest! We still have two days to go, so rest up and don’t disgrace your master.”","“Yes!” The three replied and returned to the cabin to rest.","On the other side, when Nancheng Monarch and the others arrived at the sky where Mo Chen was advancing, they couldn’t help but be secretly surprised. They thought that it would be Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu who would ascend here, but they didn’t expect it to be Nalan Mo Chen.","“So it was him who ascended. But didn’t he disappear from the world long ago? How could this be...” One of the monarchs looked at Mo Chen, who was undergoing the lightning tribulation, with astonishment and confusion.","“Yes! In that battle back then, many cultivators saw him die protecting Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu. At that time, I saw him dissipate into the sky with my own eyes, leaving not even a corpse behind. I didn’t expect him to still be alive, and now he’s even in the ascension stage. It’s truly unbelievable...”","“Look at his body, it seems a little different. And that golden lotus between his eyebrows, could that be the Primordial Golden Lotus?” said one monarch, looking in surprise at the golden lotus between Mo Chen’s eyebrows.","The Nancheng Monarch pondered, “I wonder what kind of extraordinary encounter he had to be reborn and ascend to immortality.”","“Look, the Ghost Doctor is there protecting him!” Another monarch motioned for everyone to look. In the distance, a red figure was very conspicuous."]},{"number":4764,"title":"Chapter 4764: Illusion Ring","paragraphs":["\"Back then, the Green Dragon Monarch couldn't withstand the lightning tribulations and met with an accident. Could Nalan Mo Chen be even more powerful than the Green Dragon Monarch? Could he survive this tribulation and ascend directly?\"","\"No, look at the immortal aura surrounding him. It seems that he has already attained an immortal body, and ascending to the nine heavens is in accordance with the will of heaven. He should be different from the Green Dragon Monarch back then.\"","Hearing this, the group was startled. Upon closer inspection, they could see that this person was indeed surrounded by divine energy and was different from the others.","They did not get too close, for fear that the lightning tribulation would strike them by mistake and cause them harm. Since they were still quite far away, after figuring out what was going on, they did not intend to go up and greet Feng Jiu. Instead, they exchanged glances and left.","Feng Jiu, who was sitting cross-legged with her eyes closed, opened her eyes, glanced at the direction in which the monarchs had left, then glanced at Mo Chen in front of her, and closed her eyes again to continue her cultivation.","With her guarding the place, ordinary people would not dare to attack Mo Chen, who was in the midst of tempering, and she could also use the immortal energy around her to cultivate, which was extremely beneficial to her.","Unlike the three lightning tribulations that Mo Ze had defeated when he advanced, perhaps because Mo Chen's immortal body had already been formed, each of the lightning tribulations that struck him fell again after only about half an incense stick's worth of time. It could almost be said that there was no respite.","She could feel it here too. Just as Mo Chen had said, these lightning tribulations could only make his immortal body stronger, because after each lightning strike, the immortal energy on his body overflowed again and again. Not to mention the immortal energy that filled the surrounding area, even his own body was surrounded by immortal energy, which was very thick.","She believed that in a few days, he would be able to ascend directly to the Ninth Heaven...","Two days later, in the Upper Immortal Realm, on the airship, the Azure Emperor summoned his three disciples.","\"Master.\"","\"Master.\"","The three came before him, called out to him, looked at him, and waited quietly for him to speak.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the three of them and said, \"I have refined three illusionary artifacts for you that can change your appearance. Once you wear them, even the most powerful people will not be able to see your true faces.\"","As he spoke, he flipped his hand, and three simple rings appeared in his palm.","Hearing his words, the three looked at the three rings with curiosity. After picking them up, Yue'er asked curiously, \"Master, did you refine these? When did you refine them? You can refine illusionary artifacts? Why did you wait until now to give them to us?\"","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor glanced at her, leaned back, and said slowly,","\"These illusionary artifacts are not ordinary items. They are extremely time-consuming to refine. It took me nearly a year to refine them. After you recognize them with a drop of blood, they will change your appearance according to your original features. Once you put them on, do not take them off.\"","\"Yes, thank you, Master.\"","Hao'er and Muchen said, bit their fingers to draw blood to recognize the master, and then put the rings on their hands. The originally loose rings shrank to the size of their fingers, and then disappeared from their hands, looking as if they weren't wearing illusion rings at all.","\"Huh? They're gone?\"","Yue'er looked at her finger and said in surprise, \"Master, this really seems to be a treasure.\"","She knew that anything that could be hidden was a treasure of the immortals, but she didn't expect the illusion rings forged by her master to be so powerful."]},{"number":4765,"title":"Chapter 4765: Finally Becoming Immortal","paragraphs":["\"Sister, you look different.\" Muchen looked at her small face, his eyes flashing slightly.","She was clearly still the same person, but her appearance had changed slightly. It wasn’t that she had completely changed into a stranger, but rather that she had become three-quarters similar to her original appearance.","\"Brother, you’ve changed too!\" Yue’er looked at him, smiled and asked her big brother, \"Big Brother, are we still the same?\"","Hao’er looked carefully at their faces and shook his head, \"No, they’re not the same, just a little similar, but you can tell they’re two different people.\"","\"Big Brother, look at yourself.\" Yue’er took a mirror out of her space and held it up to him. \"Big Brother, you look good too!\"","Hao’er looked at his reflection in the mirror and saw that it was very different from his original appearance. It was only three-quarters similar to his original appearance, and if you said it was good-looking, it wasn’t actually as good-looking as his original appearance.","\"That’s good.\" This way, even if outsiders saw them, they would never think that their parents were Xuanyuan Mo Ze and Feng Jiu.","The Azure Emperor looked at the three of them and said slowly, \"This illusion ring will change your appearance as you grow up. Put it on today and don’t take it off. In the future, when you have the power to protect yourselves, you can take it off.\"","\"Yes, thank you, Master.\" The three of them replied, bowing in gratitude.","Another day passed, and Hao’er, Muchen, and Yue’er followed their master, standing at the bow of the ship, watching him point ahead and below, telling them what kind of place this was and where they were. Suddenly, they heard a loud clap of lightning, and a rainbow appeared in the distant sky, accompanied by faint heavenly music...","\"How beautiful!\"","Yue’er’s eyes lit up as she looked at the rainbow in the distance and asked, \"Master, how did the rainbow get there? It sounds like someone is playing the qin. It’s so beautiful.\"","The Azure Emperor glanced at the distance, folded his arms behind his back, and said slowly, \"It is a supernatural phenomenon in the sky caused by Mo Chen’s imminent ascension.\"","Hearing this, Hao’er and Muchen, who were standing beside him, also looked toward the distance, and smiles appeared on their faces.","Uncle Mo Chen was finally going to ascend!","At the same time, at the peak of Sky Mountain, after the last lightning tribulation fell, the spirit energy in the surrounding area surged and rose, and a swirling vortex appeared in the sky. The vortex was not the usual grayish-black color, but the bright colors of a rainbow.","It was as if a rainbow had formed a series of cloud rings, extending down from the sky above and towards Mo Chen. Within the clouds, heavenly music played, and magpies flew around the seven-colored clouds, creating a beautiful scene...","Feng Jiu stood up, her eyes shining with joy and excitement. She looked at Mo Chen in front of her, dressed in white, standing in the wind with his sleeves fluttering, his black hair flying and a smile on his lips. A sacred light enveloped him, and an ethereal aura spread around him. She watched as he looked at her with a gentle and refined smile on his immortal face, and watched as his white figure was enveloped by the golden light of the immortal aura refracted from the vortex, and his figure flew up into the sky.","\"Mo Chen, take care, we’ll see each other again someday!\"","She called out, waving her hand at him, her stunning face blooming with joy.","At that moment, seeing him finally ascend to immortality, she felt a deep sense of relief..."]},{"number":4766,"title":"Chapter 4766: Immortal Elder Lingmu","paragraphs":["With his successful ascension, the colorful vortex in the sky gradually closed, as if it had never appeared.","However, cultivators from almost all realms noticed this scene at that moment. Even though his ascension only lasted for a moment, the appearance of the immortal music and the strange phenomenon in the sky were difficult to ignore.","Feng Jiu stood at the top of Sky Mountain, looked at the surroundings that had returned to normal, then turned and glanced at the cave abode behind her, thinking of Old Man Tianji and Mo Chen.","Now, Old Man Tianji had died saving Mo Ze, and Mo Chen had ascended to the Nine Heavens of the Immortal Realm. Now, this place was empty and deserted, covered in snow and devoid of human life. Perhaps in a few years or decades, this place would be forgotten.","At this thought, her heart stirred slightly. Her gaze fell on a half-human-tall stone nearby, and she walked toward it slowly.","With a flick of her hand, the Blue Edge appeared in her hand. She infused the sharp sword with spirit energy and moved it casually, carving the words \"Immortal Peak\" on the half-human-high stone. Then, she carved smaller words below, noting that Old Man Tianji, the master of Sky Mountain, and his disciple Mo Chen had ascended to the Nine Heavens on a certain year, month, day, and time. Finally, she carved the name of the person who carved the words, Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu.","She did not leave immediately, but planned to stay here for a few more days. Because once she left, she would probably never come back.","In the Upper Immortal Realm, the Azure Emperor brought his three disciples to a floating island in the clouds. As soon as they entered the island, Yue’er couldn’t help but look around in wonder. She felt that the place was filled with immortal energy and was very beautiful.","\"Master, it’s so beautiful here, just like a fairyland,\" said Yue’er as she looked at the misty scenery around her.","\"This is the domain of the Immortal Elder Lingmu. He is a reclusive immortal. Although this island is not very big, it is rich in Spirit Energy and surrounded by fairy energy, making it very famous,\"\" said the Azure Emperor slowly as he walked forward at a leisurely pace.","When they arrived at the entrance, several immortal servants bowed to them. At this moment, the Azure Emperor handed over a note. The immortal servant opened it, glanced at it, then closed it and bowed respectfully once more.","\"Greetings, Azure Emperor.\"","The immortal attendant, dressed in flowing white robes and with a handsome face, looked at the Azure Emperor in front of him, smiled, and turned slightly to the side in a gesture of invitation: \"Azure Emperor, please come in. My immortal master is waiting inside.\"","The Azure Emperor nodded slightly and led his three disciples behind him to follow an attendant inside.","There, the immortals were gathered and chatting happily. An old man with white hair and beard stroked his beard and laughed, \"Immortal Elder Lingmu, I heard that the Azure Emperor will also be attending this banquet. Is that true?\"","\"The Azure Emperor is coming too? He never likes to attend banquets. No matter how many people invite him, he never comes. Immortal Elder Lingmu, you really have great influence!\" said a man in a purple robe sitting on the other side, his eyes filled with surprise.","\"Hehehe, I sent him an invitation, but I didn’t expect him to accept. I’m very surprised too! After all, he has been in seclusion for many years, and even when he comes out, he only stays in his Yunxiao Mountain and never goes out. I didn’t expect him to come this time.\" Immortal Elder Lingmu said with a smile, \"But you may not know that I heard the Azure Emperor mention that he has newly accepted three disciples, and he will bring them with him this time.\""]},{"number":4767,"title":"Chapter 4767: Which Family Are They From?","paragraphs":["\"Oh? I see, no wonder you told us to bring the younger generation along. So that's why!\" The other person also laughed, seeming very interested in the Azure Emperor's arrival.","\"The Azure Emperor took a disciple back then, but that disciple later died in a calamity. I didn't expect him to take three more disciples. However, many people want to become disciples of the Azure Emperor but don't have the chance. I'm sure these three disciples must have something special about them. It's perfect, we can take this opportunity to meet them today.\" Immortal Elder Lingmu smiled as he said this and looked at the younger generation sitting behind their master.","\"The disciples of the Azure Emperor must be extraordinary people. It's a rare opportunity to see them, so we naturally can't miss it.\" Everyone laughed and felt very excited.","Outside, the Azure Emperor and his entourage were walking slowly toward the entrance.","They were walking on a small stone path lined with strange flowers and fruits on both sides. A gentle breeze blew, and the fragrance of flowers and fruits filled the air. Even Hao'er and the others had never seen such a place before. They felt as if every pore in their bodies had opened up and was breathing, and it was extremely comfortable.","After walking for a long time, turning left and right, they finally arrived at an archway formed by flower vines. Bright and beautiful flowers were in full bloom on the archway, and four handsome immortals stood there. Seeing them arrive, the four bowed slightly, and from inside, a voice rang out.","\"The Azure Emperor has arrived!\"","The people inside were chatting and talking, but upon hearing the title of the visitor, they all stood up with smiles and went to greet him.","Even the Immortal Elder Lingmu in the seat of honor stood up with a smile and walked forward to the archway to greet him. When he saw the Azure Emperor, who was still as handsome and dignified as ever, the Immortal Elder Lingmu smiled and bowed his hands, \"Azure Emperor, it's been many years, you look as handsome as ever!\"","\"Immortal Elder Lingmu.\" The Azure Emperor returned the greeting with a slight smile on his face. He looked at the others, nodded slightly, and said, \"My fellow immortals.\"","\"Greetings, Azure Emperor.\" The others did not dare to accept his greeting. They turned slightly to the side and only gave a half-bow in return. After all, he was of a different status, so they could not treat him the same.","Even though the Azure Emperor lived in seclusion and did not concern himself with worldly affairs, he was still a great emperor, and they could not be disrespectful to him. Therefore, when they saw him, they all bowed respectfully and took their places below him.","\"We were just talking about the Azure Emperor, and here he is. These three must be his new disciples.\" Immortal Elder Lingmu had a long-standing friendship with the Azure Emperor, so he spoke more casually and naturally, unlike the others who were more reserved.","His gaze passed over the Azure Emperor and fell on the three children behind him. He was a little surprised that the Azure Emperor's three new disciples were so young.","\"Yes, these three little ones have been with me for a year now.\" As the Azure Emperor spoke, his expression softened when he mentioned his three disciples. He turned slightly and looked at the three of them, \"Come forward and greet Immortal Elder Lingmu and the other Immortal Lords.\"","Hearing this, the three stepped out from behind him and bowed gracefully to Immortal Elder Lingmu.","\"Yun Chen.\"","\"Yun Yuan.\"","\"Yun Qi.\"","\"Greetings, Immortal Elder Lingmu and all the Immortal Lords.\"","The three spoke in unison. Even though they were young, they were graceful, spoke clearly, and carried themselves naturally, instantly winning the favor of everyone present.","\"Very good, very good. The Azure Emperor has indeed taken good disciples. These three children are clearly of noble birth. May I ask which family they come from?\""]},{"number":4768,"title":"Chapter 4768: Not Knowing Their Identity","paragraphs":["Chapter 4768: Not Knowing Their Identity","Immortal Elder Lingmu asked casually, thinking that these three children were so extraordinary and well-mannered at such a young age, they must be from a distinguished family, which is why he asked. However, he didn’t expect the Azure Emperor’s next words to make him pause.","“Once they become my disciples, they are only disciples of Yunxiao Mountain. Their families are no longer related to them, so there is no need to mention them.” The Azure Emperor spoke slowly, his expression indifferent. He guessed that among all the people present, he was the only one who dared to speak like this.","The crowd was still wondering who these three children were, but when they heard this, they were stunned for a moment. They glanced at each other and smiled at the same time.","This was indeed the Azure Emperor’s usual style!","After all, becoming a disciple of the Azure Emperor would bring great fortune to the families of the three children.","After all, becoming a disciple of the Azure Emperor would bring great fortune to the families of the three children as well.","“Yes, yes, don’t mention it. Come, come, this is your first time here with the Azure Emperor, so here are three things as gifts for you.” Immortal Elder Lingmu said with a smile as he took out three immortal artifacts and handed them to the three of them.","The three of them looked at their master, not knowing whether they should accept them.","“Since they are gifts from Immortal Elder Lingmu, you should accept them!”” The Azure Emperor said, motioning for the three of them to accept.","“Yes.” The three replied, took the gifts, and bowed to him again, “Thank you, Immortal Elder Lingmu.”","“You’re welcome.” Immortal Elder Lingmu said with a smile, gesturing for them to sit down, “Azure Emperor, please.” He personally invited him to sit down and came to sit with him at the head of the table.","Hao’er and the other two followed suit and sat behind their master, imitating the others.","As they sat down, the others followed suit. The servants poured wine, and the immortal music sounded again. Several beautiful fairies danced in the middle, and for a moment, there was laughter and joy everywhere.","“Azure Emperor, today we watched the lower realm and it seems that someone ascended to immortality. Does the Azure Emperor know who it is?” an old man asked. The person who ascended directly from the lower realm was not an immortal like them, but had directly ascended to become a great emperor, whose status was far above them.","However, with their power, they could not discern who had ascended to immortality.","“As you all know, I have always been indifferent to worldly affairs, either living in my cave abode or in seclusion to cultivate. Therefore, I only know that someone ascended to immortality today, but I do not know who it is,” said the Azure Emperor slowly and calmly as he picked up the wine cup in front of him and took a sip of the spirit wine.","“I didn’t expect that there were so many talented cultivators in the lower realm. Some time ago, there were also people who ascended to immortality, but they failed and died. I didn’t expect that a year later, there would be another person from the lower realm who ascended to immortality. This is truly unexpected!”","“I heard that in the lower realm, there is a female immortal who is extremely powerful and exceptionally talented. Not only that, she is also known as the Ghost Doctor because of her mastery of alchemy and medicine. Her name is Feng Jiu.” The man in the purple brocade robe played with his wine cup as he spoke, smiling, ”","It is said that this woman is unparalleled in beauty, with every smile and frown captivating the heart and soul. She is also said to be an immortal soul incarnated in the mortal world and the destined Phoenix Star. If someone ascended today, it is highly likely to be her. However, we have only heard of her name and never seen her. I am truly curious to know if she is as legendary as the rumors suggest.”"]},{"number":4769,"title":"Chapter 4769: The Azure Emperor’s Thoughts","paragraphs":["Chapter 4769: The Azure Emperor’s Thoughts","The Azure Emperor half-closed his eyes and sipped the spirit wine, looking unconcerned, as if he was not interested in their conversation. He did not respond or interject, but listened quietly while leisurely drinking his wine.","Behind him, the three children’s eyes flashed when they heard them mention their mother. They glanced at the man in the purple robe and carefully examined him.","He appeared to be in his early thirties and did not look very old, but according to their master, these people were all old bones.","Taking advantage of this moment, they looked at the younger generation sitting quietly behind their masters. Almost all of them were teenagers or in their twenties, except for one elderly man who was accompanied by a teenager in his late teens and a boy around ten years old.","The Immortal Elder Lingmu in the seat of honor took over from the purple-robed immortal and smiled, “Whether the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu is really as rumored, I believe we will know in the future. Come, everyone, let me offer you all a drink. Thank you all for gracing me with your presence.”","As he spoke, he held up his wine cup and gestured to everyone.","Seeing this, everyone also raised their wine cups in return and said, “Immortal Elder Lingmu, you are too kind. It is our good fortune to have the opportunity to visit here.”","Everyone chatted and drank together. After a while, the immortal dancers in the middle withdrew, and the Azure Emperor looked at Immortal Elder Lingmu and said slowly, “Immortal Elder, today, all of our immortal friends have brought their disciples with them. How about letting them have a competition in your Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm?","Hearing this, everyone’s hearts stirred, and they couldn’t help but look at Immortal Elder Lingmu, wondering if he would agree.","You must know that the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm was a wonderful place. If their disciples could go in and gain some experience, it would be a great blessing and extremely helpful for their cultivation.","The younger generation did not understand what he was talking about and had no idea what kind of place it was, so they just glanced at each other and looked at the Azure Emperor. They did not expect him to make such a request. But what kind of place was it? Even if Immortal Elder Lingmu agreed, did he really think that the three little kids behind the Azure Emperor could compete with them?","Wasn’t that a bit too arrogant?","Immortal Elder Lingmu heard the Azure Emperor’s words, stroked his beard, laughed heartily, shook his head, and said, “I knew it. The Azure Emperor hasn’t appeared for many years, so how could he accept my invitation? So that’s why you came!”","He glanced at the three children behind Azure Emperor, his eyes full of laughter.","He was not annoyed by his request, but said, “It’s rare for everyone to be here, so it’s fine to let these young ones go in. However, Azure Emperor, when it comes down to it, your three disciples are the youngest here. Are you sure you can let them go in?”","“Of course.”","The Azure Emperor smiled, playing with the wine cup in his hand, a glint flashing in his eyes. “In your Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm, there is a nine-section red flame phoenix scale whip. How about we see which disciple can get that whip? If my three disciples get it, I will give you a treasure of equal value as a token of my gratitude. What do you think?”","Hearing this, not only the Immortal Elder Lingmu, but also the others were stunned for a moment. However, when they heard the Azure Emperor mention the nine-section red flame phoenix scale whip, a gleam flashed in their eyes."]},{"number":4770,"title":"Chapter 4770: Target","paragraphs":["That whip is truly a secret treasure of the immortals. It was passed down from ancient times and cannot be compared to ordinary immortal weapons. Moreover, it is said that the nine-section red flame phoenix scale whip is also known as the whip that strikes gods. Even a cultivator with extraordinary cultivation would find it difficult to withstand a single lash.","Furthermore, being wounded by that whip would cause the skin to burn and blister, and ordinary medicine would be unable to cure it. It could be said that it was an ancient divine whip known throughout the four corners of the world. However, that whip had always been kept by Immortal Elder Lingmu, and although everyone had heard of it, no one had ever seen it.","Immortal Elder Lingmu smiled and looked at the Azure Emperor, saying, \"You, you came all this way just to see me, and it turns out you came for my treasure.\" He laughed softly, looking at the Azure Emperor with a meaningful gaze, and said, \"That treasure is in the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm. It was left there by my master back then, and even I cannot retrieve it. If someone really manages to get it, what harm would it do for me to give it away?\"","He smiled and looked at the other Immortal Lords, saying, \"Everyone, it's rare that the Azure Emperor is in such a good mood. I can't disagree! I wonder if your disciples would like to go in and try?\"","\"It's a rare opportunity and a chance for them. We would like to thank you on their behalf.\" Everyone stood up and bowed to him.","\"Very well, since that is the case, please follow me!\" He stood up with a smile and looked at everyone.","The Azure Emperor also stood up and, with the three little ones behind him, followed Immortal Elder Lingmu.","After walking for a while, they came to a mirror stone half as tall as a person with the words \"Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm\" engraved on it and stopped. Immortal Elder Lingmu looked at everyone and said, \"This is the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm. However, those who enter will have their powers suppressed. The stronger one is, the more difficult it will be to move inside.\"","He smiled, flicked his sleeves, and petals flew down and turned into a ray of light that entered the inner arms of the younger generation. Each person's inner arm was covered with beautiful petals.","\"Once you enter, if the petals on your arms are scratched and bleed, they will disappear, bringing you out of the realm. Similarly, if you can't hold on inside and want to come out, scratch the skin where the petals are and let the blood seep out, and you will come out on your own. Do you understand?\" Immortal Elder Lingmu looked at everyone and asked.","\"Understood.\" Everyone replied respectfully.","\"There is one thing you must remember. If you die inside, you will truly die inside. Therefore, when the time comes, remember what I have said. The petals on your arms will be your lifeline.\" Immortal Elder Lingmu said again, looking at them deeply.","\"Yes.\" Everyone replied again.","With a wave of his sleeve, the Immortal Elder Lingmu's robe fluttered, and the spirit stone mirror, which had looked ordinary, instantly emitted a soft glow, and a vortex appeared on the mirror.","\"Go in!\" Without giving their master a chance to give them any last words, Immortal Elder Lingmu waved his sleeve, and all the younger generation were sucked in. As they went in, the spirit stone mirror returned to its normal state.","Seeing this, everyone glanced at each other. There were still some things they hadn't had time to tell them! But now, they had all gone in. Thinking of this, they felt as if they had a lump in their throats, unable to breathe, which was very uncomfortable.","However, thinking of how young the Azure Emperor's three disciples were, they took a deep breath and felt at ease."]},{"number":4771,"title":"Chapter 4771: It’s A Deal","paragraphs":["Chapter 4771: It’s A Deal","Never mind, what’s the point? It’s their own fate. Let them wait and see!","“Everyone, shall we go back and enjoy some wine and music?” Immortal Elder Lingmu smiled and looked at everyone.","Everyone glanced at each other, then agreed and walked back with him.","The Azure Emperor and Immortal Elder Lingmu walked side by side in front, while the others followed behind. Perhaps they were worried about their disciples, so they walked with a dazed look on their faces, as if they were thinking about something.","Immortal Elder Lingmu glanced at the Azure Emperor and smiled, “Azure Emperor, aren’t you worried about those three? After all, they are so young, even I am a little worried about them!”","It was precisely because they were so young that when he sent the younger generation into the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm, he saw that the three children were holding hands, so he didn’t separate them and sent them in together.","Such young children, if they were separated, who knows what might happen. He and the Azure Emperor were old friends, so he decided to just take care of them a little more.","The Azure Emperor listened to his words, the corners of his lips slightly raised, and said slowly, “Although the three of them are still young, they are very intelligent, so I’m not worried.”","As he spoke, he turned his head slightly toward Immortal Elder Lingmu, a smile on his lips, and said, “You should worry about your whip!”","“Hahahaha.”","Immortal Elder Lingmu laughed loudly, his eyes and eyebrows filled with joy, showing that he was very happy. He said, “That treasure has been with me for a long time. Many people have tried to take it, but how many years have passed? No one has been able to enter the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm to retrieve it.”","As he spoke, he stroked his beard and laughed, “If your three disciples really manage to get it out, I’ll give you the whip and even hand you the book of whip techniques left behind by my master with both hands. How about that?”","“Hah, it’s a deal!” The Azure Emperor laughed and said, “Just don’t regret it when the time comes.”","“Hey, I am a dignified immortal, and my word is binding. How could I go back on my word? As long as your three disciples can get it, I will naturally fulfill my promise.” He laughed, thinking from the bottom of his heart that the Azure Emperor’s three disciples would not be able to get the whip. Not only would the Azure Emperor’s three disciples not be able to get it, but even the disciples of others would not be able to get it.","If that treasure was so easy to obtain, it wouldn’t be called an ancient treasure. It wouldn’t still be in his possession. Therefore, he was completely confident that those young disciples would only be going through the motions.","After all, their disciples probably spent most of their time following their master around and had little experience of real combat, not to mention that they would be entering his Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm.","The Azure Emperor listened and just smiled without saying anything.","At this moment, Immortal Elder Lingmu also did not expect that he would have a day when he would miscalculate...","At the same time, in the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm. After being sent in, everyone scattered, except for Hao’er, Muchen, and Muyue, who were alone.","Facing an unfamiliar environment, they were a little older and had seen many dangers and things, so they quickly calmed down and familiarized themselves with this place."]},{"number":4772,"title":"Chapter 4772: Compassion","paragraphs":["Chapter 4772: Compassion","While the others were trying to find their senior brothers and sisters to join them in their search for the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Whip, Hao’er and the other two were already surveying the area.","“Senior Brother, where should we go to find the whip?”","On the way here, their master had told them what the main purpose of their trip was, so they knew early on that their master had brought them here to see the world, but also because of a precious whip.","“Let’s look for it first! Be careful to protect the petals on your arms, don’t let anyone hurt them, or they will be sent away,” Hao’er reminded them.","“Yes, we know,” the two younger ones replied.","“Let’s go and take a look ahead first,” said Hao’er, motioning for the two to follow him.","The two followed him forward, paying attention to their surroundings. They walked a long way without encountering anyone else, so they decided to take a break.","“Senior Brother, Second Senior Brother, let’s protect the petals! It will be safer with a layer of protection.” While resting, Yue’er took out some bandages from her space, then took out a gold coin and wrapped her arm with the bandages before letting down her sleeves.","Seeing this, Hao’er and Muchen followed her example and made some simple protective measures. After the three of them were done, they drank some water and continued on their way.","“Roooooar!”","“Something’s moving!” Hao’er whispered, signaling the other two to be careful. They held their breath and followed the sound, coming to a large tree. When they saw the scene in front of them, their eyes flashed.","In front of them was a huge gray bear, about two meters tall. With each step it took, it left a deep footprint on the ground. The fierce beast had a cruel look in its eyes, and its open mouth revealed sharp fangs. At that moment, it was lunging forward with its hands and feet, trying to bite a boy around ten years old in front of it.","“It’s that boy.” Yue’er blinked. She knew him. Apart from them, he was the youngest. She didn’t expect him to be alone.","To their surprise, despite his young age, the boy was remarkably agile, dodging the bear’s attacks left and right. However, he was still just a child of around ten years old, and soon he was panting heavily, knocked to the ground by a bear’s paw, coughing up blood and looking utterly battered.","“Arghhhh!”","He let out a cry of pain as the bear’s sharp claws slashed across his body, leaving several marks.","Seeing him beaten so badly, Yue’er bit her lip and looked at her two brothers, asking, “Should we help him?”","Muchen didn’t say anything, just frowned and looked ahead.","Hao’er looked indifferent and said, “If he doesn’t want to die, he can save himself by cutting his arm and escaping. There’s no need for us to save him. If we save him, he will become our rival in the battle for the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip. When the time comes, are we supposed to go easy on him?”","Hearing this, Yue’er opened her mouth but couldn’t refute it. She knew that Big Brother was telling the truth, and her older brother didn’t say anything, so he probably agreed with Big Brother’s approach. Moreover, Master had said that if the three of them obtained the whip, it would be given to her.","Thinking of this, her heart was set.","Her master, Big Brother, and her older brother were all looking for weapons that she could use in the future. No matter what, she couldn’t let them down!"]},{"number":4773,"title":"Chapter 4773: Immortal Zinan","paragraphs":["The three watched from the sidelines, seeing the little boy struggling to escape the giant bear's attack. However, the bear did not seem willing to give up its prey and attacked fiercely. In no time, the little boy was covered in wounds and gasping for breath.","\"Roar!\"","A beastly roar rang out, and the giant bear lunged forward, its mouth wide open, its sharp teeth aimed at the little boy's neck.","With no escape in sight, the little boy turned pale with fear as the bear opened its mouth to bite him. He clenched his teeth, raised his hand, and slashed the petals on his arm. As the blood seeped out, the petals instantly turned into a beam of light, enveloping the child. The light flashed, and as the bear lunged forward, the child vanished into thin air.","Seeing this, Yue'er couldn't help but breathe a sigh of relief, and her heart finally settled down.","\"Roar!\"","The giant bear stretched out its sharp claws and scratched the ground, kicking up a cloud of dust and leaving several deep claw marks on the ground. It glanced around, then raised its head and let out two howls before running forward with all its might.","Watching the giant bear leave, the three people hiding nearby glanced at each other and continued on their way.","Just then, a voice came from behind them.","\"Please stop, all three of you.\"","Hearing the voice, the three stopped in their tracks and turned around warily. They saw that the newcomers were a man and a woman, both around twenty years old. The man was dressed in a blue brocade robe, while the woman was dressed in white, and both were very handsome.","They remembered these two as the disciples of the man in the purple robe who had mentioned their mother.","\"Hehe, we didn't have a chance to greet you three at the banquet earlier. I didn't expect to meet you here. I am Zhao Ziming, and this is my Junior Sister, Nangong Yuyan. We are disciples of Immortal Zinan.\"","The man spoke gently, looking at the three with a smile and said, \"It is extremely dangerous in here, and there are many fierce beasts. It's rare that we met you. How about we travel together?\"","Before the three of them could respond, the woman beside them said, \"This is our first time here too. We just heard the sound of a bear nearby. Did it hurt you?\"","\"No.\"","Hao'er replied, then looked at the man and said, \"The three of us are still young. Traveling with you will only cause you trouble, so we'd rather not.\"","When someone refused like that, most people would naturally leave, but the man and woman exchanged glances and smiled, \"It's no trouble. We're all disciples of immortals, and you're young, so we should take care of you.\"","Without waiting for them to refuse again, the man laughed and said, \"Could it be that the three of you look down on us? Is that why you don't want to travel with us?\"","Hearing this, Yue'er, who was standing nearby, curved her beautiful eyes and said with a smile, \"Senior Brother, let Young Master Zhao and Young Miss Nangong travel with us! That way, we'll have company.\"","Hearing this, Hao'er glanced at her and saw her smiling eyes and smiling face. However, those who knew her well saw this smile and felt a stir in their hearts, and they couldn't help but curve their lips slightly, their expressions softening a little.","\"In that case, please accompany us! I'm afraid we'll trouble you on the way,\" said Hao'er, bowing to them."]},{"number":4774,"title":"Chapter 4774: Making Friends","paragraphs":["Chapter 4774: Making Friends","“Traveling together, there’s no such thing as trouble.” Zhao Ziming smiled, looked at Yue’er, and said, “Yun Qi, can we call you by your first name? If you don’t mind, you can call me Big Brother Zhao, no need to address us as Young Master or Young Miss.”","Hearing this, Yue’er smiled at him, her beautiful eyes filled with innocence, and said earnestly, “My master said that we can’t call you Big Brother casually.”","Hearing this, Zhao Ziming was taken aback for a moment, then laughed and said, “Then we can’t call you Big Brother. How about you call us Senior Brother and Senior Sister?” Unexpectedly, as soon as he finished speaking, the little girl shook her head again.","“No, my master said that he only took the three of us as disciples, so we can’t call anyone else Senior Brother or Senior Sister.”","Seeing the little girl’s serious refusal, the smiles on their faces froze a little. When traveling outside, the children of wealthy families would often call each other brother or senior brother and junior sister. Who would be so strict about such things?","But this little girl spoke with such sincerity, her beautiful eyes filled with innocence and innocence. She looked like a well-protected, naive little girl who knew nothing of the world, pure as a blank sheet of paper. For these young adults in their twenties to discuss matters of etiquette and titles with a five or six-year-old child was like talking to a wall.","“Ha ha, then how about we just use our names?” The man smiled awkwardly and took a long time to come up with this sentence. If people of the same age used their names, it would be fine, but a child who was ten years younger than them calling them by their names seemed a little...","“Is that alright? Won’t that be inappropriate? Master didn’t say anything about it!” Yue’er bit her lip lightly, blinked her beautiful eyes, and looked hesitant.","“It’s alright, we’re all cultivators, we don’t care about such trivial matters.” The man said with a slightly stiff smile.","The woman beside him also smiled unnaturally and said, “Why don’t you just call us what you did before? You can call me Young Miss Nangong, it doesn’t matter.”","“Alright then, we’ll call you Young Master Zhao and Young Miss Nangong!” Yue’er said with a smile.","They had wanted to get closer to them, but who knew that after talking for so long, they ended up back where they started. The two couldn’t help but glance at each other, their eyes filled with a hint of helplessness.","If they weren’t disciples of the Azure Emperor, why would they lower themselves to befriend them? These three children were so young, and after talking to them for a while, they felt more tired than if they had fought a fierce beast.","“By the way, did your master mention the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip to you?” The man asked, looking at the three of them.","Muchen glanced at them and said, “Yes.”","Hearing this, the two couldn’t help but feel a stir in their hearts. They looked at each other and asked with a hint of joy, “How did he tell you about it? Did he say how to find the whip?”","“Our master said that it was an ancient treasure, the only one in the world. He didn’t tell anyone else.” Knowing that they wanted to pry, how could Muchen tell them?","“That’s right, it’s definitely an ancient treasure. No matter how many people want it, they can’t get it. I never thought we would have the chance to come here.” The man said, looking at them and smiling, “Let’s go! I heard my master talk about this treasure. He said it’s hidden in the deepest part of the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm.”"]},{"number":4775,"title":"Chapter 4775: Deceive","paragraphs":["Chapter 4775: Deceive","Hearing this, the three of them glanced at him but said nothing, simply letting him lead the way as they walked forward together.","On the way, Hao’er and Muchen didn’t say much, their little faces were indifferent and cold, and they didn’t seem easy to get along with. In particular, when the other two tried to strike up a conversation with them several times, Hao’er and Muchen only responded with a few simple words. Therefore, along the way, Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan got a pretty good idea of the three’s temperaments.","Therefore, Nangong Yuyan turned the topic to the smiling, innocent, and lovely Yun Qi, while Zhao Ziming occasionally spoke to Hao’er and Muchen, intending to distract them so that Nangong Yuyan, who was two steps behind them, would have a chance to find out some information.","“I heard that the Azure Emperor also had a female disciple named Yun Qi. If he named you, why would he name you Yun Qi?” Nangong Yuyan looked at Yue’er and asked.","Hearing this, Yue’er smiled and said, “Yes, we had a senior sister who was also called Yun Qi, but she is no longer with us. Our master said that he would name me Yun Qi so that she would always be with us.”","“Oh? I see. Then what was your original name, Yun Qi?” Nangong Yuyan asked again. She was actually very curious about their identities. As long as she asked their names, she could easily find out which family they came from.","Hao’er and Muchen listened to Zhao Ziming’s words while paying attention to Yue’er’s movements behind them. When they heard Nangong Yuyan asking about their origins, they pursed their lips but didn’t show any emotion.","This was because they believed that their sister was more than capable of dealing with Nangong Yuyan.","“Our master doesn’t allow us to reveal our real names,” Yue’er shook her head and said in a crisp voice, “Our master said that names are just code names. Once we become his disciples, we only need to remember that we are his disciples. If others ask, we cannot reveal our real names.”","The more they heard, the more curious they became. However, they had thought that these three children were young and it wouldn’t be difficult to pry something out of them, but who would have known that although they spoke, everything they said was useless information.","Moreover, the things they didn’t say were all attributed to their master, which left them feeling quite helpless.","“Be careful!”","Suddenly, Hao’er let out a low cry, quickly turned around, grabbed Yue’er and Muchen, and retreated several meters away.","At almost the same moment, Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan’s hair stood on end, and they quickly dodged. Just as they dodged, a figure as fast as light flashed past the spot where they had been standing, kicking up a cloud of dust.","“Hiss!”","“It’s a mutant golden ape!”","Zhao Ziming said, but his gaze was fixed on Hao’er, who was holding the two little ones. Just now, his reaction was extremely fast. At that moment, even he hadn’t noticed the danger, but he reacted first and pulled his Junior Brother and Junior Sister away.","At this moment, the side of himself that this child named Yun Chen had shown gave him a new understanding of him.","“Monkey!” Yue’er opened her eyes wide and looked at the huge monkey, curiously looking up and down, feeling that it didn’t look quite like a normal monkey.","“It’s not a monkey, it’s a mutant golden ape.”"]},{"number":4776,"title":"Chapter 4776: Stunned","paragraphs":["Nangong Yuyan's pretty face was serious as she said, \"Look at its eyes. They're red, which means it's a mutant monkey. These monkeys are already powerful, and with the mutation, they have both speed and strength, making them extremely powerful in battle. Most importantly, these monkeys live in groups, so I'm afraid there's more than just this one.\"","\"Hiss! Roar!\"","They heard the golden monkey that had darted out hissing, but then it suddenly let out a loud roar that echoed through the air.","\"No! Let's go!\" Zhao Ziming's face changed, and he immediately said, \"Hurry up! It's calling the other monkeys!\" As soon as he finished speaking, he took advantage of the mutant gorilla's lack of reaction to attack them and rushed forward.","Unexpectedly, as soon as they moved, they heard a cry.","\"Ah! Run, run! Senior Brother, Second Senior Brother, I'm scared! Master said that when there's danger, we should run away quickly...\"","Yue'er cried out in alarm, and almost as soon as her panicked voice fell, she pulled her two senior brothers and darted forward, moving so fast that they couldn't recover for a long time.","Startled by their speed, both of them froze in place. By the time they regained their senses and tried to call out to them, the mutated golden ape had already darted forward and swung a punch toward them.","\"Whoosh!\"","\"Senior Brother, be careful!\" Nangong Yuyan cried out in alarm as she saw the giant ape's fist carrying a powerful gust of wind swing toward Zhao Ziming. The force was so great that it was terrifying.","Zhao Ziming also regained his senses at that moment. He dodged swiftly but could still feel the terrifying force of the punch as it whizzed past his head. Facing a gorilla that combined both speed and strength, and worried that more gorillas might come to surround them, they dared not linger and only sought an opportunity to escape.","Just as the two of them dodged the mutated golden ape and chased after the three children in the direction they had fled, they heard screams echoing back. Soon, the three children returned, running back as if the wind were at their backs.","\"Ahhh! Run! There are so many monkeys chasing us!\" Yue'er shouted, her tiny legs running as fast as they could, dust flying up from her feet, with her two brothers on either side of her.","It wasn't that they didn't want to fight, but these monkeys—no, these apes—were too fast, and there were so many of them attacking them. Their fists were coming at them, and they watched helplessly as the giant ape knocked down a large tree with a single punch. Such terrifying combat power—they dared not fight.","Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan, who had been preparing to flee in their direction, saw the group of howling giant apes chasing after the three children and were instantly scared pale.","\"How, how are there so many!\" Nangong Yuyan gritted her teeth, turned around, and immediately ran to the left.","Zhao Ziming recovered his senses and didn't dare to hesitate. He just shouted at the three children, \"Hurry up! Run faster!\" As soon as he finished speaking, he also ran away without looking back.","Hao'er and the other two were being chased by the group of giant apes. They wanted to take this opportunity to separate from them, but the road was blocked, so they could only follow Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan.","Their speed in running for their lives was not only due to Feng Jiu's instructions, but also due to the special training they had received from the Azure Emperor.","Therefore, in no time, the three who had been lagging behind gradually ran ahead of Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan, leaving them staring in amazement..."]},{"number":4777,"title":"Chapter 4777: Not Simple","paragraphs":["Chapter 4777: Not Simple","“You guys, wait for us!” Zhao Ziming shouted, gritting his teeth and running desperately.","A few steps behind, Nangong Yuyan was so frightened by the giant apes that she was running for her life at full speed.","The group of them ran deeper into the forest. After chasing them for a long distance, the giant apes suddenly stopped for some unknown reason, remaining in place and roaring loudly, but no longer pursuing them.","Hao’er and the others looked back as they ran, and only when they could no longer see the giant apes did they breathe heavily and stop to rest.","When Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan arrived, they saw the three of them bent over with their hands on their knees, panting. They had run a long way and were covered in sweat, their faces red from the heat.","“How did you guys run so fast?” Zhao Ziming asked, panting slightly, with one hand on his waist, as he came over to them.","Nangong Yuyan was so tired that she didn’t even want to talk. She sat down under a tree nearby and took out some water to drink while panting heavily.","“Master said that our cultivation may not be perfect, but we must master the art of running for our lives, so we may not be good at other things, but our running skills are definitely top-notch.” Yue’er’s little face was flushed, and she blinked her beautiful eyes and said seriously, telling a lie.","The three of them weren’t just skilled at escaping; they also had self-defense abilities. Otherwise, their master wouldn’t have allowed them to enter this place.","What’s more, they were already used to those fierce beasts. If they weren’t worried about releasing the ancient pressure within their bodies and alerting others, they could just summon their contract beasts or release the pressure of the ancient divine beasts within their bodies, and those giant apes would naturally not dare to chase them anymore.","However, they remembered their master’s words and knew not to summon their contract beasts unless absolutely necessary, lest someone with ulterior motives discover their origins.","Hearing her words, the two stared at the three of them, speechless for a long time.","Their escape skills were far from ordinary. Even the two of them couldn’t keep up with their speed, which was truly extraordinary. What left them stunned and disbelieving was that despite their young age, how had they managed to develop such exceptional escape skills?","Nangong Yuyan looked at the three of them and said, “I didn’t expect that you had only been under the Azure Emperor’s tutelage for about a year, yet you were able to master such footwork. You are truly gifted and talented. No wonder the Azure Emperor took you as his disciples.”","“You two, there are many dangers and fierce beasts here. I think it would be better if we split up, lest we attract the attention of the fierce beasts with too many people.”Hao’er looked at the two of them and said, without waiting for them to respond, “Please go ahead.”","Saying that, he looked at Muchen and Yue’er and said, “Follow me.”","“Yes.” The two replied. Yue’er looked at the two of them, smiled and waved her hand, saying, “We’re leaving now, take care~”","“Hey, you guys...” Zhao Ziming had just opened his mouth when he saw the three of them rush into the forest. He couldn’t help but open his mouth, but the words behind it couldn’t come out.","“Senior Brother, these three are not simple,” said Nangong Yuyan as she stood up and looked in the direction the three had left, “Their reaction speed is astounding.”"]},{"number":4778,"title":"Chapter 4778: Illusory","paragraphs":["Chapter 4778: Illusory","Zhao Ziming smiled bitterly, “How could it be simple? They are geniuses. These three look young, but their reactions cannot be fooled. Even though they didn’t show anything special, just from the move they showed earlier and Yun Chen’s quick reaction to the danger, it’s clear that they are not incompetent.”","With that, he sighed lightly and said, “How could the disciples of the Azure Emperor be mediocre? We thought they were young and made assumptions.”","“Senior Brother, I think we should follow them. They might find the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip before us.” Nangong Yuyan said thoughtfully, looking at him and saying, “I don’t think they told us the truth. Since Azure Emperor brought them here, he must have told them about it.”","“Hmm, let’s go, follow them!” Zhao Ziming said, not bothering to rest, and immediately followed them forward with her.","Some of the other immortal disciples were injured, some had been teleported away, some were traveling in groups, some were searching for the nine-section red flame phoenix scale whip alone, and some were being chased by fierce beasts and running around.","Yue’er followed her two brothers forward, and when she occasionally saw some spirit herbs, she couldn’t help but crouch down and dig them up.","Muchen stood guard beside Yue’er while she dug up the spirit herbs. He noticed two people secretly following them not far behind and couldn’t help but look at their Big Brother.","“Senior Brother, they’ve been following us.”","Hao’er glanced at the two people and said, “Let’s find a chance to shake them off.”","“I’m done digging. Senior Brother, Second Senior Brother, let’s go!” Yue’er said with a smile.","So, the three exchanged glances and walked slowly at first, but gradually they picked up their pace, walking faster and faster to shake off the two behind them.","Just as the two were about to chase after them, the three men saw them and called out, “Brother Zhao! Young Miss Nangong!”","With no choice, the two stopped and looked at the three men walking quickly toward them.","While Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan were being held up, Hao’er and the other two had already quickened their pace and gone deeper into the forest...","At the same time, the masters in the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm were drinking wine and chatting idly. Although they were chatting casually, their minds were all on their disciples. They wanted to know if they had gained anything inside.","However, even if they wanted to help, they were powerless to do so and could only wait here.","The disciples who had entered but were injured and came out first were now sitting quietly behind their masters with their heads bowed, seeming somewhat ashamed and self-reproachful.","They were ashamed that they had left the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm so quickly, and they blamed themselves for failing to earn face for their masters and instead being eliminated early.","However, the injuries they suffered inside disappeared without a trace after they left the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm, as if what they experienced inside was nothing more than a mirage...","Furthermore, even though they had been inside for some time, it had not even been half an incense stick’s worth of time outside, so they only then realized that time inside and outside were different."]},{"number":4779,"title":"Chapter 4779: Watching From the Sidelines","paragraphs":["\"The Azure Emperor doesn't seem worried about your three disciples?\" Immortal Zinan, dressed in a purple brocade robe, played with his wine cup as he looked at the Azure Emperor, who appeared relaxed and carefree.","Hearing his words, the others who had been talking paused for a moment and looked at the Azure Emperor with a strange gleam in their eyes. Since they had entered, five disciples had come out, but the Azure Emperor's three young disciples had not yet been transported out, which was somewhat unexpected.","Could it be that those three children were already battle-hardened despite their young age? Did they have the absolute ability to deal with everything inside?","For a moment, everyone's minds were racing, secretly speculating.","The Azure Emperor took a sip of spirit wine, the corners of his lips curving slightly, and said slowly, \"What is there to worry about? If they can't handle it, they will come out naturally. However, since my three disciples have already gone in, they will definitely not return empty-handed.\"","With that, he smiled, looked at the Immortal Elder Lingmu beside him, flipped his hand, took out a night pearl that was so large it was difficult to hold in his palm, and said, \"Immortal Elder Lingmu, I obtained this night pearl a few years ago. I didn't bring any gifts with me this time, so let this pearl be my gift to you!\"","Hearing this, Immortal Elder Lingmu laughed heartily, took the huge night pearl with both hands, and said, \"Azure Emperor, you are really confident! Are you really so sure that your three disciples can obtain the treasure in the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm?\"","Having known each other for many years, he naturally knew what he meant by taking out this pearl, but Immortal Elder Lingmu still didn't believe it and found it funny.They were just three children who had only been with him for a year. How could they possibly obtain the ancient divine whip from inside?","\"Just keep it!\" The Azure Emperor smiled and said nothing more.","\"Very well, night pearls this large are rarely seen, and with such a beautiful luster, they are truly a rare treasure. Since it is a gift from the Azure Emperor, I will take the liberty of accepting it.\"He stroked his beard and smiled as he called over an immortal attendant to put away the night pearl.","Immortal Elder Lingmu looked at everyone and laughed, \"I'm sure you are all curious about their experiences and ability to adapt to the situation inside. Since that is the case, let's watch from here! It will also be a good opportunity to see how your disciples perform.\"","As he spoke, he took a mirror from his sleeve and threw it into the middle of the banquet table. The mirror flashed with a ray of light and stopped in midair between them, clearly reflecting the scenes of the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm.","Just then, the image in the mirror showed the three disciples of the Azure Emperor. In the image, the three were sitting under a tree, resting and drinking water while talking. However, just at that moment, a giant python darted toward them from not far away, hissing loudly. Even those outside could hear the sound and couldn't help but feel a chill run down their spines, but the three children didn't seem to notice.","Seeing this, everyone looked at the Azure Emperor, but he did not seem the least bit worried. He sat there slouching, looking lazy and carefree, gently swaying the wine cup in his hand and sipping the spirit wine inside while watching the scene in the mirror, looking as if he were an outsider watching a play.","\"Azure Emperor, this is a giant python at the peak of the sacred beast realm. The lives of your three disciples are in danger!\" Immortal Zinan sighed lightly and watched the scene in the mirror with great interest, seemingly looking forward to the giant python swallowing the three children in one gulp."]},{"number":4780,"title":"Chapter 4780: Calculations","paragraphs":["Chapter 4780: Calculations","The Azure Emperor swirled the wine in his cup and smiled, “I heard that Immortal Zinan once obtained a Purple Sun Golden Thread Soft Armor. How about we make a bet? Let’s see if this giant python eats my three disciples, or if my disciples kill this giant python?”","Hearing this, Immortal Zinan’s eyes flashed and he said, “Azure Emperor, you want my Purple Sun Golden Thread Soft Armor? I wonder, if I bet the Purple Sun Golden Thread Soft Armor, what would Azure Emperor bet?”","Azure Emperor tugged at the corner of his mouth and smiled, “I have too many treasures, I wonder which one Immortal Zinan has set his sights on?”","“Hehe, since the Azure Emperor has spoken, then how about the Azure Emperor’s Heavenly Seal as the bet?” Immortal Zinan looked at the Azure Emperor and said.","“Agreed.” The Azure Emperor smiled and agreed.","Just as he finished speaking, the giant python darted forward in an instant, opening its huge mouth and biting towards Yue’er.","Everyone present watched this scene and held their breath, but unexpectedly, in that instant, the little girl who had been smiling and talking with her two Senior Brothers just a moment ago rolled on the ground, pulled a dagger from her boot, and almost reflexively slashed at the snake’s tail.","The speed and ferocity of her move stunned everyone present.","As the dagger flew out, the little girl suddenly emitted a fierce killing intent, and the aura around her changed instantly. Just a moment ago, she had been innocent and harmless, but now she exuded a ruthless and decisive intent. The transformation was so sudden that it left everyone stunned.","Moreover, not only was the little girl’s reaction swift, but the two young boys’ reactions were also extremely quick. They both stepped back swiftly as the giant serpent lunged forward. However, when they saw the little girl confronting the giant serpent, they did not rush to help but stood by and watched.","Immortal Elder Lingmu saw this scene, and his hand, which was stroking his beard, paused, and a look of surprise appeared on his face.","Obviously, he did not expect that the little girl would dare to deal with the giant snake alone, and that her two Senior Brothers would not come forward to help.","The Azure Emperor just watched quietly, but his eyes were filled with gentleness and pride.","This was his disciple. Even though she was still young, she had extraordinary courage and outstanding skills.","Looking at the excitement in the little girl’s eyes, he guessed that she wanted to catch the snake’s gallbladder for medicine! Thinking of this, he shook his head secretly, feeling a little helpless and a little indulgent.","If anyone looked unhappy, it was probably Immortal Zinan. Compared to the shock and surprise on the faces of the others, his face was a little dark. After all, he was a person of his cultivation level, so he could naturally tell if someone was really skilled with just one move.","This young girl, though still young, demonstrated remarkable strength, fierce attacks, and blinding speed when she lunged forward with the dagger. It was clear to him that he had underestimated her."]},{"number":4781,"title":"Chapter 4781: Kill","paragraphs":["Chapter 4781: Kill","Seeing this, he couldn’t help but feel a surge of joy. He had known it all along—this little girl was only five or six years old; how could she possibly stand a chance against that giant python? Watching the little girl being wrapped up by the python’s tail, he couldn’t help but glance at the man in azure.","Perhaps his Purple Sun Golden Soft Armor would not only protect him, but he would also be able to obtain the Azure Emperor’s treasure, which would be a great thing.","Thinking of this, the corners of his mouth curled up imperceptibly, but his face was full of worry as he said, “Hey, Azure Emperor, look, that little girl is wrapped up in the python’s tail. You must know that a python’s strength is no joke. Even an adult, it can crush all of their bones, let alone a child!”","Although he said this, he wasn’t worried. As long as the little girl couldn’t withstand the pressure, she would naturally be transported out. Of course, if she was transported out, he would win his bet with the Azure Emperor.","Unexpectedly, the Azure Emperor remained expressionless. He only glanced at him indifferently before looking away, his eyes seeming to say that he didn’t want to talk to him. This made him feel ashamed and angry, but he didn’t dare to show it.","“Hehe, Immortal Zinan, just watch! It’s not over yet!” Immortal Elder Lingmu stroked his beard and smiled, looking at the Azure Emperor’s three disciples with newfound respect.","What’s more, so far, the two boys had only been watching and hadn’t approached. If the little girl really couldn’t handle it, they would naturally go up and help her. How could they just stand by and watch?","As he finished speaking, he heard a surprised voice.","“Look!”","An immortal looked at the scene in the mirror and saw that the python’s tail, which had been tightly wrapped around the little girl a moment ago, suddenly loosened. The snake’s body twitched, and the little girl seized the opportunity to raise the dagger and stabbed it fiercely at the snake’s seven-inch spot. The dagger in her hand pierced deep into the snake’s body, and when she pulled it out, a column of blood spurted out.","“Hiss!”","The giant python hissed and tried to turn back to bite her, but it seemed as if it didn’t have the strength to do so. Its head fell to the ground with a bang. At this moment, the little girl quickly stabbed it again. Only after confirming that the giant python was dead did she smile and look at her two Senior Brothers.","Looking at the smile on the little girl’s face, everyone present was shocked. That was a giant snake of the Holy Beast level. Even though they were watching, they couldn’t figure out how she had killed it.","Immortal Zinan’s expression was a little ugly. He pursed his lips, glanced at the Azure Emperor, and said with a fake smile, “The Azure Emperor’s disciple is indeed different from the rest. At such a young age, she is already so decisive and skilled in combat. She is truly no ordinary person.”","“Immortal Zinan, you flatter me. My three disciples are just a little more talented than others and are quick to understand things.” The Azure Emperor smiled lightly, gently shook his wine cup, and took a sip of wine.","Seeing this, everyone around them glanced at each other, then smiled and said, “I wonder how the other disciples are doing? Immortal Elder Lingmu, shall we take a look at the others?”","Hearing this, Immortal Elder Lingmu also smiled and was about to switch the image to the other disciples, but unexpectedly, when he saw the scene in the mirror, even he was stunned. For a moment, he froze and couldn’t switch to another image."]},{"number":4782,"title":"Chapter 4782: Means","paragraphs":["Chapter 4782: Means","In the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm, Hao’er and Muchen only came over after seeing Yue’er kill the giant snake.","They had originally wanted to help, but Yue’er said she could handle it and told them to stay away, so they just stood by and watched. They didn’t expect her to actually kill the giant snake by herself. Although she used some medicine to deal with the snake, it was still her who killed it.","“Senior Brother, Second Senior Brother, wait for me. I want to take the snake’s gallbladder for medicine,” Yue’er said without looking up, as she held the dagger and cut open the giant python’s body.","The snake’s body, which was too heavy for one person to carry, was sliced open by the little girl. The sight of blood everywhere was enough to make one’s stomach churn, but the little girl remained focused. After finding the snake’s gallbladder, she carefully removed it, took out a bottle from her spatial pocket, placed the gallbladder inside, and put it away.","The people at the banquet saw the little girl’s nimble hands cut open the snake’s body, take out the gallbladder, and dig out the inner core, and couldn’t help but feel a chill run down their spines.","Her skilled movements were as if she had done this hundreds of times before, which truly shocked them!","Immortal Elder Lingmu took a deep breath and, seeing the bloody scene, waved his hand to change the image. At this moment, one of the immortals asked, “Azure Emperor, your disciples are young, but their techniques are extremely skilled. How do you train them? How did you teach them such skilled techniques at such a young age?”","The Azure Emperor looked at the changed scene, then took back his gaze with disinterest and replied to the immortal, “Not long ago, I sent them out alone to gain experience for a month. My senior disciple brought back 300 crystal cores from fierce beasts, among which were some fierce beasts with the strength of peak-level sacred beasts.”","As he spoke, he paused, took a sip of wine, and continued under their shocked gazes, “As for the two younger ones, they were sent to different places, but they also brought back 100 crystal cores each, among which there were naturally quite a few crystal cores from fierce beasts at the level of sacred beasts. Therefore, when it comes to dealing with a python, each of my three disciples is more than capable.”","“So you knew that your little disciple would definitely kill that giant python, yet you still lured me into a bet?” Immortal Zinan looked at him with a grim expression, feeling like he had been tricked.","“Ha ha...”","The Azure Emperor laughed softly, his laughter revealing indifference and coldness. “If Immortal Zinan hadn’t been greedy, how would he have bet with me? Besides, why would I pick you out of all the others?”","Hearing this, Immortal Zinan felt a lump in his throat, wanting to speak but unable to. Finally, he could only say with a hint of shame and embarrassment, “Azure Emperor, you are truly clever!”","“Not at all,” replied the Azure Emperor casually.","“Immortal Zinan, aren’t those your two disciples?” The immortal sitting next to him spoke up, changing the subject to prevent the conversation from continuing and ending badly.","“They are also the two disciples of the old man.” Another immortal smiled, his gaze also falling on the image in the mirror.","“I didn’t expect my eldest disciple and your two disciples to get together.” The other immortal also smiled.","However, they quickly stopped laughing."]},{"number":4783,"title":"Chapter 4783: Shame and Anger","paragraphs":["Chapter 4783: Shame and Anger","It turned out that they had been traveling together for some time when they encountered two fierce bears. At first, they fought together, but the noise attracted a group of mutated golden apes. The apes did not approach, but roared from the sidelines, seemingly waiting for the right moment to attack.","In this situation, as the situation became more and more dangerous and their fighting power gradually declined, the two disciples of Immortal Zinan took advantage of the other three’s lack of preparedness and pushed them out of the way when the two fierce beasts pounced, blocking them while they quickly took the opportunity to escape.","Seeing this, the three disciples’ master’s face turned ugly. The smile on his face a moment ago had turned cold, and his tone was tinged with sarcasm as he said, “Immortal Zinan has indeed taught his disciples well. Cultivators should not have such insidious thoughts and methods. It is clear that they will not go far on the path to immortality.”","Another sighed and shook his head, saying, “It is my shame that I only taught them to cultivate and admonished them to be humble and polite in their dealings with others and not to harm others, but I did not teach them that the world is treacherous and that one must be wary of others. I am truly ashamed, ashamed!”","Listening to the two, Immortal Zinan’s face turned red and green, and he felt both angry and ashamed.","His two disciples were so useless that they did such a thing in front of everyone, making him unable to hold his head up. He understood the sarcasm in their words, but he couldn’t even open his mouth to refute them. After this incident, he was afraid that others would look at him differently in the future.","Finally, he took a deep breath, suppressed the shame and anger in his heart, stood up, bowed to the two of them, and said apologetically, “It is my fault for not disciplining them strictly, which allowed those two bad disciples to do such a thing. I am truly ashamed before you two. I apologize to you here. When I return, I will severely punish those two bad disciples.”","Seeing that he had stood up to apologize, the two did not hold a grudge and their expressions softened a little. They just said, “We are immortals, and our cultivation is secondary. What is most important is our character. Immortal Zinan’s two disciples may be outstanding in strength, but if their character is impure, I’m afraid they will bring disaster upon themselves in the future, not to mention how far they can go on the path to immortality. Since Immortal Zinan has apologized on their behalf, we will not pursue the matter any further. Let’s just see how they do on their own!”","Immortal Zinan also revealed an unnatural smile, bowed to them again, and then sat down.","The others watched with mixed expressions, but said nothing, just staring at the scene in the mirror. The three who had been pushed out were seriously injured by the giant bear. With no other choice, they could only tear the petals and teleport out of the Spirit Realm to save themselves.","Seeing this scene, everyone had mixed feelings. They glanced at each other, and before long, they saw the three return from nowhere.","“Master!”","“Master!”","The three of them bowed with their hands clasped together, their faces still angry as they looked at Immortal Zinan.","“It’s alright, we all know. Sit down and rest!” Their master gestured for them to sit behind him.","Seeing this, they had no choice but to sit behind their master. Once they were seated, their junior brothers told them what had just happened...","The image in the mirror switched again, and they saw the other people inside one after another..."]},{"number":4784,"title":"Chapter 4784: Surprise","paragraphs":["Time seemed to pass quickly in the mirror. Day turned into night, and night turned into day, while outside, everyone at the banquet watched, drinking wine and chatting idly, and time passed extremely slowly.","However, as time passed, more and more disciples were transported out, until it was evening in the mirror, and only the Azure Emperor's three disciples and Immortal Zinan's two disciples remained inside.","Some people found it incredible that only five people remained inside, while others thought it was only natural. Those disciples were even more shocked and surprised after seeing the performance of the Azure Emperor's three disciples inside, and most of them were curious and wanted to befriend them.","However, they also knew that, not to mention their mysterious origins, the fact that they were disciples of the Azure Emperor alone already made them a cut above them, and with the age difference, they could only dream of befriending them.","In the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm, as night fell, the surroundings were pitch black. Hao'er and the other two lit a small fire and gathered around it to roast the meat they had hunted.","Smelling the aroma of the meat, Yue'er swallowed her saliva greedily, \"Senior Brother, is it ready? Can we eat?\"","Hao'er glanced at her and smiled: \"Yes, it's done. I'll cut a piece for you.\" He cut a piece, wrapped it in a large leaf, handed it to her, and said, \"Be careful, it's hot.\"","\"Mm hmm.\" Yue'er happily took it, blew on it, took a small bite, and immediately cried out because it was too hot.","\"Eat slowly, it's very hot when it first comes off the fire,\" said Muchen as he took the piece of meat from her hand, cut it into smaller pieces with a small knife, and then handed them to her. \"Eat!\"","\"Hehe, thank you, Second Senior Brother.\" She smiled, her eyes narrowing as she looked at her two brothers who loved her so much, one roasting meat for her and the other cutting it for her. Her heart was filled with joy.","Her two brothers were both so kind to her! She would be kind to them too! She would never let anyone bully them!","The three of them ate in the night, sprinkled some medicine around them, and then gathered around the fire to rest. They stayed there until dawn the next day, when they set off again for their final destination.","It was a mountain peak deep in the mountains with a waterfall cascading down from above, splashing countless drops of water. There were no fierce beasts around, only the sound of water hitting the rocks below the waterfall.","\"Why is there nothing here?\" Yue'er looked around and then at her two brothers.","\"Look around, it should be around here,\" said Hao'er as he released his divine sense to search the area. Unexpectedly, before he found the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip, he discovered two people hiding in the shadows.","After discovering them, Hao'er paused for a moment. After thinking it over, he said, \"Since you're here, why don't you come out and show yourselves?\"","Upon hearing this, Muchen and Muyue glanced at each other and followed their Big Brother's gaze. They saw two figures slowly walking out of the forest not far away.","\"Ha ha, what a coincidence! I didn't expect to meet you here.\" Zhao Ziming smiled, bowed his hands towards them, and looked at the three of them meaningfully, saying, \"You are really not simple to have made it this far!\"","However, just at that moment, a roar suddenly came from the sky. They looked up and their eyes lit up with surprise..."]},{"number":4785,"title":"Chapter 4785: Determining A Winner","paragraphs":["They saw a phoenix with fiery red flames emanating from its body cry out once, circle in the sky, cry out twice toward them, then land on a rock above the waterfall, looking down on them from above.","Seeing the phoenix, Hao'er, Muchen, and Muyue's eyes lit up.Their master had mentioned to them that the ancient phoenix-scale whip was transformed from this phoenix, and that this phoenix was said to have a trace of phoenix blood. If they could subdue it, it could be transformed into the ancient phoenix-scale whip for their use.","\"Is that a phoenix? Its aura seems like...\" Zhao Ziming said, looking thoughtfully at the phoenix covered in flames, lost in thought.","\"So beautiful! I didn't expect there to be such a divine bird here,\" Nangong Yuyan couldn't help saying. As a woman, she naturally loved beautiful things.","Compared to the surprise of the two, Hao'er and the other two were very calm and normal. After exchanging glances, they nodded slightly, and Hao'er said, \"You two, there are only five of us left here. Instead of fighting over the phoenix scale whip in the end, why don't we decide the winner first? What do you think?\"","Hearing this, the two exchanged glances and looked at the three of them, pondering for a moment. If they settled the outcome first, they would have no fear of the three of them resorting to underhanded tactics when it came to the final battle for the phoenix scale whip. They could focus solely on securing the whip. Moreover, while the three of them were skilled, they were still no match for the two of them. Two against three—the odds were in their favor.","Thinking of this, the two looked at each other and nodded imperceptibly: \"All right.\"","As soon as they finished speaking, Zhao Ziming glanced at the three of them and said, \"If it's one-on-one, we'll be suspected of bullying the weak. Even if we win, it won't be a fair victory. How about two against three? The three of you can attack together!\"","It sounded good, but if the three of them attacked together, their fighting power would be even greater. They thought that the three children were too young to know this, but they didn't know that the people outside the mirror were watching their every move, and Hao'er and the others knew this very well.","However, they were confident in their abilities, so they did not refuse. After all, their goal was to get them out of this spiritual realm as soon as possible and retrieve the whip. Therefore, they let them make their decision.","\"Alright,\" Hao'er replied, drawing his sword and saying, \"Let's fight here!\"","\"Alright!\" Zhao Ziming and the other two also replied, stepping forward and bowing with their swords in their hands, \"Then we'll take you on.\" As soon as they finished speaking, the two did not hesitate and immediately drew their swords and attacked the three of them.","Hao'er, Muchen, and Yue'er were here. Except for the dagger in Yue'er's hand, Hao'er and Muchen were both holding swords. Their long swords moved with ease, and fierce sword qi slashed through the air, shooting toward the two in front of them.","All three had undergone rigorous training, their skills far surpassing those of their peers. Moreover, their innate talent was exceptional, and their mastery of sword techniques left many in awe.","At this moment, when the two men attacked, Yue'er did not step forward, but held the dagger in her hand and twirled it around, her beautiful eyes fixed on Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan."]},{"number":4786,"title":"Chapter 4786: I Can Do It","paragraphs":["Chapter 4786: I Can Do It","As soon as Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan engaged them, they realized that their formidable skills and extremely fast footwork were beyond their expectations. For a moment, they found it difficult to cope.","However, just then, they heard a voice tinged with a smile.","“I’m coming to help!”","Yue’er said with a smile. As soon as she finished speaking, her small figure darted out like a ghost, and the dagger in her hand did not attack anywhere else, but instead aimed at the two men’s arms, trying to slash the teleportation petals on the inside of their arms.","Zhao Ziming and Nangong Yuyan, who had already found the two of them difficult to handle, were both startled and alarmed when they saw the little girl holding the dagger and targeting the inner sides of their arms. They quickly dodged while blocking the two boys’ fierce attacks. After a brief skirmish, the two of them were forced into retreat, unable to keep up with the relentless assaults.","“Whoosh! Clang!”","“Whoosh, whoosh!”","“Ahhhhhh!”","In a moment of carelessness, Nangong Yuyan’s arm was cut by Yue’er, but it wasn’t the inner side of her arm. She gasped as she saw the blood seeping out of her arm, and a flash of anger crossed her eyes as she glared at Yue’er.","“Senior Brother, I’ll send this little girl out first!” Nangong Yuyan gritted her teeth and said, letting him support himself. She then swung her sword at Yue’er, who looked innocent and clueless. The sharp sword was aimed at Yue’er’s arm.","Seeing her sword coming at her, Yue’er was slightly surprised. She blinked her beautiful big eyes and quickly backed away, her soft voice carrying a hint of seriousness and curiosity: “Young Miss Nangong, do you always pick on the soft persimmons? But I’m not a soft persimmon!”","As she spoke, her eyes curved into a smile as she looked at her: “My master said that I am very powerful, and I will be even more powerful in the future!” As she spoke, her aura changed, and she suddenly leaned forward, changing from defense to offense. Her moves were fierce and violent, and the dagger in her hand aimed at the fatal points of the human body, forcing Nangong Yuyan’s face to change drastically, and she became flustered.","“Damn it!”","Nangong Yuyan cursed under her breath. Once inside, their strength was suppressed, and the higher their strength, the more difficult it was to move. Although they had not reached that level, their suppressed strength greatly reduced their fighting ability.","At this moment, seeing that she was being forced to retreat, she gritted her teeth and attacked Yue’er’s vital points with all her might.","If she really hurt her, then she really couldn’t be blamed!","After all, she had been cultivating for many years. When she became fierce, the fierce sword qi attacked Yue’er’s body, causing her to be cut by the fierce sword qi and bleed slightly.","“Junior Sister!”","Hao’er and Muchen saw that she had been cut by the sword energy. Although there were no large wounds, there were many small ones, and blood seeped from her body, blooming on her pink dress like red plum blossoms, extremely dazzling.","“I’m fine, I can do it!” Yue’er said, stopping them from coming to help with her eyes, telling them to defeat Zhao Ziming first.","“You are no match for me!” Nangong Yuyan said, turning the sharp sword in her hand. As the sword energy attacked, the long sword also slashed down, aiming at her arm.","“Clang!”","Yue’er’s dagger blocked the sharp sword, and when the dagger and sword collided, they made a crisp clanging sound."]},{"number":4787,"title":"Chapter 4787: Amazed","paragraphs":["Yue'er was only a child of five or six years old, and was no match for a grown woman. Therefore, when the sharp sword slashed down at her, the force of the blow pressed down on her. Even though she held the dagger tightly to block it, she couldn't hold it back and was gradually pushed down.","Just then, Nangong Yuyan's gaze swept over her arm, and she suddenly turned the sword in her hand, slashing at her arm.","\"Whoosh!\" <small class=\"plain-imprint-b\">Uploaded by the M|V|L(EMPYR) team.</small>","With extreme speed, it slashed across Yue'er's arm. In that instant, her sleeve was cut by a sword mark, and her small, pink arm was also cut by a slanted sword mark. As blood seeped from her arm, Nangong Yuyan couldn't help but laugh.","\"You're out!\"","This strike nearly sliced through her entire inner arm, naturally also cutting through the petal on the inner side of her arm. With the petal destroyed, blood would seep out, and she would naturally be teleported away. Unexpectedly, just as her voice fell and she revealed her smile, Yue'er endured the pain in her arm and revealed a fox-like, cunning smile: \"That's not necessarily true!\"","With a soft and sweet voice, she took advantage of her opponent's moment of triumph and pressed her dagger against her sword, rubbing it forward. When it was close to the tiger's mouth, she suddenly turned the dagger, and the sharp blade directly slashed the petal on the inside of her arm.","\"Sss! You!\"","Nangong Yuyan let out a cry of pain and glared at the little girl in front of her, but she was startled by a bandage that slipped off her arm and something that fell to the ground.","\"Clang!\"","A golden coin, shimmering with a golden glow, landed on the stone, emitting a crisp sound. As she saw the coin, Nangong Yuyan stared in disbelief at the bleeding inner side of the young girl's arm. Her sword had slashed across her arm, but the sword had missed the spot where the flower petal was. The gold coin had protected the flower petal, leaving it intact on her arm! \"How... how is this possible...\" Before she could finish her sentence, her arm, where the flower petal had been sliced open, was instantly teleported away along with the petal, leaving only her unfinished words echoing in the air.","Outside the mirror, everyone who witnessed this scene was speechless for a moment. They couldn't hide their shock and bewilderment. They never imagined that the little child had protected the spot where the petal was with a gold coin, and that the coin had blocked the wound caused by the sword. After a moment, they looked at the Azure Emperor, who was watching the scene in the mirror, and couldn't help but mutter to themselves: \"This Azure Emperor is a demon, and his three disciples are even more perverted than he is!\"","\"I'm really impressed. The three people opposite us are truly convinced.\" A young man sitting behind their master said, looking at the little girl in the mirror with admiration and amazement. \"How can she be so powerful? How did she think of using gold coins to protect that petal? If we had thought of that earlier, we probably wouldn't have been eliminated so quickly.\"","\"She's only five or six years old and already so powerful. She'll be even more amazing when she grows up.\" Another young man said with an inexplicable gleam in his eyes, \"I wonder what she'll be like in ten years.\""]},{"number":4788,"title":"Chapter 4788: No Wonder","paragraphs":["Chapter 4788: No Wonder","During the banquet, the air was abuzz with discussion. Everyone present was clearly amazed and impressed by the three children, and it was evident from their words. After all, these adults, more than a decade older than the children, had spent less time within the trials than the young ones. Upon their emergence, they had witnessed firsthand the children’s remarkable ability to adapt and respond to challenging situations. In a world that so deeply revered strength and power, these three children, despite their tender age, were indeed worthy of admiration and respect.","At this very moment, observing the unfolding scene in the mirror, Immortal Elder Lingmu couldn’t help but shake his head and smile gently. He turned to the Azure Emperor beside him and remarked, “It seems my late master’s Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip will end with me! I never thought I would have a day when I would misjudge someone so thoroughly. What a mistake, what a mistake!”","The Azure Emperor merely glanced at him, curling his lips ever so slightly. He gently swirled the wine cup in his hand, took a leisurely sip, and then replied, “Didn’t I already send you something? Even if it’s a loss, it’s not that big of a loss. Besides, that whip is useless to you now, so it’s perfectly suited for my disciple.” Immortal Elder Lingmu simply smiled in response, saying nothing more, his gaze fixed once again on the events unfolding in the mirror. He seemed to silently add, ‘Even if he gave it to them, they would have to be able to take it out! Let’s just wait and see!’","Inside the mirror, Zhao Ziming, was visibly shocked to witness his Junior Sister, Nangong Yuyan, defeated by that little girl and subsequently teleported away. In that brief moment of distraction, he suddenly felt a sharp pain in his own arm, and his heart sank. He looked down and couldn’t help but offer a bitter smile. Fresh blood was already seeping from the inside of his arm, and the petals there were rapidly disappearing. In the very next moment, before he could utter a single word, he too was teleported away.","“How are you? Are you seriously injured? Quickly apply some medicine,” Hao’er and Muchen quickly urged, rushing to Yue’er’s side after dealing with Zhao Ziming. Seeing the deep wound on the inside of her arm, they couldn’t help but feel a pang of pain themselves.","“It hurts a lot, doesn’t it?” Muchen asked, gently holding her hand, his small face etched with worry.","“Yes, it hurts a lot. Senior Brother, please be gentle when you apply the medicine. I’m afraid of pain,” Yue’er said, a truly pitiful look on her face.","“Yeah, Senior Brother will be gentle; just bear with it,” Hao’er reassured her as he carefully applied medicine to her wound and then bandaged it. “Junior Sister, stay here and watch! We’ll go get the whip for you.” Hao’er then helped her rest on one side.","Yue’er’s arm indeed hurt a great deal, so she didn’t try to act strong anymore. She simply nodded, saying, “Okay, Senior Brother and Second Senior Brother, please be careful.”","“We know,” the two replied in unison. Then, they both looked up at the majestic phoenix perched above them. In the next moment, they gathered their energy and soared towards the creature.","Outside the mirror, everyone watched the unfolding scene, unable to stop pondering its implications. They looked at Immortal Elder Lingmu and asked, “Immortal Elder, could it be that this Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip is this phoenix?”","Immortal Elder Lingmu smiled, stroking his long beard thoughtfully. He looked at everyone and then laughed, “You don’t know, but this phoenix is not a beast at all. It is, in fact, the spirit of the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip itself. In the Moon Reflection Illusory Spirit Realm, it has always appeared in the form of a spirit.”","“No wonder we only knew that the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip was somewhere in the depths of the spirit realm, but no one ever knew where it was hidden. So that’s how it is!” An immortal elder nodded, a sudden realization dawning on him, his long-held doubts finally cleared.","Immortal Elder Lingmu smiled again, then looked at the Azure Emperor and said, “I have never mentioned this before, so you would not have known. I am telling you today because I estimate that the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip will be revealed today, so there is no need to hide it anymore.”"]},{"number":4789,"title":"Chapter 4789: Doing It the Hard Way","paragraphs":["Chapter 4789: Doing It the Hard Way","Hearing this, everyone’s hearts stirred slightly. Did Immortal Elder Lingmu mean that the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip would ultimately have to be retrieved by the Azure Emperor’s three disciples? Thinking of their impressive performance inside the realm, everyone felt that this outcome was not impossible. With this in mind, all gazes turned back to the mirror, fixed once more on the spirit realm.","Inside the spirit realm, Yue’er watched her two brothers work together to battle the phoenix. The magnificent creature flapped its wings, releasing powerful flames from its body as it attacked the duo. Hao’er and Muchen quickly dodged and counterattacked. Their goal was to make it submit, not to kill it, which meant their battle felt somewhat restrained.","Yue’er observed that her brothers seemed to be primarily focused on dodging, not having inflicted much harm on the phoenix. On the contrary, both of her brothers had sustained scratches on their shoulders from the phoenix’s sharp claws. Seeing the blood seeping from their wounds, she couldn’t stand by any longer. Clutching the dagger in her hand, she stood up and declared, “Senior Brothers, I’ll help you!” This entire endeavor was originally meant to help her retrieve the whip. Seeing them injured, how could she just stand idly by and watch? They might be reluctant to harm it, but she certainly wasn’t. Anyone who dared to hurt her brothers would be taught a lesson by her!","The two brothers heard her voice, turned, and saw her rising into the air. With an agile flip, she landed directly on the phoenix’s back.","“Be careful not to hurt her!” Hao’er cried out, worried that she would be harmed by the flames.","“How dare you hurt my Senior Brother? I’ll kill you!” Yue’er shouted in a soft voice that didn’t sound particularly threatening. However, as soon as she spoke, the dagger in her hand stabbed fiercely into the phoenix’s body. For some unknown reason, the flames on the phoenix’s body were extinguished as she landed.","“Junior Sister! You’ll kill it!” Hao’er and Muchen were startled by her fierce stance. They hadn’t expected her to take advantage of their distraction of the phoenix to ride on its back when it wasn’t prepared, and then actually stab it with the dagger in her hand. At that very moment, they sensed an ancient pressure emanating from her, forcibly suppressing the phoenix’s aura. The flames on the phoenix’s body also vanished instantly due to the appearance of that ancient pressure.","“Sssss!” The knife truly pierced the phoenix’s body. It let out a cry, though it was unclear whether it was out of fear of the pressure that burst forth from Yue’er’s body or if it was genuinely injured. It folded its wings and dove down from mid-air. With a flash of red light, it transformed into a whip that slammed into the ground, the whip now stained with blood.","“Huh?” Yue’er was also stunned. Although she had stabbed fiercely, she didn’t expect that after a single stab, the phoenix would turn into a whip like that. Seeing this, Hao’er and Muchen exchanged glances. They both knew that this sudden transformation probably had something to do with the ancient pressure their sister had released just moments ago. However, that pressure had come and gone so quickly that no one else should have noticed it.","“Senior Brother, Second Senior Brother, look! If soft doesn’t work, you have to use force. Now look, it’s obediently turned into a whip,” Yue’er said with a smile as she walked forward to pick up the whip. The more she looked at it, the more she liked it. “It’s really beautiful.”"]},{"number":4790,"title":"Chapter 4790: Acknowledging The Master","paragraphs":["The whip's handle was exquisitely shaped like the head of a phoenix, and the whip itself was a vibrant, fiery red with nine intersecting whip marks. When held, one could feel a distinct hint of heat radiating from it.","\"Put it away first, let's go out! Don't make Master worry,\" Hao'er advised, urging her to store the whip.","\"Alright.\" Yue'er smiled sweetly, a look of pure joy on her face. She placed the whip into her personal space, then proceeded to cut the petals on the inside of their arms. In the next moment, a bright light enveloped them, instantly teleporting them away.","Outside the mirror, at the banquet, everyone watching exchanged surprised glances. No one had anticipated that the Nine-Section Red Flame Phoenix Scale Whip would be obtained in such a manner, or that the person to acquire it would be a five- or six-year-old girl. Their feelings, it was safe to say, were incredibly complicated.","The three children, now outside the spirit realm, saw that their injuries had all miraculously healed. They couldn't help but smile, quickly making their way forward.","As they approached the banquet hall, Yue'er hadn't quite arrived, but her excited voice already reached the Azure Emperor's ears. \"Master, Master, I got the whip!\" She ran over, pulling the whip from her space as if presenting a priceless treasure, and held it out for her master to see. \"Master, look, this is the whip! It was transformed from a phoenix!\" <abbr class=\"plain-imprint-a\">Brought to you by MV6LEMPY6R.</abbr>","\"Master.\" Hao'er and Muchen also arrived before the Azure Emperor, bowing respectfully.","\"Hmm, sit down!\" The Azure Emperor gestured, a satisfied smile gracing his features as he bade them take their seats.","\"Yes,\" the two replied, walking behind him to sit down.","The Azure Emperor picked up the whip, glancing at its intricate form. Then, he looked at Immortal Elder Lingmu beside him and said, \"Immortal Elder, this whip has been obtained by my little disciple.\"","Immortal Elder Lingmu offered a bitter smile and replied, \"Yes! I really didn't expect this!\" He then retrieved an ancient book from his own space, looked at the little girl, waved his hand, and called out, \"Yun Qi, little girl, come here, come here.\"","Yue'er glanced at her master, who gave a slight nod of approval. She then walked over to Immortal Elder Lingmu, bowed respectfully, and addressed him, \"Immortal Elder.\"","\"What an extraordinary child,\" Immortal Elder Lingmu said with a smile. \"From today onwards, that whip is yours. I will also give you this book on whip techniques. Take it back and practice hard.\" He handed her the book and gently patted her on the head.","\"Yes, thank you, Immortal Elder Lingmu.\" Yue'er smiled happily, taking the book with both hands and expressing her gratitude before running back to her master.","The Azure Emperor held the whip in his hand, a ray of light flashing from it before he handed it to Yue'er. \"Drip your blood on it for it to acknowledge its master!\"","Hearing this, Yue'er bit her finger, allowing a single drop of blood to fall onto the whip. She watched as a flash of light, like a red flame, quickly passed through the weapon.","\"Take it.\" The Azure Emperor placed the whip in her hand. \"This whip can transform at will. It can be long or short, it can turn into a dagger or a soft sword, and it can even turn into red silk. In the future, you must practice hard. This treasure can become a weapon with extreme lethality in battle.\"","\"Yes, disciple will remember,\" Yue'er replied happily. She took the whip, rolled it up, and tucked it into her waist.","\"Congratulations! Congratulations to the Azure Emperor's beloved disciple for obtaining such an ancient treasure,\" an immortal old man said with a smile, bowing in congratulations."]},{"number":4791,"title":"Chapter 4791: A Costly Bet","paragraphs":["Chapter 4791: A Costly Bet","“Today, we’ve truly broadened our horizons. The three beloved disciples of the Azure Emperor are genuinely outstanding and exceptional!” another immortal said with a smile, his gaze fixed on the three children, brimming with admiration. How could they have possibly missed such talented individuals?","Everyone offered their congratulations one by one, a string of compliments flowing from their mouths. Hearing this, the Azure Emperor also smiled, his heart swelling with joy. He then looked at Immortal Zinan, who sported a grim expression, and remarked, “Immortal Zinan, it seems you still haven’t given me the item you lost to me!”","Hearing this, Immortal Zinan’s mouth twitched, and he managed a stiff smile. He glanced at the Azure Emperor, then retrieved a piece of golden-purple soft armor from his interspatial ring. With a flick of his hand, the item flew out and landed in front of the Azure Emperor.","“Azure Emperor, keep this well. This is the Purple Sun Golden Soft Armor.” Seeing his treasured possession change hands so easily, his heart truly ached.","The Azure Emperor’s lips curved slightly. He glanced at the golden-purple soft armor before him and said to Yue’er, “Little Qi, you won this back; take it!”","Hearing this, Yue’er was stunned and a little confused. She blinked her beautiful eyes and asked curiously, “Master, how did your disciple win it back? Your disciple didn’t do anything!”","“Hehehe...” The Azure Emperor laughed softly, glancing at Immortal Zinan, who looked utterly miserable and pained. “Didn’t you kill that giant python? Immortal Zinan made a bet with me and lost this treasure.” He smiled as if it were nothing, reaching out and stroking the purple-gold soft armor in front of him. “This is one of Immortal Zinan’s rare treasures. Wearing it can protect one’s life and also help with cultivation. It’s so precious that even Immortal Zinan himself is reluctant to wear it! Today, it’s your lucky day, little girl.”","Hearing this, Yue’er’s eyes lit up, and she flashed a sly smile. She bowed to Immortal Zinan and said in a crisp voice, “So it’s such a treasure. Thank you, Immortal Zinan.”","Immortal Zinan listened to the master and disciple, his mouth twitching again, and he managed another stiff smile: “It’s all thanks to your skill.” If it weren’t for this little girl who genuinely killed that giant python herself, how could he have possibly lost that treasure? Now, there was no point in saying anything more.","Yue’er turned around and looked at her master, asking, “Master, can I give this treasure to Senior Brother?”","“Of course you can,” the Azure Emperor smiled and nodded.","Hao’er was slightly taken aback, then stood up and said, “Master, I also have soft armor to protect myself, so let’s give this one to Junior Sister instead!”","“Senior Brother, Master said that this is a good treasure, so please accept it! Wearing it will help you cultivate! In the future, you’ll become even more powerful and be able to protect us better!” Yue’er said with a smile as she picked up the soft armor and placed it in his hands.","“Since your Junior Sister has said so, then accept it!” the Azure Emperor interjected.","Seeing this, Hao’er nodded and said, “Yes.” He then turned to Yue’er and smiled gently, “Thank you, Junior Sister.”","“Don’t mention it, don’t mention it. You’re my senior brother, not an outsider,” Yue’er said with a smile, walking forward to hold Muchen’s hand and adding with a grin, “Second Senior Brother, next time I get a good treasure, I’ll take it and give it to you.”"]},{"number":4792,"title":"Chapter 4792: The Immortal Palace","paragraphs":["Chapter 4792: The Immortal Palace","Muchen smiled and agreed. He wasn’t angry that his sister gave the soft armor to their elder brother. After all, he was their eldest, and they naturally wanted to share good things with him.","Everyone present was taken aback and a little surprised. It was, after all, a rare treasure, and the little girl had simply handed it over to her senior brother. It truly caught them off guard. What was even more surprising was her declaration that the next good treasure she found, she’d give to her second senior brother.","Just hearing this sent a jolt through their hearts. They wondered if any of their own treasures might pique her interest. After confirming they possessed nothing so valuable that others would covet, they secretly breathed a sigh of relief. If there truly was a treasure that caught her eye, it would be difficult to say if they could keep it!","“Ha ha, I’m sure everyone is tired. Why don’t you go to your rooms and rest first?” Immortal Elder Lingmu said with a smile, then ordered the immortal servants to escort everyone to the guest rooms.","Yue’er, having obtained both the whip and the whip technique book, was eager to go back and study them. Upon seeing her master stand up, she immediately followed, preparing to leave. Unexpectedly, the Azure Emperor glanced at the three of them and said, “You follow the immortal attendants to the guest rooms to rest. Your master will play a game of chess.”","“Yes,” the three replied in unison, then followed the immortal attendants away.","Meanwhile, in another corner of this celestial realm, extraordinary phenomena continued to unfold in the sky. Celestial music resounded, a rainbow spanned the heavens, cranes soared gracefully, magpies chirped joyfully, and patches of seven-coloured auspicious clouds drifted lazily. Amidst this celestial display of blessings, a sacred island rose majestically from below, now suspended in the sky.","A magnificent and elegant Immortal Palace naturally took shape within the sacred light. On the island, flowers bloomed in abundance, sacred trees bore fruit, and celestial mist swirled around, creating a scene of unparalleled beauty. Even more enchanting were the flower fairies who had transformed into human form, their colourful robes flowing as they danced among the blossoms. In the sky, two cranes transformed into two white-robed immortals, holding petals in their hands as they danced through the air, gently scattering petals and laughing joyfully.","And in that holy light and shower of flowers, Mo Chen, dressed in white like an immortal, slowly descended from the sky and landed on this floating celestial island. As the golden light on his body dissipated, the strange phenomena in the sky also gradually disappeared, leaving only the fairy attendants, now transformed into human form, kneeling respectfully on the ground, offering their congratulations.","“Congratulations to the Holy Emperor on his ascension! May he live as long as heaven and earth, and shine as brightly as the sun and moon!”","“Immortal lords from all over, we have come to pay our respects to the Holy Emperor and congratulate him on his ascension! May he live as long as heaven and earth, and shine as brightly as the sun and moon!”","The immortal lords and other immortals who had arrived outside the immortal island at some unknown time now came forward to offer their congratulations. The newly ascended Holy Emperor had descended upon this place, and he was now their master. Even though they were powerful immortal lords and immortals from the lower realms, with influential families ruling over vast regions, they still had to come here to pay their respects to the ascended Holy Emperor.","However, everyone was very unfamiliar with this newly ascended Holy Emperor. They didn’t know where he had ascended from, what kind of person he had been before, or how he had managed to ascend from the lower realms to become a Holy Emperor. Yet, despite being filled with curiosity and a desire to investigate, they did not dare to be the slightest bit presumptuous. Without his permission, even though they were all powerful Immortal Lords, they dared not enter the Holy Emperor’s Immortal Island domain.","At this moment, Mo Chen, who had landed in front of the Immortal Palace, heard the voices from outside and looked out."]},{"number":4793,"title":"Chapter 4793: Visitors from All Around","paragraphs":["\"Please, everyone, come in,\" Mo Chen's voice resonated clearly, carrying a powerful spiritual energy that reached the ears of all present. Hearing the invitation, they exchanged glances before entering the immortal palace together.","Upon their arrival, the grand gates of the immortal palace stood open. Inside, a man dressed in pristine white, resembling a celestial being, sat serenely on the main seat. His youthful appearance sparked a flicker of surprise in their eyes. With respectful bows, they greeted him, \"Greetings, Holy Emperor. Congratulations on your ascension.\" <code class=\"phantom-imprint\">The g+enui&n$e a%rticle& r%e!s&i^des@ on M|$V+|L#&+.</code>","These were individuals who had cultivated for many years, reaching the pinnacle of the Divine King level, and were reverently known as Immortal Lords or Immortal Elders. They were astonished to see someone so young possessing the strength of a supreme peak cultivator, having ascended and achieved the qualification to live as long as heaven and earth itself. They couldn't help but acknowledge his extraordinary talent, feeling a mix of envy, shock, and, above all, profound awe. To ascend at such a tender age spoke volumes about his exceptional cultivation and innate gifts.","\"There's no need for such formalities; please, sit down,\" Mo Chen said, gesturing for them to take seats on either side of the hall.","\"Yes, thank you, Holy Emperor,\" they replied, moving to their designated places. As they settled down, their gazes once again fell upon the Holy Emperor. This closer look brought an even greater wave of astonishment. Previously, they hadn't observed him meticulously, but now they noticed that the Holy Emperor had cultivated a true immortal body. Furthermore, a golden lotus mark shimmered between his eyebrows, and his entire being was bathed in a brilliant holy light, creating an ethereal halo around him.","This radiant presence was precisely why they addressed him as the Holy Emperor. His ascension had been marked by a vast expanse of holy light that illuminated the earth—a phenomenon ordinary beings could not replicate. It was now evident that this luminescence was a reflection emanating from the golden lotus. Once a cultivator's strength reached the peak of the Supreme Realm and they ascended to immortality, there were no further immortal ranks to climb, only the esteemed title of Holy Emperor.","Among those gathered, some were at the peak of the Divine King realm, while others were in the early stages of the Supreme realm. Their respectful titles, Immortal Lords or Immortal Elder, depended on their bone age. Despite having attained such formidable strength, and even ruling over their respective regions, some among them might never achieve true immortality and become Holy Emperors. Therefore, even though they commanded reverence from others, they stood before this newly ascended Holy Emperor with utmost respect, devoid of any trace of arrogance.","\"It has been nearly a thousand years since anyone has ascended to immortality through cultivation. To witness the Holy Emperor's ascension today is truly a great joy,\" an Immortal Elder remarked, rising to bow with a smile. \"I am Immortal Elder Muhua, the Old Predecessor of the Duan family in Lucent Immortal City. Today, I have brought gifts to congratulate the Holy Emperor on his great joy.\"","As he spoke, he flicked his sleeves, and four boxes filled with treasures, alongside two rare and precious artifacts, materialized in the center of the palace. With the first gift presented, others followed suit, one after another, retrieving treasures from their spatial artifacts and offering them. In a short time, the various treasures in the middle of the grand hall piled up like a small mountain, radiating a dazzling, brilliant light.","On this side, Mo Chen and his guests engaged in leisurely conversation in the hall, with Mo Chen inquiring about the situations in the territories under their jurisdiction, as time quietly passed them by.","Meanwhile, on Immortal Elder Lingmu's fairy island, the Azure Emperor had allowed them to stay for a few days, giving them time to relax and enjoy themselves. After these few days, the Azure Emperor took the three of them to pay their respects to Immortal Elder Lingmu before they returned."]},{"number":4794,"title":"Chapter 4794: Yet Another Year","paragraphs":["Chapter 4794: Yet Another Year","Inside the airship, Yue’er settled beside the Azure Emperor, leaning against him. “Master,” she asked, “can we go see Uncle Mo Chen? He ascended; can we go visit him?”","The Azure Emperor, with his eyes closed and one hand propping his head, didn’t even open them. “No,” he stated.","“Why not? No one will recognize us now,” Yue’er blinked, a puzzled expression on her face.","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor opened his eyes, sat upright, and glanced at the two individuals not far away, then at the little girl beside him. He slowly said, “Your mother didn’t send you to me so you could visit relatives. If you have free time, you’d better use it to practice.” He then looked at Yue’er. “Have you memorized your whip technique?”","“I’ve memorized it, but I haven’t practiced it all yet,” Yue’er replied softly.","“Then put some effort into it and don’t think about anything else. Until you can stand on your own two feet, I won’t let you see anyone you know,” he said slowly, glancing at all three of them. “When you go back, all of you go into seclusion to practice.”","“Yes,” the three responded in unison.","Yue’er then left his side and joined her two brothers. The three of them went into the cabin and whispered among themselves. After following their master back to the mountains, they were ordered to close themselves off for training and not to venture out. Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, another year had passed.","In the Immortal Realm, Feng Jiu, dressed in her signature red robes, once again arrived at the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm. Du Fan, Leng Hua, and Leng Shuang were guarding this area. They hadn’t seen their master for a year, so they were overjoyed to see her return.","“Master!”","“Master, you said you were coming back, but we didn’t expect you to arrive so quickly.”","“Master, have you been all right these past few days, being away from home?”","The three gathered around her, their eyes filled with concern and affection.","Feng Jiu smiled slightly. “Yes, I’m fine.” She then looked out at the sea and asked, “Is everything normal here?”","“Yes, Master, everything is normal. We haven’t gone into the sea to check because of your orders. We don’t know how Hell’s Lord is doing this past year,” Du Fan replied, his gaze also falling on the sea.","“No one has gone into the sea to disturb him this year, right?” Feng Jiu asked softly.","“No, those few knew that Hell’s Lord was resting in the sea, so they didn’t come to disturb him. Over the past year, the cultivators who were originally guarding the area have also dispersed, and no one dares to sneak into the sea anymore.”","“Master, it’s getting late. Let’s go to the airship and rest first!” Leng Shuang suggested.","“Mmm,” Feng Jiu replied, then followed the three of them to the airship.","All the Feng Guards were delighted by her arrival and prepared to welcome her. They divided up the work: some went hunting for wild game, while others prepared different dishes and wine. When night fell, everyone sat together, eating, drinking, and chatting. Feng Jiu also shared stories of what she had seen and encountered during the past year.","“You must have heard about Mo Chen’s ascension. Over the past year, I made a special trip to the Nalan family to inform his father of the news,” Feng Jiu said, taking a sip of wine and looking up at the sky, her eyes narrowing. It had been a year since Mo Chen’s ascension."]},{"number":4795,"title":"Chapter 4795: Meeting Again","paragraphs":["Chapter 4795: Meeting Again","It felt to her as if Mo Chen’s ascension day had occurred just yesterday, yet in the blink of an eye, a full year had already come and gone. The passage of time was sometimes startling in its swiftness, and this particular year seemed to have flown by with an almost unsettling speed. Feng Jiu found herself reflecting on the myriad changes and challenges that had unfolded during this period, all while the memory of Mo Chen’s departure remained so vivid in her mind.","“Master, news of Young Master Mo Chen’s ascension has gradually spread throughout the land,” Leng Hua reported, her gaze fixed on Feng Jiu. “Many people are quite surprised. After all, so many witnessed his disappearance from the heavens, so they didn’t anticipate him ascending first.” Leng Hua then shifted the conversation, her tone becoming more cautious. “Master, in the past year, have those people sent anyone to hunt you down? We’ve been vigilant, but the world is vast, and their reach could be extensive.”","Feng Jiu’s lips curled into a faint, knowing smile. “Even if they wished to kill me, they couldn’t reach me here. The disparity in strength is far too great; how could they possibly take my life?” Her confidence was unwavering, rooted in an understanding of her own power and the formidable defenses she had established. The threats of mere mortals seemed trivial against her might.","“Master, in the past year, the Black Tortoise Monarch has come looking for you several times,” Du Fan interjected, his eyes on her. “The last time was only a month ago. He arrived with his wife, stating that they wished to see the eldest young master, Hao’er.” Du Fan’s expression was unreadable, but a hint of weariness could be discerned.","“He wants to see Hao’er?” Feng Jiu’s smile vanished, replaced by a cold expression. “Does Hao’er still have any relationship with them? That connection ended eight hundred years ago. How dare they come here now and claim they want to see Hao’er?” Her voice held a sharp edge, betraying the lingering resentment she harbored. The past, for her, was not something easily forgotten or forgiven, especially when it involved her son.","Du Fan and the others remained silent, understanding the depth of their master’s feelings. They knew that when Feng Jiu had taken Hao’er away, there had been significant unpleasantness and a profound rift between him and the Black Tortoise Monarch and his wife. Perhaps with the inexorable passage of time, the Monarch and his wife had begun to remember their eldest son, perhaps they had come to realize the extent of their past mistakes and how truly far they had gone in their actions. However, for now, it was simply impossible for them to see Hao’er. The wounds were too deep, the betrayal too profound.","“I sent people to persuade them away each time,” Du Fan continued, breaking the silence. “The last time, I was the one who personally urged them to leave. They claimed they wanted to see Master and apologize to him in person, and they sincerely hoped that the eldest young master would find it in his heart to forgive them.” He delivered the message faithfully, even though he knew the likely reaction it would elicit.","Feng Jiu’s eyes turned to ice. “In the future, simply send them away. As for everything else, especially any news about Hao’er, do not let them know anything. Do you understand?” Her command was absolute, leaving no room for negotiation or interpretation.","“Yes,” they replied in unison, their voices firm. In truth, only their most trusted confidants knew the true whereabouts of Hao’er, Muchen, and Muyue. The others, the vast majority of their associates, had no idea, a secret carefully guarded to protect them.","“I’m going out to sea tomorrow, so I won’t be drinking tonight. You all should drink less too,” Feng Jiu announced, rising from her seat and addressing Leng Shuang. “Is the hot water ready for my bath?”","“Yes, Master, it’s ready,” Leng Shuang affirmed, also standing and leading her toward the cabin.","Du Fan rubbed his nose, a hint of regret in his posture. “Perhaps I shouldn’t have told the Master about this.” He knew that this particular news would invariably put their master in a somber mood, and he felt a pang of responsibility.","Leng Hua patted him on the shoulder reassuringly. “The Master is probably just tired, Du Fan. Besides, this information had to be conveyed eventually. You didn’t do anything wrong by telling her the truth.”","“Alright, clear everything away!” Du Fan commanded, turning to the others. “The Master will go out to sea tomorrow, so don’t drink any more wine tonight, lest it interfere with his work. We need to be alert and prepared.” He then ordered everyone to clear away the remaining wine and food, ensuring a focused and sober evening.","Early the next morning, as the first rays of dawn touched the horizon, Feng Jiu descended alone into the depths of the sea. Her destination was the sacred place where Mo Ze was still slumbering, awaiting his full recovery.","Perhaps after another year of the ocean’s silent nourishment, his body seemed to have become much more solid at the bottom of the sea, his form more defined, less ethereal. Looking at his familiar face, which appeared as serene as if he were merely asleep, her eyes were filled with an overwhelming tenderness and profound affection. The sight of him, even in this suspended state, brought a solace that transcended words.","He was still there, even if it was at the very bottom of the sea, even if he hadn’t fully woken up yet. But to her, his presence was undeniable, a constant anchor in her life. She held an unshakeable belief that one day, he would indeed awaken fully, rise from his deep slumber, and return to her and their beloved children, completing their family once more.","With a gentle resolve, she removed the protective barrier she had placed at the bottom of the sea, allowing herself passage. She then walked step by step toward him, her movements deliberate and full of purpose. In the very next moment, the potent spirit energy within her body surged forth, a powerful current of life. Simultaneously, the unique Blue Lotus energy, an intrinsic part of her being, also surged out, flowing directly towards his body, intending to accelerate his recovery and bring him back to her."]},{"number":4796,"title":"Chapter 4796: Preparing for Ascension","paragraphs":["She remained at the bottom of the sea for a full day and a night, continuously transferring her Blue Lotus energy to him. It was a tireless vigil, a selfless act of devotion, until the next day, when a wave of exhaustion finally washed over her. She gently withdrew her hand, drawing all the Blue Lotus energy back into her own body, feeling the familiar ebb and flow of power within her.","“Mo Ze, I am ready to ascend,” she whispered, her voice soft yet resolute, echoing in the profound silence of the deep. “Stay here and take good care of yourself. After I ascend, I will kill all those who harmed you and avenge you! When that time comes, if you still haven’t woken up, I will bring the children back to see you.”","She spoke tenderly, raising her hand to gently stroke his familiar face, a gesture filled with an aching love. Leaning down, she pressed her lips to his, a soft, lingering kiss. However, the sensation was ethereal, as though she were kissing the surface of water, with the faint, almost imperceptible sound of ripples spreading outward from their contact. She stepped back, quietly observing him, her eyes a complex mixture of reluctance, longing, and unwavering determination.","“Don’t worry, I’ve made all the necessary preparations,” she murmured softly, as if speaking directly to his sleeping spirit. “I will definitely succeed in ascending.” She gazed at him deeply one last time, committing every detail of his peaceful face to memory. Then, she began to step back, one careful step at a time, creating a respectful distance. After retreating sufficiently, she re-cast the protective barrier around him, ensuring his undisturbed rest, and then slowly ascended out of the water.","Back on the surface, she landed gracefully on her airship. She stood at the bow, gazing quietly out at the vast, shimmering expanse of the sea. A profound sense of peace settled in her heart, a quiet calm before the impending storm of her ascension.","Du Fan, Leng Hua, and Leng Shuang stood respectfully behind her. Observing her standing there in silent contemplation, without uttering a single word, the three exchanged knowing glances. They understood the weight of the moment and her internal struggles, so they chose not to speak, simply offering their silent, unwavering companionship from behind.","After a long time, which felt both fleeting and eternal, Feng Jiu finally turned around. She spoke a few brief words to the three loyal companions, her voice low and steady, before heading back into the cabin to rest.","“Is Master okay? You don’t look very well,” Leng Shuang ventured, a note of genuine concern in her voice.","“She’s probably just tired,” Du Fan replied, his tone dismissive of any deeper issues. “It’s nothing serious.” He tried to sound reassuring, but a hint of worry lingered in his own eyes.","“I wonder what kind of situation Hell’s Lord is in right now?” Leng Hua mused softly, his gaze drifting out across the endless sea, a quiet sadness in his voice.","“I guess the situation isn’t very good, otherwise Master wouldn’t have come up alone,” Du Fan sighed lightly, the weight of their unspoken fears hanging in the air. “She would have brought him with her. At that time, Master said that it was impossible to bring Hell’s Lord out of the bottom of the East Sea Spirit Realm. Otherwise, how could Master bear to leave Hell’s Lord alone in the deep sea?”","Hearing this, Leng Hua and Leng Shuang fell into a mournful silence. Indeed, the logic was undeniable. If there were any way to bring Hell’s Lord out of that submerged realm, their master, with her boundless love and devotion, would never have left him to sleep alone in the cold depths. But the grim reality was that they didn’t know when Hell’s Lord would wake up, or if he ever truly would.","What they didn’t expect, however, was that when their master said she would go in to rest “for a while,” that rest would stretch into an astonishing three days...","Three days later, in the early morning, Feng Jiu finally emerged from the cabin. The exhaustion that had etched itself onto her face a few days prior was now completely gone, banished by deep recuperation. Her entire mental state had recovered remarkably well, and a renewed vigor radiated from her.","“Master,” the three greeted her in unison, their relief palpable as they saw her looking as energetic and vibrant as ever.","“Mm,” Feng Jiu replied simply. She walked out to the bow of the ship and sat down at the table there, then motioned for them to join her. “You sit down too! I have something important to tell you.”","Hearing the gravity in her voice, the three exchanged quick glances before dutifully sitting down. “What are your orders, Master?” they asked, their postures attentive.","“I am preparing to undergo tribulation and ascend,” she declared, her voice calm and steady, despite the momentousness of her words. “So, you will have to take charge of everything in the future. Also, I haven’t yet told the Feng family’s old residence about my impending ascension, so after I ascend, you should inform them about it personally.”","Feng Jiu looked at each of them, her gaze firm and clear, as she meticulously instructed them on the myriad responsibilities they would need to undertake in the days to come. Finally, she concluded, “There is also the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm where Mo Ze rests. After I ascend, you must guard it carefully and not make any mistakes whatsoever. You don’t need to actively check on the situation at the bottom of the sea; simply focus all your efforts on guarding it with your lives.”"]},{"number":4797,"title":"Chapter 4797: Ascension at the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm","paragraphs":["Chapter 4797: Ascension at the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm","Listening to her words, the three fell silent for a moment, a mix of apprehension and awe on their faces. Finally, Du Fan broke the stillness, his voice laced with concern. “Master, how long will it take for Hell’s Lord to wake up? Are all the preparations for your ascension truly complete? Is everything absolutely certain? If those above take advantage of your ascension to strike again, then...”","Feng Jiu offered a faint smile, her expression serene. “I don’t know when he will wake up, but when he does, it will be time for me to ascend. You just need to stand guard and not worry about anything else. As for my ascension, don’t worry! I am ready. I know that those people want to kill me, so I won’t give them the chance. Besides...”","She paused, her gaze lifting to the vast sky above her. The corners of her lips curved slightly, revealing a hint of a chilling smile. Her voice was soft and faint, yet carried an undercurrent of cold determination. “My ascension will be a battle between me and them. Once I ascend, they will no longer be able to do as they please. Instead, they will be the ones who should be worried.”","“Master is ascending, let’s go protect her!” Du Fan declared, his resolve firm.","“I notified my brother and sister three days ago,” Feng Jiu continued, addressing her loyal companions. “The place I chose for my ascension is this Eastern Sea Spirit Realm. They should arrive in a few days, and Luo Yu and the others will also be coming.”","She looked at them, her tone serious. “Listen carefully. When I ascend, there will be Spirit Energy overflowing and Immortal Energy swirling within a hundred meters of me. This Immortal Energy is a rare opportunity for those who cultivate. You must seize this opportunity and see if it can help you.”","They exchanged glances, their eyes wide with understanding, then nodded in solemn agreement. “Yes, Master.”","Feng Jiu looked up again, her clear gaze fixed on the endless sky, her eyes brimming with determination and conviction. She spoke slowly, each word carrying immense weight. “Now, the different layers of the Heavenly Realm are separated, but one day in the future, I will open the gates connecting the nine layers of the Heavenly Realm, break through the layers of separation, and unite the nine layers of heaven and earth!”","Hearing this audacious declaration, the three were deeply shaken to their core. Their eyes flashed with a burning light, and they looked at their master with gazes filled with fervent admiration. Unconsciously, wide smiles spread across their faces.","“We believe that Master can definitely do it!” they exclaimed in unison, their voices filled with unshakeable faith.","They didn’t know about others, but their master, with her indomitable will and power, could absolutely achieve such a monumental feat!","The next day, early in the morning, even before dawn had fully broken, Feng Jiu was already seated on a massive rock by the sea within the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm. She was dressed in a striking red, a color that seemed to hum with latent power against the muted predawn light. Her black hair, untied and free, cascaded naturally behind her. The gentle sea breeze stirred, as if a pair of invisible, tender hands were lightly lifting and dancing with her tresses.","Because Feng Jiu was choosing this sacred place for her ascension, all humans and beasts within a hundred-mile radius had been meticulously driven away by the Phoenix Guards. No one else had arrived yet; only a dedicated Phoenix team remained standing guard, accompanied by the ever-loyal Du Fan, Leng Hua, and Leng Shuang.","Following Feng Jiu’s precise instructions, they stood at a respectful distance, dozens of meters away from her, watching quietly and guarding her. Despite their outward composure, their hearts pounded with a mixture of anticipation and worry.","With the preceding event of Hell’s Lord’s current state fresh in their minds, even if their Master had confidently declared it was fine and that she was fully prepared, they still couldn’t help but feel a pervasive anxiety. The sheer magnitude of an ascension, and the dangers it entailed, weighed heavily on them.","However, they also knew, with absolute certainty, that their worries, while genuine, could not truly help her in this moment. All they could do was quietly stand guard from afar, ensuring that absolutely no one disturbed her sacred ascent, allowing her to embark on this momentous journey with complete peace of mind.","Feng Jiu sat calmly on the ancient boulder, her eyes fixed on the horizon as the morning light began to slowly creep up from the eastern sea, painting the sky with soft hues. A gentle, knowing smile graced her lips. Then, with a quiet resolve, she slowly closed her eyes, ready to face the heavens."]},{"number":4798,"title":"Chapter 4798: Deafening","paragraphs":["Chapter 4798: Deafening","At that moment, her heart was calm, and her resolve was unwavering.","She knew what she had to do, she knew what she would face, and she knew the path she would choose. It was a path forged in fire and tempered by unwavering love, a journey she embraced with every fiber of her being.","As she gently closed her eyes, the morning sun rose in the east, transforming the vast sea into a breathtaking expanse of red and gold. With graceful, deliberate movements, she turned her hands, mobilizing the vast spirit energy within her body, and slowly settled them into a lotus position upon her legs.","Pure spirit energy surged outwards from her body, spreading in an invisible wave around her. Simultaneously, the ancient divine beast’s aura, a potent force residing deep within her, was unleashed. It mingled with the surging spirit energy, amplifying its power as it expanded.","The sheer force of the surging spirit energy caused her red robes to rustle violently in the wind, her black hair fluttering wildly in the growing breeze. The very air, both in the sky and above the sea, gradually began to stir, churning up powerful waves and drawing in dense clouds from the distant horizon.","The early morning sky, which had been clear and cloudless just moments before, now underwent a dramatic transformation. With the immense surge of energy from Feng Jiu’s body and the unleashing of her true power, heavy clouds rapidly gathered and floated in from the distance. They converged steadily over the East Sea, swiftly forming a vast, ominous dark cloud formation that swallowed the light.","The rising morning light from the east was completely obscured by these thick, oppressive clouds, with not a single ray of sunlight able to break through. Below, the once calm sea was now violently churned by fierce winds, and colossal waves crashed against the shore with thunderous roars, spraying countless droplets of water high into the turbulent air.","In the sky, a low, muffled rumble of thunder began, slowly but surely intensifying. One after another, the deep reverberations followed, as if gathering into a colossal lightning tribulation that hung menacingly, yet did not immediately descend. Lightning flashed intermittently from within the dark clouds, illuminating their terrifying depths, but still, the mighty thunderbolts themselves held back.","In the distance, Du Fan, Leng Hua, and Leng Shuang watched with bated breath, their palms growing sweaty with anticipation and fear. They looked at their master, a small, solitary figure against the tumultuous backdrop, then at the menacing dark clouds in the sky, and the enormous lightning tribulation that seemed to be gathering directly above her head, poised to strike at any moment.","“Don’t worry, Master will be fine,” Du Fan muttered nervously, his voice thin with strain. “She said that everything is ready, and she is confident and sure that nothing will happen. Don’t worry, don’t worry.” He spoke almost frantically, not knowing whether he was trying to comfort the two people beside him or desperately trying to convince himself.","As time stretched agonizingly, a moment of profound significance arrived. At the first precise moment of the hour of Chen, a blinding flash of lightning split the sky. With a deafening roar, a colossal bolt of lightning thundered down from the clouds, striking Feng Jiu below with terrifying precision.","“Boom!”","The sound of the lightning tribulation reverberated throughout the sky, echoing to the very highest clouds and resonating across the heavens. It was a sound that startled powerful beings in all directions, drawing their immediate attention!","Just as the initial lightning tribulation struck her, several more bolts of lightning simultaneously descended from the sky. These new bolts formed several towering pillars of electricity that completely encircled Feng Jiu. These crackling pillars stretched from the churning surface of the sea all the way up into the dense, dark clouds above, emitting loud, continuous crackling sounds. Strands of raw electricity shot out from these formidable pillars, sending a chilling sensation down the spines of all who witnessed the spectacle, a clear warning of the immense power unleashed.","At the very same moment, when the powerful beings from all corners of the realms heard the resounding boom of the lightning tribulation, they were all momentarily stunned into silence.","“Lightning tribulation?! Who has advanced?”","“Listen to the sound of the lightning tribulation; it’s a little different from before. It seems like...”","“Is this the lightning tribulation of ascension? How could someone else have ascended? A year ago, Mo Chen ascended to the Nine Heavens, and now, a year later, could it possibly be... Feng Jiu?”","Everyone was utterly shocked, their voices rising in a cacophony of speculation and discussion. Not long after, another thunderous clap of lightning sounded, even more deafening than the first, echoing across the vast expanse of the world!"]},{"number":4799,"title":"Chapter 4799: Reactions Across the Realms","paragraphs":["Chapter 4799: Reactions Across the Realms","“It must be that Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu who ascended!” a voice boomed, cutting through the murmurs.","“Apart from that Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu, there is no one else!” another agreed, conviction in their tone.","“Quick, follow me to take a look!” an eager command rang out.","After hearing the unusual sound of the lightning tribulation, powerful figures from all corners of the land rushed towards the source. In the past, they would never have had the opportunity to witness such a momentous event. However, with the recent emergence of Xuanyuan Mo Ze, Feng Jiu, and Nalan Mo Chen—three extraordinary, demonic geniuses, all remarkably young yet possessing supreme cultivation—the landscape had shifted. Especially with Mo Chen having already ascended, and now it being Feng Jiu’s turn, a palpable excitement rippled through the onlookers.","Perhaps another Great Emperor would be born and ascend to the Nine Heavens! This thought ignited hope and awe in many.","Some, however, harbored a different kind of happiness, secretly thinking that with the “demon” Feng Jiu gone, this realm would finally be theirs. They would no longer have to worry about her interference, no matter what they chose to do in the future.","Thus, with a mix of anticipation, apprehension, and even malicious glee, the powerful beings from all directions, driven by their varied motivations, rushed towards the booming sound of the lightning tribulation, eager to witness the unfolding spectacle.","In the Upper Immortal Realm of the Nine Heavens, far above the mortal world, Mo Chen opened his eyes in the serene Immortal Palace on the floating Immortal Island. A gentle smile touched his lips as the distant sound of the lightning tribulation reached him.","His expression was calm and gentle, as always, but the light in his eyes was unmistakably filled with joy and anticipation.","Feng Jiu, she’s finally coming! The silent thought resonated within him.","Meanwhile, in another part of the Upper Immortal Realm, when one of the Great Emperors of the Four Directions heard the unmistakable sound of the lightning tribulation echoing from the lower realm, his expression transformed in an instant. Who else in the lower realm would dare to ascend to the heavens except the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu? A surge of fury twisted his features.","“Damn it!” he spat, his voice laced with venom. “I never thought that after trying every trick in the book for over a year, I still couldn’t take her life! She’s still alive, and now she actually wants to ascend to immortality? She truly doesn’t know her place!”","The Emperor stepped out of his opulent palace, his hands clasped behind his back. He looked up at the vast expanse of the sky, listening to the ominous rumble of thunder that permeated the air, and his face darkened further.","“Fine!” he declared, a sinister smile creeping onto his lips. “Since she dares to ascend, we can kill her while she’s in the air!” In the next moment, he flicked his sleeves with a decisive gesture and vanished from the spot, bound for the scene of the ascension.","Meanwhile, at Yunxiao Mountain, when the Azure Emperor heard the powerful sound of the lightning tribulation, he raised an eyebrow in surprise. He muttered in a low voice, “This Feng Jiu is truly bold. How long has it been? She dares to ascend to immortality? It seems that she is genuinely prepared for this momentous step.”","As soon as he finished speaking, he paused for a brief moment, then walked out of his tranquil cave abode. Placing his hands behind his back, he gazed up at the sky, listening intently to the rumbling thunder overhead. A faint, amused smile played on his lips as he murmured, “I wonder if she can truly ascend successfully.”","“Master, Master!”","The three children—Hao’er, Muchen, and Yue’er—descended from the sky on their swords, their faces etched with anxiety and worry. They quickly landed before him, their small forms radiating concern.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the three of them, a knowing look in his eyes, and inquired, “Why aren’t you cultivating properly? Why have you come all the way here?”","“Master, is my mother undergoing the ascension tribulation?” Hao’er asked, his eyes fixed on the Azure Emperor, brimming with urgent inquiry. Being the oldest of the three, when he heard the distinct sound of the lightning, he immediately suspected that it was very likely their mother who was facing the formidable ascension tribulation.","“Master, Master, is it my mother? Will she be able to ascend successfully? Is she in danger?” Yue’er, the youngest, stepped forward and tugged gently on his sleeve, her little face scrunched with worry.","They were still young and didn’t fully comprehend the complexities of ascension, but after hearing their Big Brother Hao’er’s words, a stark realization dawned on them: the person ascending to the Immortal Realm was most likely their beloved mother. Therefore, without a second thought for their cultivation, the three of them hurriedly rushed to their master, desperate for answers and reassurance."]},{"number":4800,"title":"Chapter 4800: The Sky Is About To Change","paragraphs":["Muchen didn’t say anything, but he looked at their master nervously, his young mind grappling with the possibility that this incredibly powerful being, undergoing such a fierce advancement, was truly their mother, just as their Big Brother had suggested.","The Azure Emperor glanced at the three anxious children. He gently tugged at his sleeve, which was still being held by Yue’er, and slowly walked over to the stone table beneath a leafy tree, where he settled down. \"Now, in the Immortal Realm, apart from your parents, there is no one else with the ability to ascend,\" he stated calmly. \"Your father, Xuanyuan Mo Ze, failed to ascend last time and barely escaped with his life, so it is impossible for him to ascend now. Therefore, the person who has arrived today, undergoing this tribulation, is undoubtedly your mother.\"","\"Then... then is our mother in danger? Will she be able to ascend safely?\" Muchen couldn’t help but ask, his voice tinged with youthful apprehension.","\"Master, will those who want to harm my parents take this opportunity to attack my mother?\" Hao’er pressed, his brow furrowed with worry. \"Is it dangerous for her to ascend now?\"","\"Master...\" Yue’er also called out hurriedly, her small voice full of urgency.","The Azure Emperor raised a hand, a quiet gesture to stop them from asking any more questions. He simply said, \"Those who want to harm her will naturally not let such a good opportunity slip by. Whether she can ascend smoothly depends entirely on your mother herself.\"","\"Master, please help our mother!\" Yue’er pleaded, her eyes wide and pitiful as she knelt before him.","\"Master.\"","\"Master!\"","Hao’er and Muchen followed suit, also kneeling down. Though they remained silent, their intentions were abundantly clear: they, too, were begging for his intervention.","\"Get up!\" the Azure Emperor commanded firmly. Looking at them, he explained, \"Kneeling before me is useless, because your mother’s path is different from others. What she has to do in the future will be even more difficult and dangerous than ascending today. If she cannot resolve this crisis and ascend smoothly today, how will she face her enemies in the future?\"","He paused, his gaze sweeping over each of them. Then, he continued slowly, \"Are you saying that in the future, when she encounters danger and problems she cannot solve, you will just kneel down and beg me to help her? You must know that everyone has their own mission, their own life they want to live, and their own difficulties to face. If you just rely on others for help, how long can they truly help you?\"","The three children listened to his words, stunned for a moment. Perhaps because they were still so young, they didn’t fully comprehend the profound implications of his message, but they vaguely understood what he meant. So, the three exchanged glances, paused for a moment in quiet contemplation, then bowed their heads and said in low, chastened voices, \"Master, we are ignorant.\"","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor nodded approvingly. \"Get up!\" he instructed.","The three responded and stood up, their youthful faces still a mixture of worry and burgeoning understanding.","\"Life and death are predestined, and calamities are determined by heaven. You don’t need to worry, as worrying is useless,\" the Azure Emperor said slowly, his voice carrying an ancient wisdom. \"She has begun her advancement today, but she won’t be able to ascend in just a day or two. Calm yourselves and go back to practicing your cultivation!\"","Hearing this, the three children moved their lips, wanting to protest or express their lingering fears, but in the end, they held their tongues. They simply responded with a quiet affirmation and left together, their steps heavy with unspoken concern.","Their mother was undergoing the fierce lightning tribulation; how could they possibly calm down and cultivate? But then again, what else could they do if they didn’t cultivate? They were still so young, too small to offer any meaningful help in this colossal trial.","\"Let’s go! Let’s go back and cultivate. We have to believe in Mother. She will definitely make it!\" Hao’er said, his voice firm as he held their hands tightly, instilling a sense of resolve.","\"Yes, Mother will definitely ascend safely. When that time comes, maybe we’ll be able to see her,\" Yue’er nodded, her little face serious with newfound determination.","\"Let’s go back and cultivate,\" Muchen agreed, and the three of them dutifully returned to their cave abode.","The Azure Emperor watched them leave, a subtle smile gracing his face. He then looked up at the turbulent sky and murmured slowly, \"I guess the sky is about to change significantly.\""]}]);
